WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.500
It’s the late 90's, and an Air Canada flight
experiences severe malfunctions while traveling

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.390
from London to Vancouver.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:12.310
The pilots are unable to do anything and the
plane crashes into the woods of Northern Alberta.

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:17.930
The crash was devastating - only 10 of the
nearly 300 people on board are alive.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:22.650
And even though they survived the initial
disaster, their battle for life has only just

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:23.650
begun.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.630
It’s late autumn in Northern Canada and
there’s no telling when help will arrive,

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:28.680
if at all.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:34.050
If the survivors want to make it through the
night they need to find shelter, and fast.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.910
As they trudge through the freezing woods,
the group finds a path that looks like it

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.109
might lead them to civilization.

00:00:40.109 --> 00:00:44.340
After all, if there was a path in the woods,
that meant they were probably in a national

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.280
park, and if they were in a national park,
there had to be a ranger's station around

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.920
somewhere where they could warm up and call
for help.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.840
They didn’t have many other options, so
they followed the path which opened up to

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:59.530
a clearing, but instead of finding a ranger's
station or campground, they found something

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:01.309
none of them could have expected.

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:04.860
It was a pond, but there was something off
about it.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:10.670
As they got closer they saw that this strange
pond wasn’t filled with water, but blood.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.420
The survivors were horrified.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.439
That couldn't really be blood, could it?

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:17.540
It must be a weird algae or a chemical reaction.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:21.700
But one member of the group, a man named Thomas
Dean, who had been on his way back to his

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:26.610
hometown of Prince George, British Columbia,
thought there was something strangely familiar

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:27.610
about this.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:32.420
He remembered being a boy and going to visit
family in Alberta, and hearing an urban legend

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.040
from the older local kids.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:38.790
According to the stories, somewhere out in
the wilderness, in the northern part of the

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:44.321
province, there was a pond full of human blood,
and what made it even worse, was that some

00:01:44.321 --> 00:01:47.010
said the pond was a gateway to hell.

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:51.790
The SCP Foundation was also aware of this
legend, and had been trying to pinpoint the

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:55.790
exact source of it for decades prior to the
Air Canada crash.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:02:00.259
They would finally receive definite confirmation
of the blood pond when Foundation personnel

00:02:00.259 --> 00:02:05.570
intercepted a radio transmission from a ranger's
station located within the Wood Buffalo National

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:06.570
Park.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:10.720
It was the survivors of the crash, who had
managed to make it through the night, and

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.720
they were about to be escorted out of the
park by rangers.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.740
The Foundation mobilized quickly to cordon
off the pond, as at this time they were unsure

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.760
of what potentially harmful properties the
pond might have had.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:26.080
They set up Watch Station Epsilon-38 and put
staff on guard to deter travellers from the

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.080
area.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:32.099
The pond was given the designation of SCP-354
and classed as Euclid.

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:36.960
Foundation scientists made a number of interesting
discoveries about SCP-354 when they collected

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.530
samples for testing.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:44.080
First, the pond was not in fact full of blood,
merely an inorganic liquid that closely resembles

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.450
blood in color and consistently.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:51.409
Second, and even stranger than the red liquid,
is that the pond doesn't seem to have definite

00:02:51.409 --> 00:02:52.970
banks or a bottom.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:57.480
Instead, the liquid in the pond increases
in density as the radius away from the center

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:02.940
increases - the liquid congeals at the edges,
becoming more solid and blending into the

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:03.940
surrounding soil.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:08.800
It also becomes thicker as one descends deeper
into the pool, and a bottom of the pond has

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.970
not yet been reached, if it even exists.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:15.299
Initially, the foundation found no signs of
life within the blood pond.

00:03:15.299 --> 00:03:20.930
But that would all change at 2:03 PM on the
day following the opening of Watch Station

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:25.680
Epsilon-38, when the science team noticed
an unusual level of activity on the pond's

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.680
surface.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.879
Security footage feeds showed a shape rising
up out of the pond, followed by a deafening

00:03:30.879 --> 00:03:31.879
shriek.

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:35.930
After that, the feed was cut and Foundation
lost all communication with Watch Station

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:36.930
Epsilon-38.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:40.580
Fearing the worst, a Mobile Task Force was
dispatched to the location.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:44.799
When they got there, all personnel at the
watch station had been killed by what could

00:03:44.799 --> 00:03:47.590
only be described as a gigantic bat.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:52.200
The task force was able to neutralize the
entity, and as soon as they could, the Foundation

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:58.140
moved in to increase security around the SCP,
creating Area - 354 and installing a permanent

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.750
security detail.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:04.849
After this point, the pond started to regularly
spit out a variety of monstrous entities,

00:04:04.849 --> 00:04:09.340
almost as if it was reacting to the SCP Foundation's
increased security measures.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:14.410
After SCP-354-1, the giant bat came SCP-354-2.

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:20.190
354-2 was an echidna-like monster the size
of a bear, that was virtually bulletproof

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.009
but unable to escape Area 354.

00:04:23.009 --> 00:04:26.590
The foundation neutralized this anomaly with
napalm.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:32.630
SCP-354-3 was a floating black sphere capable
of firing deadly beams of concentrated energy.

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:36.360
The area's head scientist was able to hit
it with a sledgehammer, causing the sphere

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:40.389
to malfunction and self-destruct before it
was able to escape the area.

00:04:40.389 --> 00:04:44.780
The Foundation wasn't as lucky with SCP-354-4.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:49.539
This creature was a reptilian humanoid that
stood roughly 15 feet tall and was unable

00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:51.699
to be put down with gunfire.

00:04:51.699 --> 00:04:55.919
This was the first creature from the pond
to successfully escape containment, and was

00:04:55.919 --> 00:05:01.050
only able to be neutralized when the Foundation
sent in Mobile Task Force Omega 7, also known

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.139
as “Pandora's Box.”

00:05:03.139 --> 00:05:08.560
The data on pond incursions is partially corrupted,
so a complete list of creatures is not available,

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:12.630
but some of the other monsters that came out
of the blood pond included a killer robot,

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:17.330
a set of gigantic tentacles that dragged several
D-class personnel into the pond, a pair of

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:21.740
panther-like creatures - one made of ice and
the other of magma - that ignored foundation

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:27.150
staff and instead fought each other, and one
seemingly normal human man who was executed

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.789
as soon as he emerged from the pond.

00:05:29.789 --> 00:05:34.259
Tests on his body revealed that he was, in
fact, totally normal and would have posed

00:05:34.259 --> 00:05:35.440
no threat.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:39.780
These anomalies came out of the pond at fairly
regular intervals for several months, before

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:43.780
the pond went silent for an unprecedented
22 months.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:47.650
The head scientist at the time noted, “I
suspect this means one of two things.

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:51.730
Either the Red Pool has ‘died’ or ‘powered
down’ or whatever the correct term for it

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:55.460
is; or it is ‘charging up’ for something
big to come through.

00:05:55.460 --> 00:06:00.229
O5 believes the former is the most likely
explanation, and has recalled 30% of our total

00:06:00.229 --> 00:06:02.520
personnel and cut 25% of our funding.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:08.021
While I can only hope that they are correct,
if the latter situation is true, we're soon

00:06:08.021 --> 00:06:12.669
to face some terrible monstrosity and we won't
have anywhere near the force necessary to

00:06:12.669 --> 00:06:13.669
deal with it.

00:06:13.669 --> 00:06:15.819
I worry for all of our safety.”

00:06:15.819 --> 00:06:21.840
His words would prove eerily prophetic following
the events of Exploratory Mission 354 Alpha.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:25.500
The Foundation's research and development
team built a specialized craft to explore

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.600
the pond.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:30.569
Because of the strange properties of the pond's
density, the craft was essentially made to

00:06:30.569 --> 00:06:35.120
be both a submarine, for parts of the pond
where the contents were liquid, and a drill,

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:38.759
for when the liquid congealed into a semi-solid
towards the bottom.

00:06:38.759 --> 00:06:45.300
The exploration team consisted of Agent Swanson,
Agent Turquoise, Agent 86, Dr. Jay Macarthur,

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.760
Chris Simmons, Leroy Tucker, and a pilot named
Marty.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:52.400
With the team assembled, the ship was sent
down into the pond.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:56.830
Nothing eventful happened for the first two
days of the mission, but at 4:30 AM on the

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:00.759
third day, gravity suddenly reversed for the
crew of the ship.

00:07:00.759 --> 00:07:04.370
This seemed to indicate that they were approaching
the halfway point, though what would be on

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:06.960
the other side, nobody could say.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:11.290
On the fourth day, the ship surfaced, proving
definitely that the pond was in fact some

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:12.449
sort of portal.

00:07:12.449 --> 00:07:15.960
The crew looked out of the portholes to see
the darkness of night above them.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:20.160
While sensors outside the ship detected nothing
harmful in the atmosphere around them, the

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.080
crew were wary of exiting the craft.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.970
The other side of the pond was nothing like
the world the crew knew.

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:31.789
For one thing, the night lasted for 28 hours
before dawn came, and when the sun finally

00:07:31.789 --> 00:07:35.729
rose, it was much larger and redder than the
earth's sun.

00:07:35.729 --> 00:07:40.030
Under the light of that strange, red star,
the crew could see that the pond on this side

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:44.910
was massive compared to where they'd come
in - more like a large lake.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:48.680
Surrounding the lake was sand and rocks that
were covered in a kind of moss that disappeared

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:51.550
under sunlight and regrew during the night.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:54.379
The team left the ship and started to explore.

00:07:54.379 --> 00:07:58.680
During their time in this strange world, they
found that the day lasted just a few hours

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:03.470
shorter than the night, meaning that whatever
planet they were on had roughly a 43-hour-long

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:06.629
rotation as opposed to our own planet's 24.

00:08:06.629 --> 00:08:10.699
The team found a number of anomalous elements
on their expedition, including razor-sharp

00:08:10.699 --> 00:08:14.530
grass that can puncture skin and streams of
liquid carbon dioxide.

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:19.270
They heard some loud roars in the distance
once or twice, but other than that the planet

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:23.420
was eerily silent, with seemingly no animal
life and not even wind.

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:28.889
When it rained, the soil remained dry, and
based on that, the scientists theorized plants

00:08:28.889 --> 00:08:31.680
in this world were more efficient at absorbing
moisture.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:36.950
On the 25th day, the team ran into a huge
metal wall that appeared to be artificially

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:37.950
constructed.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:42.690
Luckily, Leroy Tucker, a quick-thinking researcher,
was able to rig a blowtorch from camping supplies

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:44.550
and melt a hole through the metal.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:49.500
On the other side, there was finally wind,
and odd black grass.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.801
That's the extent of what is known about the
other side of the wall, though, because the

00:08:52.801 --> 00:08:56.920
expedition logs are heavily corrupted after
that point, but we know that whatever was

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:00.430
in there wasn't good, because the team never
returned.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:04.530
Strangely, there's no record of any of the
names mentioned in the ship's log - almost

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:08.529
as if being killed on the other side completely
erased them from history.

00:09:08.529 --> 00:09:11.740
No other expeditions into the pond were launched
after that.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:15.950
On an undisclosed date, a year following the
discovery of the blood pond and construction

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:21.950
of Area 354, the site was completely evacuated,
and the power was cut to the area.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:26.120
Mobile Task Force Theta-12 was dispatched
to investigate the cause of the evacuation,

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:31.580
but before contact could be established, the
area's on-site nuclear warhead was detonated,

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.940
completely destroying the site.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:37.950
MTF Theta 12 was then attacked by a convoy
made up of D-class and other low-ranking staff

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:40.020
who had evacuated Area 354.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:44.520
It was apparent that there had been some kind
of mutiny within the site, and that a dissolution

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:48.380
of the chain of command had led to its evacuation
and destruction.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:53.750
The convoy totally annihilated MTF Theta 12,
and no further contact with the former personnel

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:57.180
of Area-354 has been made since.

00:09:57.180 --> 00:10:01.610
Following the site's detonation, a new site
was constructed, called simply the Red Pool

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:03.100
Containment Site.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:07.380
Unlike the previous facility, which focused
on research and neutralization, the new site

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:09.990
is entirely concerned with containment.

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:14.240
The shift in directive came as a response
to the pond's apparent reactive nature - each

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:18.980
creature that emerged from the pond seemed
to be in retaliation to the Foundation's actions,

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:23.460
and it was theorized by some that the mutiny
at Area 354 was triggered by some kind of

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:26.200
psychic attack from the pond itself.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:31.180
An interview in the SCP file on 354 reveals
that there was one more disastrous attempt

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:34.170
to control and understand the blood pond.

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:38.060
According to an interview with a Foundation
agent, the head doctor proposed a scheme to

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:41.620
drain the blood pond using a system of pumps
and hoses.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:46.250
All non-essential personnel were evacuated
in case of emergency, leaving only the pump

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:50.180
technicians, D-class personnel, and a few
agents for security.

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:54.990
However, as soon as the pump was scheduled
to be turned on, everyone at the site experienced

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:57.240
a mass dissociative episode.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:02.130
The agent described the feeling they all experienced
as like being in a dream and suddenly realizing

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.130
that you're asleep.

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:05.600
He said “Everything stopped being real.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.860
It was like we had to escape right now.”

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:12.270
When asked what happened when the pump was
turned on, he simply explained that it “wouldn't

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.270
let them”.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:17.000
This interview confirmed the theory that the
pond is not only capable of releasing monsters

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:22.910
out into our world, but also that it's capable
of powerful but much more subtle, psychological

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:23.910
attacks.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:29.110
This suggests a chilling possibility - that
the pond isn't just blindly reacting to being

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:34.459
attacked, but it's fully sentient, and the
actions of the SCP foundation have only served

00:11:34.459 --> 00:11:35.740
to annoy it.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:40.220
And worse, studies of the pond's banks have
provided evidence that the area of congealed

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:44.640
liquid around the perimeter of the pond has
been steadily expanding.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:47.640
That's right - the pond is getting bigger.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:51.630
The last thing the Foundation agent stationed
at the site said before being dragged out

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:56.860
of the interview and sedated was “It gets
bigger and stronger every day, and now we've

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.620
made it angry!”

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:05.070
One of the primary aims of the SCP foundation
is to contain the anomalies that they discover.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:09.060
Secure, Contain, Protect is their mission
statement, after all.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:15.230
However, there are some forces so unknowable
and malevolent that there is no way to truly

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:17.510
contain them.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:21.240
SCP-4205 is one such force.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:27.320
Very little is known about SCP-4205, even
compared to other SCPs, many of which are

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:29.430
mysterious by their very nature.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:34.990
We do not know what it is, we do not know
what it wants, and we do not have any meaningful

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:36.660
way to stop it.

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:41.630
The best that can be done to protect yourself
from it is to implement the few known preventative

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:47.110
measures available, and pray that it doesn’t
set its sights on you.

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:53.260
The little information that exists on SCP-4205
was recorded by Wade Dalitz, a former junior

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:55.100
researcher at the Foundation.

00:12:55.100 --> 00:13:00.901
He wrote the initial report on SCP-4205 on
a computer, Terminal 4, which was linked to

00:13:00.901 --> 00:13:01.901
his brain and consciousness as he wrote.

00:13:01.901 --> 00:13:04.880
Though his work was highly valuable, and provided
many previously unknown insights about the

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:08.980
nature of the SCP, sadly his knowledge could
not save him.

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:17.600
The official entry on SCP-4205 was his final
act before his death on December 11, 1992.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:21.860
Before we get deeper into that entry, and
Wade’s final day on earth, it’s important

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:24.850
to understand what SCP-4205 is.

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:29.620
Or, at least, understand the little we know
about what it is.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:35.740
4205 is a Keter class SCP, meaning that it’s
incredibly difficult or complicated to contain.

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:39.260
It also shows extreme hostility toward all
life.

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:43.720
It is described as an amber-colored pair of
human-like eyes, with the ability to appear

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:49.370
spontaneously in windows, mirrors, or any
other glass or glass-like surface.

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:53.950
One of the reasons so little is known about
these eyes, is that anyone who sees them dies

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:54.950
within seconds.

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:55.950
The effect is nearly instantaneous.

00:13:55.950 --> 00:14:02.920
Much like the mythical basilisk, the gaze
of SCP-4205 is deadly and inescapable.

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:08.730
The eyes only seem to appear to people who
are alone in a room, and never in places where

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:11.360
there’s more than one person.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:16.220
But aside from that, there is no way to predict
where the eyes will appear.

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:20.790
Since it is unknown if the eyes are part of
a corporeal body, or even present on this

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:26.040
plane of reality, there is no way to contain
them or stop them from killing.

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:30.710
This brings us back to that fateful day, December
11, 1992.

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:35.860
The day that the SCP Foundation would finally
be given some tangible information on the

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:41.300
mysterious amber eyes, at the cost of one
of their researcher’s lives.

00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:45.800
Wade Dalitz, a young man fresh out of his
university studies, was brought onboard as

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:50.200
a Junior Researcher by Dr. Mark Forsyth, a
Senior Researcher.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:54.730
Dr. Forsyth recruited Wade after giving a
guest lecture at his university and being

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:59.990
impressed by Wade’s keen observational skills,
thirst for knowledge of the unexplained, and

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:04.390
determination to understand that which seemed
to defy explanation.

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:08.709
After Wade graduated, he was recruited by
Dr. Forsyth, and given the position of Junior

00:15:08.709 --> 00:15:10.680
Researcher at the SCP Foundation.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:16.139
where he assisted Dr. Forsyth, now a site
supervisor, in his research.

00:15:16.139 --> 00:15:20.730
After several months of working under Dr.
Forsyth with minimal responsibilities, Wade

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:28.450
was finally given the opportunity to write
his first SCP report... on SCP-4205.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:33.750
Following some initial documented appearances
of 4205, Dr. Forsyth approved further research

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:38.820
into the anomaly, with Wade appointed as the
lead researcher on the subject.

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:44.010
According to Wade’s entry, he was responsible
for the discovery of SCP-4205 when he spotted

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:45.490
the anomaly in a window.

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:50.000
Though later reviews of security footage determined
that he was not the first person to observe

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:55.529
the eyes, he did claim to be the first to
observe them and live to tell the tale.

00:15:55.529 --> 00:15:59.600
In his writing on the subject, Wade is puzzled
by the fact that he survived his encounter

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:04.940
with SCP-4205, and wonders what could have
set him apart from the others that fell victim

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:06.399
to its gaze.

00:16:06.399 --> 00:16:12.970
He found himself frustrated as he documented
SCP-4205, his rough drafts of reports dissolving

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:15.980
into angry rants about his own incompetence.

00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:21.570
Wade had difficulty adjusting to his new responsibilities,
especially with the added element of his assigned

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:24.149
subject’s mysterious and volatile nature.

00:16:24.149 --> 00:16:30.269
In between his reports on SCP-4205, its previous
appearances, and its effects on its victims,

00:16:30.269 --> 00:16:34.680
he wrote letters to his father, desperate
for reassurance that he was not messing everything

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:35.680
up.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:38.100
Letters that would sadly go unsent.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:44.100
In his coverage of SCP-4205, Wade made note
of a troubling recurring element in each victim’s

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.100
death.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:48.399
When medical professionals attempted to revive
the victims, it was always noted that their

00:16:48.399 --> 00:16:53.480
brain activity stopped much more quickly than
in cases of death by natural causes.

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:58.050
When examined, all aspects of the body aside
from the brain were completely unharmed.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:03.130
The brain, however, showed massive nerve damage
in the amygdala, hippocampus, medial temporal

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:04.730
lobe, and occipital lobe.

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:08.640
The appearance of this brain trauma has been
compared to the effects of electrical shock

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:09.640
or a severe head injury.

00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:16.559
In addition to Wade, six other people on record
encountered SCP-4205.

00:17:16.559 --> 00:17:21.470
Every encounter ended the same way, with sudden
brain death and severe nerve damage immediately

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.490
after viewing the eyes in a reflective surface.

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:29.340
The first encounter occurred on January 5,
1990, when Deputy Liaison Gena viewed the

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:32.340
eyes in a reflective glass one-way window.

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:35.870
Security tape reveals that the eyes appeared
in the window eight minutes before the Deputy

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.990
Liaison spotted them.

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:42.120
As soon as he did, he fell from his chair
and immediately died.

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:46.290
Though the specifics varied from case to case,
the end result of every encounter was the

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:50.450
same, with none surviving long enough to relate
what they experienced.

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:52.860
Every encounter except Wade’s.

00:17:52.860 --> 00:18:00.620
As he continued his documentation of SCP-4205,
Wade’s mental state quickly began to deteriorate.

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:05.580
The process of his mind coming apart, and
his thoughts giving way to confusion, fear,

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:09.660
and anger at his own survival, is documented
in his reports on the SCP.

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:16.750
He agonized over the question of why he was
able to survive gazing into the eyes of SCP-4205

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:19.490
when so many others had not?

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:24.360
The question consumed him until he was unable
to eat, sleep, or do anything but obsess over

00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:27.130
the SCP he was tasked with researching.

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:32.200
As he became more agitated, he began to write
about the eyes appearing to him again.

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:36.390
On one occurrence, he attempted to touch them,
and described the sensation like touching

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:40.460
a balloon to your arm after it has been charged
with static electricity.

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:43.050
He continued to report seeing the eyes.

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:48.240
The worst was when trying to sleep, during
which he was overtaken by violent sleep paralysis

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:51.280
and plagued with visions of the amber eyes.

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:54.820
The only comfort Wade seemed to find was in
memories of his loved ones.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:59.680
He wrote about his mother and his father,
even as their memories grew foggier to him.

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:04.240
He also mentioned a man by the name of Theodore
Quale, who he claimed was a researcher at

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.450
the Foundation.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:09.250
Later fact checking determined that this was
not the case, and that Quale must have been

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:10.600
someone from Wade’s past.

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:16.010
He wrote about Quale wistfully, mournfully,
with words of love and loss, tormented by

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:21.180
the sense that he was losing his grip on reality
and everything he once held dear.

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:26.179
As Wade descended deeper into a hell inside
his own mind, he continued to mull over the

00:19:26.179 --> 00:19:29.260
questions of SCP-4205.

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:30.990
Was there more to it than what was visible?

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:32.970
Did it have a body?

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:35.320
Why had he survived his encounter with it?

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.679
And what did it want from him?

00:19:36.679 --> 00:19:40.350
He decided that those who had perished immediately
were the lucky ones.

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:44.110
They had escaped the torture that had overtaken
his life.

00:19:44.110 --> 00:19:48.429
The eyes were everywhere now, watching him
even as he attempted to unlock their secrets

00:19:48.429 --> 00:19:49.880
on a Foundation computer.

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:54.240
He spoke to the eyes at one point, but refused
to write down what they had said to him.

00:19:54.240 --> 00:20:00.250
His last entry, his last thought, was a plea
for Theodore Quale’s embrace.

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:05.430
There is no more written about the research,
or about the eyes, only a simple, desperate

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:08.600
need for a comfort that is long lost.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:12.280
Now is the part of our story where terror
meets tragedy.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:17.040
Contrary to what Wade thought, and what was
recorded in his final computer entries, he

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:20.620
did not survive his brief brush with SCP-4205.

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:25.320
The truth is that he spotted the amber eyes
in the glass above his terminal monitor while

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:28.320
recording the entry, and died seconds later.

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:34.170
Though his death was swift, it felt agonizingly
slow, as revealed by his descent into panic

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.890
and paranoia recorded in his writings.

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:41.580
The entries recorded as a result of the connection
Wade and the computer, his physical contact

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:47.820
with it at the moment of exposure to SCP-4205’s
anomalous effects allowing the terminal to

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:53.490
archive his final thoughts before he succumbed
to the deadly nature of the eyes.

00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:58.540
The entries were never physically typed, but
rather jumped from his dying mind into the

00:20:58.540 --> 00:20:59.540
mainframe.

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:05.970
His entries, the echoes of a dying mind, offer
a glimpse into the way that SCP-4205 kills

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:07.150
its victims.

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:11.860
In the seconds leading up to death, the amber
eyes fast-forward a person’s mind, feeding

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:16.429
on the electrical impulses that it gives off
as it speeds through what seem to be days

00:21:16.429 --> 00:21:19.020
of fear and of a loosening grip on reality.

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:24.100
The death may be swift, but the suffering
is long.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:29.289
Wade left the foundation with a digital fingerprint,
an echo of the person he was at his core in

00:21:29.289 --> 00:21:34.370
addition to his experiences with SCP-4205
itself.

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:39.340
Wade spent his final moments terrified for
his life, dreaming of a father that he missed

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:42.440
and a long-lost love from his college days.

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:45.870
His sacrifice must not be forgotten.

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:51.800
Because no one ever survives an encounter
with SCP-4205, his documented final moments

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:54.799
are the only first-hand account in existence.

00:21:54.799 --> 00:21:57.929
Junior Researcher Wade Dalitz gave us a gift
in death.

00:21:57.929 --> 00:22:05.030
He allowed the SCP Foundation a glimpse into
the true horror of the amber eyes, and a reminder

00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:08.460
of what they are capable of stealing from
us.

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:14.679
So be careful of windows, mirrors, screens,
and all reflective surfaces.

00:22:14.679 --> 00:22:20.039
When you look into them, you never know what
you might see looking back.

00:22:20.039 --> 00:22:26.150
The year is 1941, and the world is gripped
by the most violent and widespread war in

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:27.650
history.

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:32.260
Millions march to war as bloody battles are
fought across the globe, horrendous atrocities

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:37.500
are carried out on groups of people, and parts
of London are bombed to rubble on a weekly

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:38.500
basis.

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:42.520
Considering it’s only been twenty years
since the last world war, it must seem to

00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:48.000
the residents of the early 20th century that
the world is coming apart at the seams.

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:52.440
And amongst all this chaos, it’d be easy
not to notice a secluded manor house in the

00:22:52.440 --> 00:22:58.140
English countryside disappearing without a
trace for eleven days, before suddenly returning

00:22:58.140 --> 00:22:59.740
to our reality.

00:22:59.740 --> 00:23:05.520
But thankfully, one organization makes it
its sole duty to notice the unnoticeable and

00:23:05.520 --> 00:23:09.880
understand the impossible - The SCP Foundation.

00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:15.080
And within that anomalous manor house, Foundation
agents and researchers were about to find

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:19.160
horrors beyond even their darkest imaginations.

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:25.140
This is the grim tale of SCP - 1461, better
known as…

00:23:25.140 --> 00:23:27.230
The House of the Worm.

00:23:27.230 --> 00:23:31.760
When the manor house reappeared after its
eleven day absence, the Foundation zeroed

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:34.460
in, sending agents inside to investigate.

00:23:34.460 --> 00:23:39.890
It was a two-level dwelling complete with
twelve bedrooms, four baths, three studies,

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:45.320
a main foyer slash ballroom, a library, a
kitchen, and a pantry-basement.

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:50.299
The Foundation observed that a number of these
rooms had been fitted with rows of bunk beds,

00:23:50.299 --> 00:23:52.669
similar to a boarding house or barracks.

00:23:52.669 --> 00:23:55.250
Only later would they understand why.

00:23:55.250 --> 00:24:00.100
They found that the upper portion of the home
exhibited no abnormal qualities whatsoever,

00:24:00.100 --> 00:24:05.169
but as the agents investigated further, they
found an entrance to the truly anomalous portion

00:24:05.169 --> 00:24:08.780
of the manor - The extensive sub-level system.

00:24:08.780 --> 00:24:12.630
No previous records of the building kept by
the local council indicated that there would

00:24:12.630 --> 00:24:17.720
be anything below the manor’s basement - so
either the mysterious previous occupants,

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:22.789
who were nowhere to be found, had built this
sub-level, or it’d just appeared here on

00:24:22.789 --> 00:24:23.789
its own.

00:24:23.789 --> 00:24:28.410
Regardless of which was the case, agents and
researchers knew that whatever had happened

00:24:28.410 --> 00:24:33.080
down here had everything to do with the manor’s
mysterious disappearance.

00:24:33.080 --> 00:24:38.929
They descended into the depths of what seemed
like a man-made cave system, constructed primarily

00:24:38.929 --> 00:24:41.940
from a mix of concrete, iron, and brass.

00:24:41.940 --> 00:24:48.169
It was a behemoth of 20th century technology
- intricate, snaking systems of pipes, gears,

00:24:48.169 --> 00:24:49.630
and pumping pistons.

00:24:49.630 --> 00:24:53.960
It was like someone had built an entire factory
down here - but for what?

00:24:53.960 --> 00:24:58.309
The agents began to spread out through the
labyrinthine bowels of the manor, hoping to

00:24:58.309 --> 00:25:03.830
find some answers, but all they seemed to
discover was more questions.

00:25:03.830 --> 00:25:07.090
This place hadn’t been built with any form
of comprehensible logic.

00:25:07.090 --> 00:25:13.049
It was full of dead ends, stairways that ascended
and descended to nowhere, doors that would

00:25:13.049 --> 00:25:16.710
open to reveal just walls behind them or not
open at all.

00:25:16.710 --> 00:25:19.170
It was like a maze built by a maniac.

00:25:19.170 --> 00:25:23.380
It didn’t help that it looked like the place
was recently hit by an earthquake with some

00:25:23.380 --> 00:25:27.130
passages caved in and mangled machinery strewn
about.

00:25:27.130 --> 00:25:32.010
It seemed that no human workers had interfered
with the impossibly complex and bizarre machinery

00:25:32.010 --> 00:25:33.480
in quite some time.

00:25:33.480 --> 00:25:37.970
A number of the materials used to construct
said machinery, as well as the gray sandstone

00:25:37.970 --> 00:25:42.700
filling in the collapsed passageways, remain
unidentified to this day.

00:25:42.700 --> 00:25:47.330
Already, the sub-level was proving to be a
complex puzzle box with only an estimated

00:25:47.330 --> 00:25:51.809
75% of its layout ultimately being mapped
by Foundation researchers.

00:25:51.809 --> 00:25:57.210
However, they would soon realize that this
place wasn’t just confusing - it was deadly.

00:25:57.210 --> 00:26:01.240
The only method of self-maintenance detected
by the exploring agents were pipes that would

00:26:01.240 --> 00:26:05.260
fire a thick, black lubricant onto the surrounding
machinery.

00:26:05.260 --> 00:26:08.990
One of the Foundation agents had the misfortune
of getting covered in it while exploring a

00:26:08.990 --> 00:26:13.640
darkened passageway, and eighty percent of
his body was melted as a result.

00:26:13.640 --> 00:26:19.320
It appeared that the viscous, black goo was
incredibly corrosive to all organic matter.

00:26:19.320 --> 00:26:25.110
A number of the machines also emitted dangerously
high quantities of gamma and X-ray radiation,

00:26:25.110 --> 00:26:29.300
making it difficult to explore many of the
caverns without heavy hazmat protection.

00:26:29.300 --> 00:26:34.470
And worst of all, were the extremely hostile
creatures living in the caves who would regularly

00:26:34.470 --> 00:26:36.800
attack Foundation personnel.

00:26:36.800 --> 00:26:43.660
These abominations came to be known as SCP
- 1461 - 1, vicious, steampunk Frankenstein

00:26:43.660 --> 00:26:49.600
monsters - once human, but with large parts
of their bodies replaced by crude, mechanical

00:26:49.600 --> 00:26:53.250
implants - including metal teeth and claws.

00:26:53.250 --> 00:26:58.480
1461-1’s have displayed a taste for human
flesh, and they have dragged multiple Foundation

00:26:58.480 --> 00:27:02.990
agents down into their lair to be “converted”
into monsters like them.

00:27:02.990 --> 00:27:07.930
It’s believed that SCP-1461 is capable of
controlling these beasts through the strategic

00:27:07.930 --> 00:27:13.240
use of sound from its brass speaking pipes,
leading them into areas where Foundation personnel

00:27:13.240 --> 00:27:16.130
are present to instigate conflict.

00:27:16.130 --> 00:27:20.210
Many of these pitiful creatures have had their
throats replaced by phonographs, endlessly

00:27:20.210 --> 00:27:24.270
repeating the same nonsense phrases over and
over again:

00:27:24.270 --> 00:27:26.270
“I am what you have made me.

00:27:26.270 --> 00:27:28.210
I am choice and I am tyranny.

00:27:28.210 --> 00:27:29.210
Forgive me.

00:27:29.210 --> 00:27:31.419
I am then and I am now.

00:27:31.419 --> 00:27:33.250
What gods they will be, then.

00:27:33.250 --> 00:27:35.039
I am evil and I am flesh.

00:27:35.039 --> 00:27:36.039
I am the trap.

00:27:36.039 --> 00:27:37.039
I am the trapped.

00:27:37.039 --> 00:27:39.520
I am beauty and I am chaos.

00:27:39.520 --> 00:27:40.940
Children are selfish.

00:27:40.940 --> 00:27:42.570
I am the worm.

00:27:42.570 --> 00:27:44.350
I have broken God.”

00:27:44.350 --> 00:27:50.799
Still, in spite of mazes, monsters, and deadly
chemicals, the agents persisted, and managed

00:27:50.799 --> 00:27:53.559
to discover several important locations.

00:27:53.559 --> 00:27:58.640
The Gel Production chamber on Sub-Level 3
creates glass jars from the unidentified sandstone,

00:27:58.640 --> 00:28:02.899
and fills them with a slime that looks to
contain living eyes and teeth.

00:28:02.899 --> 00:28:07.610
The Factory Deliveries room is filled with
a huge number of crates and boxes, which seem

00:28:07.610 --> 00:28:11.390
to shift and change in number between Foundation
patrols.

00:28:11.390 --> 00:28:16.220
The Speaking Tube Room on Sub-Level Eleven
contains a grand pulpit that acts as the connecting

00:28:16.220 --> 00:28:21.630
point for the complex array of speaking tubes
running through the entire cave system.

00:28:21.630 --> 00:28:27.549
The body parts of a deceased female also appear
to be wired into the machinery, like spare

00:28:27.549 --> 00:28:28.549
parts.

00:28:28.549 --> 00:28:32.590
And on Sub-Level Twelve, they found the so-called
Catalyst Room.

00:28:32.590 --> 00:28:37.850
Here, they discovered a huge, complicated,
clockwork and steam-powered machine that appeared

00:28:37.850 --> 00:28:41.000
to be broken and missing some parts.

00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:46.169
Most horrifying of all though, is the raised
platform in the center of the Catalyst Room

00:28:46.169 --> 00:28:49.070
on top of which is a metal hospital bed.

00:28:49.070 --> 00:28:54.610
A desiccated male corpse rests upon this bed,
its chest punctured by large syringes connected

00:28:54.610 --> 00:28:57.540
by tubes to some kind of pumping machine.

00:28:57.540 --> 00:29:01.270
The parts connecting this pumping machine
to the overall apparatus of the room were

00:29:01.270 --> 00:29:04.929
missing though, leaving its purpose a mystery.

00:29:04.929 --> 00:29:10.260
The Foundation assumed that fluids used to
be drawn out of this corpse to somehow power

00:29:10.260 --> 00:29:11.270
the machine.

00:29:11.270 --> 00:29:15.440
You may be starting to worry that there don’t
seem to be any answers here, that this house

00:29:15.440 --> 00:29:20.429
is one big mystery - but lucky for you, you’re
wrong.

00:29:20.429 --> 00:29:24.720
An old journal was also discovered in the
Catalyst Room, and if what is written inside

00:29:24.720 --> 00:29:29.660
is to be believed, then we may finally have
some truth about who created the House of

00:29:29.660 --> 00:29:35.179
the Worm, why it was created, and what horrible
events triggered its mysterious disappearance

00:29:35.179 --> 00:29:36.740
and reappearance.

00:29:36.740 --> 00:29:41.070
His true name has been redacted by the Foundation
and special efforts have been made to maintain

00:29:41.070 --> 00:29:45.840
secrecy around the House, seeing as it’s
an anomaly of great interest to a cult known

00:29:45.840 --> 00:29:51.400
as the Church of the Broken God, so we’ll
just call the one who made this place “The

00:29:51.400 --> 00:29:52.450
Inventor.”

00:29:52.450 --> 00:29:56.900
Before any of this, the Inventor was one of
the many Englishmen traumatized and almost

00:29:56.900 --> 00:30:00.620
killed in the horrific trench battles of World
War One.

00:30:00.620 --> 00:30:05.630
After a near death experience, the Inventor,
like many geniuses and madmen, was plagued

00:30:05.630 --> 00:30:07.980
by surreal and nightmarish visions.

00:30:07.980 --> 00:30:14.170
He saw a huge creature that he referred to
as “The Worm” - a gigantic, metal monstrosity

00:30:14.170 --> 00:30:19.510
with dragon-like jaws full of gnashing gears
that rampaged through Europe, destroying and

00:30:19.510 --> 00:30:22.430
devouring everything in its path.

00:30:22.430 --> 00:30:27.381
These apocalyptic visions also presented him
with a solution, vague blueprints for a machine

00:30:27.381 --> 00:30:32.899
that might be the salvation of him and any
others willing to take his new gospel to heart.

00:30:32.899 --> 00:30:37.330
An escape from a world that the Inventor knew
in his heart was about to end.

00:30:37.330 --> 00:30:41.880
He hired work-starved labourers from across
the country to help him make his visions a

00:30:41.880 --> 00:30:47.960
reality and began a massive, secret construction
project beneath his isolated country manor

00:30:47.960 --> 00:30:48.990
house.

00:30:48.990 --> 00:30:51.760
For The Inventor, it was all a labour of love.

00:30:51.760 --> 00:30:57.500
He wanted to protect his wife, son, and daughter
from the terrible jaws of the Worm.

00:30:57.500 --> 00:31:02.639
But as the project stretched on, his wife
began to suspect that he’d lost his mind.

00:31:02.639 --> 00:31:05.340
Many of his workers, however, felt just the
opposite.

00:31:05.340 --> 00:31:09.780
They became infatuated by the Inventor’s
sermons on the nature of the Worm and the

00:31:09.780 --> 00:31:12.280
coming apocalypse they hoped to escape.

00:31:12.280 --> 00:31:17.309
Soon enough, they had become a bonafide cult,
constructing the elaborate sublevels underneath

00:31:17.309 --> 00:31:21.240
the house in preparation for the fast approaching
day of reckoning.

00:31:21.240 --> 00:31:23.610
Then came World War Two.

00:31:23.610 --> 00:31:28.669
The Inventor saw Hitler, hungry for war, as
one of the avatars of the Worm.

00:31:28.669 --> 00:31:33.740
Finally, knowing the time was right, he activated
the machine, and successfully trapped the

00:31:33.740 --> 00:31:36.220
Worm in the bowels of his mechanized home.

00:31:36.220 --> 00:31:40.559
However, as the Blitz raged and London’s
bombing began, the Inventor felt as though

00:31:40.559 --> 00:31:42.740
he hadn’t stopped anything.

00:31:42.740 --> 00:31:48.000
He realized once and for all that he was never
meant to stop the apocalypse, only escape

00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:49.000
it.

00:31:49.000 --> 00:31:52.850
And by throwing the final switch and setting
the machine he and his followers had built

00:31:52.850 --> 00:31:56.880
into overdrive, he did just that.

00:31:56.880 --> 00:32:01.780
This was the moment the House of the Worm
disappeared, transporting the Inventor, his

00:32:01.780 --> 00:32:04.880
family, and his devoted staff to a different
world.

00:32:04.880 --> 00:32:11.100
An empty grey world, devoid of war, but also
lacking all the comforts of regular life,

00:32:11.100 --> 00:32:12.320
including food.

00:32:12.320 --> 00:32:16.929
Things went downhill from there, as their
supplies quickly began to run out, and the

00:32:16.929 --> 00:32:20.330
cult descended into cannibalism in order to
survive.

00:32:20.330 --> 00:32:23.370
Things weren’t going much better in the
Inventor’s personal life.

00:32:23.370 --> 00:32:28.070
His wife, fearing what would happen to the
family, took her own life and the life of

00:32:28.070 --> 00:32:29.070
his daughter.

00:32:29.070 --> 00:32:33.620
Though by this point, the Inventor’s mind
was so fractured that it’s possible he may

00:32:33.620 --> 00:32:35.090
have killed them himself.

00:32:35.090 --> 00:32:40.919
Either way, it was only the Inventor and his
son left, and more trouble was brewing.

00:32:40.919 --> 00:32:46.179
Eudora, one of the staff trapped in the building
with the Inventor and his cult, started a

00:32:46.179 --> 00:32:47.179
mutiny.

00:32:47.179 --> 00:32:51.090
She claimed the Worm spoke to her from below,
and that their only path to salvation was

00:32:51.090 --> 00:32:52.340
pleasing the Worm.

00:32:52.340 --> 00:32:53.899
How would they please it?

00:32:53.899 --> 00:32:56.059
A sacrifice, of course.

00:32:56.059 --> 00:32:59.000
They would give it the son of the man who
had trapped it.

00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:04.779
The mutineers took the Inventor’s only remaining
child, and descended into the lowest sub levels.

00:33:04.779 --> 00:33:10.100
The Inventor followed, hoping to track them
down, save his son, and salvage something

00:33:10.100 --> 00:33:11.380
from this nightmare.

00:33:11.380 --> 00:33:15.700
As he ventured deeper, battling the members
of Eudora’s new cult, he found that they

00:33:15.700 --> 00:33:20.539
were changing themselves, becoming the half-human
cyborg creatures that the Foundation would

00:33:20.539 --> 00:33:21.860
later discover.

00:33:21.860 --> 00:33:25.220
The Inventor would find Eudora herself in
the Speaking Tube Room.

00:33:25.220 --> 00:33:30.549
Her body, still living, was wired into the
machinery, and she had sacrificed his son

00:33:30.549 --> 00:33:31.650
to the Worm.

00:33:31.650 --> 00:33:37.080
In a rage, the Inventor murdered Eudora, or
whatever was left of her, then heard a familiar

00:33:37.080 --> 00:33:40.269
voice speaking out of a nearby speaking tube.

00:33:40.269 --> 00:33:41.269
It said:

00:33:41.269 --> 00:33:43.080
“I am what you have made me.

00:33:43.080 --> 00:33:45.480
I am then and I am now.

00:33:45.480 --> 00:33:48.240
I am choice and I am tyranny.

00:33:48.240 --> 00:33:50.820
I am evil and I am flesh.

00:33:50.820 --> 00:33:53.360
I am beauty and I am chaos.

00:33:53.360 --> 00:33:55.900
I am the worm."

00:33:55.900 --> 00:33:57.539
The voice was his own.

00:33:57.539 --> 00:34:03.309
In that terrible moment, the Inventor realised
that the Worm wasn’t a giant, all-devouring

00:34:03.309 --> 00:34:05.269
monster, it was him.

00:34:05.269 --> 00:34:09.570
In trying to protect his loved ones from a
perceived apocalypse, he’d brought them

00:34:09.570 --> 00:34:11.429
all to their horrible demise.

00:34:11.429 --> 00:34:15.701
He’d trapped them with the monster he’d
hoped for them all to escape from, because

00:34:15.701 --> 00:34:19.929
no matter what you build, you can’t escape
who you are.

00:34:19.929 --> 00:34:24.389
Grief stricken and broken, the Inventor descended
into the Catalyst Room.

00:34:24.389 --> 00:34:31.020
There was his son, stuck with the syringes,
drained of all life to fuel the mighty machine

00:34:31.020 --> 00:34:33.000
his father created.

00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:38.409
In his last moments, the Inventor decided
to do the only noble thing: He threw himself

00:34:38.409 --> 00:34:43.700
into the machine, destroying both it and himself
in the process.

00:34:43.700 --> 00:34:50.530
The house was transported back to our reality,
but the Worm, in a sense, was no more.

00:34:50.530 --> 00:34:53.250
But who knows if the Worm is really dead.

00:34:53.250 --> 00:34:58.520
Its thoughts and poisonous intent still lingers
in the caverns, and rattles through the speaking

00:34:58.520 --> 00:34:59.520
pipes.

00:34:59.520 --> 00:35:04.010
Whatever really happened, the Foundation is
still picking up the pieces today - and who

00:35:04.010 --> 00:35:07.829
knows what lurks in the parts still hidden
from our knowledge.

00:35:07.829 --> 00:35:13.040
We’ve all heard of the Led Zeppelin song
“Stairway to Heaven”, a title that invokes

00:35:13.040 --> 00:35:17.420
the image of a stairway leading up to a land
of peace and paradise.

00:35:17.420 --> 00:35:19.640
But where else could a stairway lead?

00:35:19.640 --> 00:35:22.290
To a dusty attic full of old photo albums.

00:35:22.290 --> 00:35:27.190
To the upper level of a mall, where the movie
theater and frozen yogurt shop are neatly

00:35:27.190 --> 00:35:28.440
situated.

00:35:28.440 --> 00:35:31.500
Perhaps it leads to a rooftop with a beautiful
view.

00:35:31.500 --> 00:35:38.170
Or maybe, just maybe, a staircase could lead
you to SCP-2427.

00:35:38.170 --> 00:35:44.530
SCP-2427, appropriately nicknamed “A Thing
Full of Stuff”, is an extradimensional area

00:35:44.530 --> 00:35:49.099
filled with a variety of unusual and anomalous
objects.

00:35:49.099 --> 00:35:56.270
SCP-2427 can be accessed by way of a broken
stone staircase located in rural Ohio.

00:35:56.270 --> 00:36:00.569
According to local legend, carrying a sprig
of hemlock up the broken stairs will allow

00:36:00.569 --> 00:36:06.370
a person to emerge into a mysterious grass
clearing that appears to be in a forest somewhere

00:36:06.370 --> 00:36:07.940
in the United States.

00:36:07.940 --> 00:36:13.420
No matter what time a person ascends the staircase,
the solar time in the clearing will always

00:36:13.420 --> 00:36:14.910
be 2:00 PM.

00:36:14.910 --> 00:36:17.510
You know how people say “it’s 5:00 somewhere?”

00:36:17.510 --> 00:36:22.530
Well, it’s 2:00 somewhere too, and that
somewhere is here.

00:36:22.530 --> 00:36:29.050
The pocket dimension that is SCP-2427 is thought
to have been a holding area for weapons, prisoners,

00:36:29.050 --> 00:36:34.040
and artifacts belonging to an ancient cult
known as The Brazen Heart.

00:36:34.040 --> 00:36:38.569
Little is known about this relatively obscure
cult, other than the fact that they worship

00:36:38.569 --> 00:36:44.980
the demonic entity Moloch - a known enthusiast
of violent human sacrifice - and were previously

00:36:44.980 --> 00:36:48.820
thought to have been eradicated during the
Spanish Inquisition.

00:36:48.820 --> 00:36:55.079
The existence of SCP-2427 suggests that they
are very much not eradicated and are still

00:36:55.079 --> 00:36:56.079
active.

00:36:56.079 --> 00:37:01.440
They refer to these holding areas as “attics”
and though no confirmed members of the Brazen

00:37:01.440 --> 00:37:06.160
Heart have been contacted, it is considered
possible that there are at least a handful

00:37:06.160 --> 00:37:09.140
of other attics hidden around the world.

00:37:09.140 --> 00:37:16.180
The Foundation has identified seven anomalous
objects inside of SCP-2427 so far, each strange

00:37:16.180 --> 00:37:20.160
in its own beautiful, though often terrible,
way.

00:37:20.160 --> 00:37:24.030
Like snowflakes, if they were capable of killing
or maiming you.

00:37:24.030 --> 00:37:32.359
The first object in SCP-2427, aka SCP-2427-1,
is a seemingly normal fire hydrant.

00:37:32.359 --> 00:37:36.510
However, if you think there’s anything normal
about the items found here then you haven’t

00:37:36.510 --> 00:37:38.210
been paying attention.

00:37:38.210 --> 00:37:44.250
The hydrant is made out of lead, and, when
opened, it expels high levels of ionized radiation.

00:37:44.250 --> 00:37:48.599
No specific measurements of the radiation
have been taken yet, but it is definitely

00:37:48.599 --> 00:37:51.190
hazardous to human health.

00:37:51.190 --> 00:37:55.620
One unfortunate member of D-class personnel
has proven that it is a high enough level

00:37:55.620 --> 00:37:57.430
to melt human flesh.

00:37:57.430 --> 00:37:59.619
Sorry about your face, Dave.

00:37:59.619 --> 00:38:03.561
The hydrant is currently contained within
an electrified perimeter and is not to be

00:38:03.561 --> 00:38:07.780
opened under any circumstances to prevent
any further flesh melting.

00:38:07.780 --> 00:38:10.730
The last thing we need is another Dave incident.

00:38:10.730 --> 00:38:18.800
The second object contained within SCP-2427,
or SCP-2427-2, is not actually an object at

00:38:18.800 --> 00:38:20.839
all, it’s a building.

00:38:20.839 --> 00:38:24.140
Only on number two, and we’re already throwing
curveballs at you.

00:38:24.140 --> 00:38:27.520
Trust no one, surprises lurk around every
corner.

00:38:27.520 --> 00:38:33.560
This particular building resembles a large,
multi-storied sanitarium built in the 1860s.

00:38:33.560 --> 00:38:38.390
Though it is clear from the outside that the
building has, or should have, multiple stories,

00:38:38.390 --> 00:38:40.730
the inside is a different matter.

00:38:40.730 --> 00:38:46.060
Past the building’s front doors is a non-Euclidian
space consisting of a single floor and three

00:38:46.060 --> 00:38:49.720
sparsely decorated rooms with one central
foyer.

00:38:49.720 --> 00:38:58.420
The first room is the holding place for SCP-2427-3,
the second contains SCP-2427-4, and the third

00:38:58.420 --> 00:39:03.690
room contains nothing except scattered religious
documents, bottled water, and a selection

00:39:03.690 --> 00:39:05.329
of canned foods.

00:39:05.329 --> 00:39:10.099
No unauthorized staff are permitted to enter
the building, in order to minimize complications

00:39:10.099 --> 00:39:12.900
or potential employee casualties.

00:39:12.900 --> 00:39:18.210
The first two anomalies on this list are hardly
even strange by SCP Foundation standards.

00:39:18.210 --> 00:39:23.089
Sure, the hydrant can melt your face and the
building defies the laws of physics and space,

00:39:23.089 --> 00:39:26.599
but that’s just a regular Tuesday around
these parts.

00:39:26.599 --> 00:39:30.299
been there, seen that.

00:39:30.299 --> 00:39:31.970
What else have you got?

00:39:31.970 --> 00:39:35.400
Well, SCP-2427-3 is where things really get
strange.

00:39:35.400 --> 00:39:40.760
If you’re wandering through the bowels of
SCP-2427-2 and you make a wrong turn into

00:39:40.760 --> 00:39:45.900
the first room, you will find yourself face
to face with a startling sight.

00:39:45.900 --> 00:39:51.089
This entity is a combination of electronic
circuitry, a cow’s digestive tract, the

00:39:51.089 --> 00:39:57.390
hairless head of a human man, a hat rack,
several lengths of garden hose, and an unidentified

00:39:57.390 --> 00:39:59.250
crystalline structure.

00:39:59.250 --> 00:40:04.560
This creature is extraordinarily fast and
strong, exhibiting carnivorous tendencies

00:40:04.560 --> 00:40:07.960
and a very strong point of view on the world
around it.

00:40:07.960 --> 00:40:13.230
Lucky for us, it is capable of speech and
is able to tell us just what it thinks.

00:40:13.230 --> 00:40:18.230
Though this monstrosity doesn’t have much
of a right to pass judgment on anyone, cow

00:40:18.230 --> 00:40:23.550
intestine body and all, it has expressed a
violent hatred of all life that it considers

00:40:23.550 --> 00:40:25.170
“impure”.

00:40:25.170 --> 00:40:31.150
Anyone who encounters SCP-2427-3 experiences
an overwhelming desire to submit themselves

00:40:31.150 --> 00:40:35.319
for judgment, allowing the creature to determine
their “purity”.

00:40:35.319 --> 00:40:40.260
There is a rumor that, if one is judged to
be “pure”, they will have a wish granted.

00:40:40.260 --> 00:40:44.540
If they are deemed impure, however, they will
be devoured alive.

00:40:44.540 --> 00:40:49.890
If you’re tempted to introduce yourself
to the creature, your odds are not especially

00:40:49.890 --> 00:40:50.890
great.

00:40:50.890 --> 00:40:53.790
The creature has not encountered a single
“pure” being yet.

00:40:53.790 --> 00:41:00.500
In order to protect the Foundation staff working
in its vicinity, the entrance to SCP-2427-3’s

00:41:00.500 --> 00:41:04.970
room has been sealed off with a reinforced
steel door, and the windows have been paved

00:41:04.970 --> 00:41:06.770
over with concrete.

00:41:06.770 --> 00:41:09.480
Armed guards are watching the entrance at
all times.

00:41:09.480 --> 00:41:14.770
The creature must be fed one live goat per
day, in order to keep its appetite sated.

00:41:14.770 --> 00:41:19.010
The Foundation’s goat budget is through
the roof these days, but it’s worth it to

00:41:19.010 --> 00:41:21.050
keep the thing contained.

00:41:21.050 --> 00:41:26.530
Better to spend money on goats now and not
spend money on cannibalized personnel later.

00:41:26.530 --> 00:41:33.380
SCP-2427-4 consists, not of an object located
within a room, but the room itself.

00:41:33.380 --> 00:41:38.180
The room, which contains no furniture and
a linoleum floor, has a peculiar effect on

00:41:38.180 --> 00:41:39.740
the human psyche.

00:41:39.740 --> 00:41:44.820
Once a person steps foot into the room, they
lose consciousness for five minutes.

00:41:44.820 --> 00:41:48.819
During this time, they will speak freely,
listing off a variety of negative qualities

00:41:48.819 --> 00:41:50.440
about themselves.

00:41:50.440 --> 00:41:54.380
Once they wake up, they have no memory of
entering this state, or anything that they

00:41:54.380 --> 00:41:55.829
said during it.

00:41:55.829 --> 00:41:58.109
It’s cheaper than therapy, right?

00:41:58.109 --> 00:42:03.060
But it’s also much weirder, and less effective,
so you get what you pay for in the end.

00:42:03.060 --> 00:42:07.829
A member of D-Class personnel who was observed
inside of the room waxed poetic about his

00:42:07.829 --> 00:42:13.750
personal failings, beginning his monologue
with “my soul is a den of spiders” and

00:42:13.750 --> 00:42:18.819
ending it with “O hearer, whence I awaken,
hesitate not to feed my flesh and my soul

00:42:18.819 --> 00:42:20.270
to the Judge-beast.”

00:42:20.270 --> 00:42:22.950
Somebody give this guy a hug.

00:42:22.950 --> 00:42:26.809
Because the room seems to have no adverse
effects on human test subjects, except for

00:42:26.809 --> 00:42:31.640
causing everyone who hears their monologue
a bit of discomfort, there are no containment

00:42:31.640 --> 00:42:34.400
procedures in effect for it at this time.

00:42:34.400 --> 00:42:38.880
We’ve had rooms, fire hydrants, and horrible
meat-robot hybrids, and now?

00:42:38.880 --> 00:42:42.530
You can’t even trust the clouds in the sky.

00:42:42.530 --> 00:42:48.670
SCP-2427-5 is a seemingly innocent cloud,
hovering stationary over the building.

00:42:48.670 --> 00:42:53.400
When looked at by a human for more than three
seconds, the cloud will eject a ball of solid

00:42:53.400 --> 00:42:56.599
lead toward the person at a supersonic speed.

00:42:56.599 --> 00:42:57.980
That’s right, folks.

00:42:57.980 --> 00:43:00.620
This cloud can and will shoot you.

00:43:00.620 --> 00:43:04.940
It hates being observed, but it also hates
when you try to leave the perimeter.

00:43:04.940 --> 00:43:09.359
It will attack any person attempting to leave
by firing the same lead ball at them.

00:43:09.359 --> 00:43:13.660
So far, 14 personnel have been killed by this
highly aggressive cloud.

00:43:13.660 --> 00:43:17.490
And some people still think thunderstorms
and hail are the worst things clouds have

00:43:17.490 --> 00:43:18.710
to offer.

00:43:18.710 --> 00:43:20.010
So naïve.

00:43:20.010 --> 00:43:24.450
As it is a literal cloud, there is no way
to contain it, so no people in the vicinity

00:43:24.450 --> 00:43:29.809
of the cloud are permitted to look at it for
more than three seconds at a time.

00:43:29.809 --> 00:43:37.950
SCP-2427-6 is a series of 18 small trees,
spread throughout the instance of SCP-2427.

00:43:37.950 --> 00:43:42.530
Above ground, the trees look normal, though
their species has proven surprisingly difficult

00:43:42.530 --> 00:43:43.750
to determine.

00:43:43.750 --> 00:43:47.700
From an external perspective, they are simply
ordinary trees.

00:43:47.700 --> 00:43:52.890
However, radar analysis revealed that the
roots of these trees are deeply strange.

00:43:52.890 --> 00:43:57.290
Instead of the usual twisting tree roots,
the ground below these trees contains a mass

00:43:57.290 --> 00:43:59.880
in the shape of a human body.

00:43:59.880 --> 00:44:04.730
Much to the disgust of the observing researchers,
these humanoid masses occasionally twitch

00:44:04.730 --> 00:44:07.660
and move, as if alive.

00:44:07.660 --> 00:44:12.050
The trees themselves appear to be growing
from the crotch area of each humanoid figure.

00:44:12.050 --> 00:44:16.220
How’s that for morning wood?

00:44:16.220 --> 00:44:21.410
This arrangement between tree and person seems
to be some kind of punishment, as each tree

00:44:21.410 --> 00:44:27.390
is marked with a plaque reading: “The lecherous
suffer what they must and it is beautiful.”

00:44:27.390 --> 00:44:31.770
Until it can be certain that the condition
of these human roots is not contagious, these

00:44:31.770 --> 00:44:37.640
trees are to be treated as potential biohazards
and isolated in individual containers.

00:44:37.640 --> 00:44:45.460
The final object in SCP-2427 currently categorized
by the Foundation is SCP-2427-7.

00:44:45.460 --> 00:44:54.309
SCP-2427-7 is a pile of ashes and wood located
just behind a posted sign that reads: “The

00:44:54.309 --> 00:44:55.680
Liars’ Cradle.”

00:44:55.680 --> 00:44:59.309
Extensive testing has established that the
Liars’ Cradle was almost certainly used

00:44:59.309 --> 00:45:03.600
as a torture device in interrogations performed
by The Brazen Heart.

00:45:03.600 --> 00:45:08.110
A person standing within the boundaries of
the cradle, which encompasses the aforementioned

00:45:08.110 --> 00:45:12.900
circle of wood and ashes, is unable to lie
without suffering the consequences.

00:45:12.900 --> 00:45:15.510
Namely, they will be set on fire.

00:45:15.510 --> 00:45:21.060
The nature of how exactly the Liars’ Cradle
works is not certain, and more research needs

00:45:21.060 --> 00:45:22.450
to be done on it.

00:45:22.450 --> 00:45:28.450
However, this much is known for sure: it contains
no sentient intelligence, it is not aware

00:45:28.450 --> 00:45:30.270
of what it is doing.

00:45:30.270 --> 00:45:35.400
It does not kill its victims, rather it keeps
them miraculously alive as it sets them on

00:45:35.400 --> 00:45:40.070
fire, prolonging their agony and allowing
their interrogators to get the truth out of

00:45:40.070 --> 00:45:41.070
them.

00:45:41.070 --> 00:45:46.800
A series of experiments revealed that it only
immolates a person who is knowingly lying.

00:45:46.800 --> 00:45:51.040
D-Class personnel given demonstrably false
information to repeat in the Cradle without

00:45:51.040 --> 00:45:54.140
knowledge of its falsehood were not set on
fire.

00:45:54.140 --> 00:45:59.470
However, when those same D-Class personnel
knowingly lied in the boundaries, they immediately

00:45:59.470 --> 00:46:01.100
were set ablaze.

00:46:01.100 --> 00:46:05.480
It is almost certain that the Brazen Heart
cult used the cradle as a method of interrogating

00:46:05.480 --> 00:46:08.050
presumed liars in their midst.

00:46:08.050 --> 00:46:12.780
Further investigation will likely reveal human
remains beneath the Cradle itself, though

00:46:12.780 --> 00:46:15.569
this is just a hypothesis currently.

00:46:15.569 --> 00:46:20.829
But come on, there has to be some bones somewhere
beneath something as ominous as The Liars’

00:46:20.829 --> 00:46:21.829
Cradle.

00:46:21.829 --> 00:46:27.470
Though they have only identified seven anomalies
inside SCP-2427 at the moment, there are plenty

00:46:27.470 --> 00:46:30.599
more lurking in there waiting to be discovered.

00:46:30.599 --> 00:46:38.099
In the foyer of SCP-2427-2, the Foundation
discovered an extremely ominous list of items,

00:46:38.099 --> 00:46:41.940
clearly belonging to members of the cult of
the Brazen Heart.

00:46:41.940 --> 00:46:47.210
This list included some familiar items, such
as “pilgrim provisions” also known as

00:46:47.210 --> 00:46:54.850
the canned beans and soups found in SCP-2427-2,
a Level Three Purity Proctor, a Purge Engine

00:46:54.850 --> 00:46:58.670
- disguised as a fire hydrant - and the Liars’
Cradle.

00:46:58.670 --> 00:47:03.260
However, it also contained many things that
have not yet been discovered, such as One

00:47:03.260 --> 00:47:10.930
Slaughtering Perseverance, 27 Pyre Children,
Three Ascended Cultivars, Seven Supreme Angelics,

00:47:10.930 --> 00:47:14.589
Nine Dragons, and the Brazen Heart itself.

00:47:14.589 --> 00:47:21.550
Dr. Gordon MacElroy, Site Director of Area-2427,
put out a memo to all Level 4 and higher staff

00:47:21.550 --> 00:47:25.540
assigned to the area after the discovery of
this list.

00:47:25.540 --> 00:47:30.740
Understandably, he was most concerned about
the “supreme angelics” and the “dragons”,

00:47:30.740 --> 00:47:32.329
particularly the latter.

00:47:32.329 --> 00:47:37.470
The cult, as most cults are, is fond of deliberately
obscure language, but you don’t want to

00:47:37.470 --> 00:47:42.460
rule out the possibility they’ve got a fire-breathing
lizard or two stashed away.

00:47:42.460 --> 00:47:48.849
In the meantime, as the Foundation is working
to better understand the contents of SCP-2427,

00:47:48.849 --> 00:47:51.460
the area has been sealed off to the public.

00:47:51.460 --> 00:47:56.840
A 500m perimeter has been established around
its entrance, and a fake private country club

00:47:56.840 --> 00:47:58.650
has been set up as a front.

00:47:58.650 --> 00:48:03.079
It’s only a matter of time before the rest
of the anomalies on the list are discovered,

00:48:03.079 --> 00:48:08.500
and this Thing Full of Stuff gets even fuller,
of even more stuff.

00:48:08.500 --> 00:48:11.200
Let’s just hope none of it ever gets out.

00:48:11.200 --> 00:48:15.520
Because if there are more of these attics
out there, who knows what else the Brazen

00:48:15.520 --> 00:48:17.230
Heart is hiding?

00:48:17.230 --> 00:48:21.880
Their little cult may not be as extinct as
we thought...

00:48:21.880 --> 00:48:25.339
You’re right in the middle of one of the
hottest summers on record.

00:48:25.339 --> 00:48:30.520
The days are filled with bright, scorching
sun and searing heat., and you’ve been laying

00:48:30.520 --> 00:48:35.550
around with your air conditioning on full
blast just to try and cool yourself off.

00:48:35.550 --> 00:48:40.540
Sadly, it’s not really working, and the
heat is becoming way too much.

00:48:40.540 --> 00:48:46.119
But then you remember, there’s this married
couple that lives near you, with no kids,

00:48:46.119 --> 00:48:49.530
and they happen to have a swimming pool in
their yard.

00:48:49.530 --> 00:48:53.890
Normally they keep to themselves, they’d
never let you use their pool, but they’ve

00:48:53.890 --> 00:48:56.230
gone out of town for a few days.

00:48:56.230 --> 00:49:00.150
Besides, the heat is killing you, you’re
sure that the neighbors wouldn’t mind if

00:49:00.150 --> 00:49:04.230
you just took a quick dip, as long as you
clean up after yourself.

00:49:04.230 --> 00:49:07.560
They probably wouldn’t even notice you were
ever there.

00:49:07.560 --> 00:49:09.940
Cautiously, you make your way to their house.

00:49:09.940 --> 00:49:14.770
It’s an unremarkable place, similar to most
of the other houses in this suburb of New

00:49:14.770 --> 00:49:15.870
Mexico.

00:49:15.870 --> 00:49:19.619
After checking that there’s nobody else
around, you climb the two-meter high cinder

00:49:19.619 --> 00:49:22.540
block wall that stands around the back garden.

00:49:22.540 --> 00:49:27.690
As you drop to your feet, sweaty and panting
from the unrelenting summer heat, you see

00:49:27.690 --> 00:49:31.190
it: the pool, your salvation.

00:49:31.190 --> 00:49:33.150
Water never looked so appealing.

00:49:33.150 --> 00:49:37.730
Immediately, you step barefoot across the
sun-scorched tiles and sit on the edge, legs

00:49:37.730 --> 00:49:38.920
in the water.

00:49:38.920 --> 00:49:42.809
It’s cool and refreshing, perfect for a
day as hot as today.

00:49:42.809 --> 00:49:46.880
You’re already changed and wearing your
swim trunks, so it doesn’t take long for

00:49:46.880 --> 00:49:51.869
you to paddle out to the middle of the pool,
letting that chilled, clean water cool you

00:49:51.869 --> 00:49:52.869
off.

00:49:52.869 --> 00:49:56.319
As you’re taking a dip, you notice the pool’s
jets turning on automatically.

00:49:56.319 --> 00:49:59.690
It’s a little bit odd, but you shrug it
off.

00:49:59.690 --> 00:50:04.369
That couple clearly shelled out for a pool
with a lot of fancy bells and whistles.

00:50:04.369 --> 00:50:09.210
But extra features aren’t why you’re here,
you came because if you didn’t, then you

00:50:09.210 --> 00:50:11.990
could have melted under all that sunlight.

00:50:11.990 --> 00:50:15.799
Floating on the surface of the water, you
relax with your arms behind your head and

00:50:15.799 --> 00:50:16.920
close your eyes.

00:50:16.920 --> 00:50:21.390
You don’t have time to realize that coming
here was a mistake.

00:50:21.390 --> 00:50:24.059
Instead, you start to feel relaxed.

00:50:24.059 --> 00:50:26.480
So calm, so tranquil.

00:50:26.480 --> 00:50:29.450
You’re one with the water around you now.

00:50:29.450 --> 00:50:33.160
It’s almost as though you could just disappear…

00:50:33.160 --> 00:50:35.470
So, you do.

00:50:35.470 --> 00:50:41.560
The police never find any trace of you, everyone
else simply writes it off as a random disappearance.

00:50:41.560 --> 00:50:47.531
There’s not even so much as a scrap of your
body left in the pool, just the clear, clean

00:50:47.531 --> 00:50:48.531
water.

00:50:48.531 --> 00:50:49.531
Why?

00:50:49.531 --> 00:50:54.700
Because the swimming pool you decided to take
a cooling dip in wasn’t an ordinary pool.

00:50:54.700 --> 00:50:55.810
It was SCP-242.

00:50:55.810 --> 00:51:01.700
But don’t worry, you won’t be the last
to make that costly mistake.

00:51:01.700 --> 00:51:05.369
What you didn’t know is that the “married
couple” who live in that house are secretly

00:51:05.369 --> 00:51:08.390
a pair of SCP Foundation doctors.

00:51:08.390 --> 00:51:13.859
The house isn’t even theirs, the Foundation
procured it after the former owner, a retired

00:51:13.859 --> 00:51:16.630
out-of-state landlord, strangely vanished.

00:51:16.630 --> 00:51:20.870
He had been struggling to find anyone to rent
the place, so eventually decided to give up

00:51:20.870 --> 00:51:24.160
on the property game and move in there himself.

00:51:24.160 --> 00:51:27.240
After three days, he was never seen again.

00:51:27.240 --> 00:51:33.980
Now, that house has only one rule that must
be followed above all else: do not swim in

00:51:33.980 --> 00:51:35.020
the pool.

00:51:35.020 --> 00:51:40.540
SCP-242 is, at least to the untrained eye,
just an average swimming pool.

00:51:40.540 --> 00:51:46.310
A decent nine meters in length, four and a
half wide, and it holds around 53,000 liters

00:51:46.310 --> 00:51:48.319
of sterile pool water.

00:51:48.319 --> 00:51:53.470
Like we mentioned before, it’s even got
some nifty features like water jets, a dual

00:51:53.470 --> 00:51:58.020
waterfall, and a built-in vacuum unit for
sucking out any impurities.

00:51:58.020 --> 00:52:01.170
And we mean any impurities.

00:52:01.170 --> 00:52:06.830
You see, SCP-242 does go by another name:
the Self Cleaning Swimming Pool.

00:52:06.830 --> 00:52:11.619
And while that might not sound as foreboding
or dramatic as “The Scarlet King” or “The

00:52:11.619 --> 00:52:16.339
Wendigo Skull” or “The Horrifying Nasty-Dude
of Ultimate Badness” - okay, we made that

00:52:16.339 --> 00:52:21.680
last one up - we can assure you that you don’t
ever want to suffer the fate of taking a swim

00:52:21.680 --> 00:52:23.140
in this pool.

00:52:23.140 --> 00:52:28.240
There was an incident a while ago, recorded
by the Foundation through a secret hidden

00:52:28.240 --> 00:52:29.240
camera.

00:52:29.240 --> 00:52:34.410
The house where SCP-242 can be found had been
left vacant for a time, and once again some

00:52:34.410 --> 00:52:38.849
opportunists decided to take advantage of
the empty swimming pool.

00:52:38.849 --> 00:52:43.089
This time it was a couple, a man and a woman
in their early twenties.

00:52:43.089 --> 00:52:47.730
They climbed up the back wall, undressed,
and even stole a couple of plastic inflatable

00:52:47.730 --> 00:52:50.660
rafts from a shed in the house’s backyard.

00:52:50.660 --> 00:52:55.590
The water jets switched themselves on, startling
the girl, but her boyfriend told her not to

00:52:55.590 --> 00:53:00.180
worry, the filter to clean the pool was probably
just on an automatic timer, right?

00:53:00.180 --> 00:53:03.609
Surely it wouldn’t have been anything to
worry about.

00:53:03.609 --> 00:53:07.119
After swimming around together for about twenty
four minutes, the couple both agreed that

00:53:07.119 --> 00:53:10.329
the water felt warm, tingly even.

00:53:10.329 --> 00:53:15.410
Both of them climbed onto their rafts, eventually
falling asleep while still holding each other’s

00:53:15.410 --> 00:53:16.410
hands.

00:53:16.410 --> 00:53:21.099
But, almost half an hour after the jets had
started, something caused the two rafts to

00:53:21.099 --> 00:53:22.099
burst.

00:53:22.099 --> 00:53:25.810
The couple awoke, startled by the loud pop
of the splitting inflatables and being plunged

00:53:25.810 --> 00:53:27.299
back into the water.

00:53:27.299 --> 00:53:33.150
The pool around them immediately began frothing
violently, deep red streams of blood swirling

00:53:33.150 --> 00:53:37.020
through the water as the couple screamed in
fear and agony.

00:53:37.020 --> 00:53:41.619
Both of them tried to desperately swim to
the edge, hoping to leave the pool and get

00:53:41.619 --> 00:53:42.619
to safety.

00:53:42.619 --> 00:53:45.890
But unfortunately, that plan didn’t work.

00:53:45.890 --> 00:53:49.280
Before they could reach the edge, the man
and the woman were pulled under the surface

00:53:49.280 --> 00:53:54.370
of the raging water, their limbs thrashing
as they still tried in vain to escape.

00:53:54.370 --> 00:53:58.080
Eventually, they vanished under the crimson,
bloody water.

00:53:58.080 --> 00:54:03.850
The frothing slowly began to calm, and the
red in the pool dissipated, once again becoming

00:54:03.850 --> 00:54:06.560
clear after forty-eight seconds.

00:54:06.560 --> 00:54:11.549
The couple were never seen again, and a cover
story was leaked to the press by the SCP Foundation

00:54:11.549 --> 00:54:13.890
two weeks after they went missing.

00:54:13.890 --> 00:54:17.069
According to them, the pair had eloped together
somewhere in Mexico.

00:54:17.069 --> 00:54:21.670
If only, that sounds a lot nicer than what
actually happened to them.

00:54:21.670 --> 00:54:27.260
So, this swimming pool clearly has some anomalous
properties, that much is obvious.

00:54:27.260 --> 00:54:32.670
But what exactly are those properties, how
exactly does SCP-242 work?

00:54:32.670 --> 00:54:37.271
Is it an interdimensional gateway that drags
people to a nasty alternate universe if they

00:54:37.271 --> 00:54:39.490
spend too long swimming in it?

00:54:39.490 --> 00:54:44.660
Or is the swimming pool itself a sentient,
carnivorous creature that lures humans in

00:54:44.660 --> 00:54:46.470
only to devour them?

00:54:46.470 --> 00:54:50.500
Maybe the water is teeming with invisible,
flesh-eating piranhas that can strip the meat

00:54:50.500 --> 00:54:52.829
from a bone in a matter of seconds.

00:54:52.829 --> 00:54:57.349
Well, good guesses all around but actually,
it’s none of these.

00:54:57.349 --> 00:55:02.869
It’s unclear what causes the pool’s anomalous
effects, it could be a property that is completely

00:55:02.869 --> 00:55:06.610
unique to the water contained in SCP-242.

00:55:06.610 --> 00:55:10.530
Or maybe it’s down to the exact shape and
measurements of the pool itself.

00:55:10.530 --> 00:55:12.619
It could even be a combination of both.

00:55:12.619 --> 00:55:16.660
But whatever the cause, the result is always
the same.

00:55:16.660 --> 00:55:23.140
When any object, substance, or even living
organism is placed in SCP-242, it will be

00:55:23.140 --> 00:55:26.619
entirely rewritten on a molecular level.

00:55:26.619 --> 00:55:31.000
The genetic and atomic structure will fall
apart, and the subject will be transmuted

00:55:31.000 --> 00:55:32.630
into sterile water.

00:55:32.630 --> 00:55:37.530
In fact, not just clean water, but water that
remains sterile even when removed from the

00:55:37.530 --> 00:55:38.530
pool.

00:55:38.530 --> 00:55:43.599
If you took a cup of SCP-242’s water and
mixed something like food coloring into it,

00:55:43.599 --> 00:55:49.059
the food coloring would not be absorbed into
the water, instead staying as one non-miscible

00:55:49.059 --> 00:55:50.069
bubble.

00:55:50.069 --> 00:55:54.820
This process doesn’t happen instantly though,
it can vary depending on how contaminated

00:55:54.820 --> 00:55:57.990
or complex the substance placed in SCP-242
is.

00:55:57.990 --> 00:56:03.880
For example, water sampled from a nearby river
was sterilized and purified by the pool in

00:56:03.880 --> 00:56:05.410
about seven minutes.

00:56:05.410 --> 00:56:10.609
A sample of stagnant pond water, riddled with
various diseases and germs, took eleven minutes

00:56:10.609 --> 00:56:11.609
longer.

00:56:11.609 --> 00:56:13.849
What about fifty thousand liters of coal tar?

00:56:13.849 --> 00:56:19.920
Well, that one took a little longer, twelve
long days to be exact, but was still turned

00:56:19.920 --> 00:56:22.059
into pure, sterile water.

00:56:22.059 --> 00:56:24.339
And as for a living human being?

00:56:24.339 --> 00:56:28.030
Maybe ask that couple that took a dip in the
Self Cleaning Pool.

00:56:28.030 --> 00:56:33.010
The Foundation is naturally fascinated with
the pool, and after extensive examination,

00:56:33.010 --> 00:56:38.460
they have determined that SCP-242 doesn’t
seem to have been intentionally designed for

00:56:38.460 --> 00:56:41.860
the specific anomalous function it performs.

00:56:41.860 --> 00:56:48.270
The components of SCP-242 beyond the pool
itself; the filter, the vacuum, the pipes,

00:56:48.270 --> 00:56:52.920
none of these parts nor anything about the
swimming pool’s design appear to be responsible

00:56:52.920 --> 00:56:56.800
for disintegrating matter until only water
remains.

00:56:56.800 --> 00:57:02.220
You might have noticed that in the case of
the ill-fated couple who took a swim in SCP-242,

00:57:02.220 --> 00:57:07.240
the water jets and waterfall features switched
themselves on automatically, before the pair’s

00:57:07.240 --> 00:57:08.589
grim demise.

00:57:08.589 --> 00:57:13.579
Somehow, these features are able to activate
without the need for electricity, as disconnecting

00:57:13.579 --> 00:57:18.300
the pool from a power source will not stop
the jets and waterfall from coming on once

00:57:18.300 --> 00:57:23.070
a non-water substance is placed into SCP-242.

00:57:23.070 --> 00:57:28.329
The same goes for the pool vacuum, which apparently
cannot be jammed or malfunction.

00:57:28.329 --> 00:57:32.950
Even when the bottom of the pool is awash
with viscous liquids like that coal tar, the

00:57:32.950 --> 00:57:39.150
vacuum will continue to operate as normal,
scrubbing away at the floor of SCP-242.

00:57:39.150 --> 00:57:43.450
The one part of the Self Cleaning Pool that
doesn’t work as you would expect is the

00:57:43.450 --> 00:57:45.220
water filtration system.

00:57:45.220 --> 00:57:49.630
There is never any water being cycled into
the pool, nor out of it.

00:57:49.630 --> 00:57:54.950
As a matter of fact, the pipes connected to
the filtration system have all been removed.

00:57:54.950 --> 00:57:58.799
Then again, who needs a filtration system
when your backyard swimming pool can just

00:57:58.799 --> 00:58:01.819
spontaneously reduce anything to clean water?

00:58:01.819 --> 00:58:06.710
But that raises another frightening thought:
Everything that the pool has ever taken and

00:58:06.710 --> 00:58:14.580
converted is still in there - animals, objects,
people - just swimming around you.

00:58:14.580 --> 00:58:19.589
Perhaps, if they could still think, they’d
scream and shout and tell you to get away.

00:58:19.589 --> 00:58:21.610
To run while you still can.

00:58:21.610 --> 00:58:26.900
But the second your skin touches the water,
you’re destined to be with them.

00:58:26.900 --> 00:58:29.829
Forever and ever and ever.

00:58:29.829 --> 00:58:32.940
It’s enough to send a liquid chill down
your spine.

00:58:32.940 --> 00:58:37.700
Okay, so if it’s not the actual physical
pool that causes these anomalous effects,

00:58:37.700 --> 00:58:40.510
that must mean it’s something in the water,
right?

00:58:40.510 --> 00:58:44.920
Perhaps some microscopic, flesh-devouring
microbe, or some ancient curse that was placed

00:58:44.920 --> 00:58:47.670
on the water before it was used to fill the
pool?

00:58:47.670 --> 00:58:53.110
Surely, if you took a cup of the water out
of SCP-242, it would still break down structures

00:58:53.110 --> 00:58:56.559
on a molecular level, leaving only more sterile
water.

00:58:56.559 --> 00:59:01.880
Well, the researchers working at the SCP Foundation
thought much the same and conducted a series

00:59:01.880 --> 00:59:07.220
of tests to determine the exact properties
of SCP-242’s water.

00:59:07.220 --> 00:59:11.970
One test involved submerging two D Class test
subjects, each wearing an atmospheric dive

00:59:11.970 --> 00:59:14.810
suit, into SCP-242.

00:59:14.810 --> 00:59:19.670
The goal was to determine if it was safe to
consume the water from SCP-242 while both

00:59:19.670 --> 00:59:22.210
inside and outside of the pool.

00:59:22.210 --> 00:59:25.990
Test Subject A was lowered into the water
and instructed to drink from a metal straw

00:59:25.990 --> 00:59:27.410
by their mouth.

00:59:27.410 --> 00:59:31.251
The eyepieces of their goggles were blacked
out, so they couldn’t see what they were

00:59:31.251 --> 00:59:32.910
drinking from.

00:59:32.910 --> 00:59:37.839
Subject B filled a barrel with the same water
from SCP-242, and then was made to put on

00:59:37.839 --> 00:59:42.140
an atmospheric dive suit, but instructed to
stay out of the pool.

00:59:42.140 --> 00:59:46.859
Test Subject A was told to drink directly
from the pool, remarking that the water was

00:59:46.859 --> 00:59:52.000
warm, and had a bit of a noticeable chemical
aftertaste, but was otherwise normal.

00:59:52.000 --> 00:59:55.530
Then, Test Subject B drank some of the same
water from the barrel.

00:59:55.530 --> 01:00:02.180
Apparently, it was cool, and tasted of…
well, nothing, just like water usually does.

01:00:02.180 --> 01:00:07.650
After a moment more of drink, Subject A began
belching, finding they had uncontrollable

01:00:07.650 --> 01:00:08.650
gas.

01:00:08.650 --> 01:00:13.520
The water had begun to feel warmer, stinging
the subject’s mouth while, for Subject B,

01:00:13.520 --> 01:00:16.260
the water from the barrel stayed cool and
refreshing.

01:00:16.260 --> 01:00:21.200
The Foundation doctors overseeing the experiment
instructed Test Subject A to keep drinking,

01:00:21.200 --> 01:00:24.490
which they did until it felt even hotter to
the taste.

01:00:24.490 --> 01:00:28.609
One of the D Class’s fillings even fell
out, and eventually, the structural integrity

01:00:28.609 --> 01:00:35.110
of Subject A’s dive suit failed, presumably
disintegrated by the water from SCP-242.

01:00:35.110 --> 01:00:40.460
After a few muffled screams and gurgling noises,
Test Subject A wasn’t heard from again,

01:00:40.460 --> 01:00:43.140
and we can all probably guess why.

01:00:43.140 --> 01:00:47.750
As for Subject B, they kept drinking from
the barrel, suffering no adverse effects,

01:00:47.750 --> 01:00:50.730
even after seventeen long hours.

01:00:50.730 --> 01:00:55.440
There were no noticeable psychological or
physical changes, even their urine showed

01:00:55.440 --> 01:00:57.660
no traces of abnormality.

01:00:57.660 --> 01:01:03.150
The water from SCP-242 left in the barrel
evaporated as normal, leaving behind no residue

01:01:03.150 --> 01:01:08.849
or any indicator as to why taking the water
out of the pool made it safer to drink than

01:01:08.849 --> 01:01:11.359
the same water in the pool.

01:01:11.359 --> 01:01:16.049
Perhaps the moral of the story is to just
be careful where you choose to take a swim,

01:01:16.049 --> 01:01:19.660
otherwise, it could be your last.

01:01:19.660 --> 01:01:25.430
You’re on a road trip - the kind that stretches
over days on end, and you need to make multiple

01:01:25.430 --> 01:01:29.420
stops along the way to refuel the car and
yourself.

01:01:29.420 --> 01:01:34.310
The last time you remember stopping to get
more gas and a bite to eat was back in Wyoming,

01:01:34.310 --> 01:01:36.289
and now, you’re in the heart of Montana.

01:01:36.289 --> 01:01:41.430
Thankfully, like an oasis in the desert, you
see the town of Clear Water off in the distance.

01:01:41.430 --> 01:01:47.480
It’s a vibrant, welcoming little place,
a perfect slice of classic, small-town Americana.

01:01:47.480 --> 01:01:51.849
You took a similar trip last year, and vaguely
remembered stopping at Clear Water that time

01:01:51.849 --> 01:01:54.339
too and you’re glad to be back.

01:01:54.339 --> 01:01:58.900
In particular, you remember the Old Prairie
Diner, a folksy little place with the most

01:01:58.900 --> 01:02:02.190
delicious Huckleberry Pie you ever tasted.

01:02:02.190 --> 01:02:05.069
Perhaps it’s about time for you to give
it another try.

01:02:05.069 --> 01:02:07.400
You fill up your tank and stop at the diner.

01:02:07.400 --> 01:02:13.020
The food tastes just as good as you remember,
but one thing is off: The entire staff seems

01:02:13.020 --> 01:02:14.150
to have changed.

01:02:14.150 --> 01:02:19.000
It’s the exact same diner you ate in a year
ago, no doubt about that, but it looks like

01:02:19.000 --> 01:02:23.740
everyone from the wait staff to the cashier
to the cooks have all been replaced.

01:02:23.740 --> 01:02:28.529
You try your best not to think about it, after
all, businesses are allowed to replace their

01:02:28.529 --> 01:02:33.930
staff, but the longer you sit in the diner,
the more uncomfortable the feelings become.

01:02:33.930 --> 01:02:38.970
You need to ask someone, just to push away
the fears that you’re going crazy.

01:02:38.970 --> 01:02:43.000
When a waiter passes by, you compliment the
food, and mention that you ate here last year

01:02:43.000 --> 01:02:44.000
too.

01:02:44.000 --> 01:02:47.109
You ask the unfamiliar waiter if they had
worked here back then.

01:02:47.109 --> 01:02:51.730
They confirm that, yes, they’ve always worked
here - and so has everybody else.

01:02:51.730 --> 01:02:54.240
The diner is a family business.

01:02:54.240 --> 01:02:59.260
You leave town not too long after that, feeling
vaguely unsettled, and as a voice on the radio

01:02:59.260 --> 01:03:03.920
warns about the incoming rain, you tell yourself
that you never want to return to the town

01:03:03.920 --> 01:03:05.840
of Clear Water, Montana.

01:03:05.840 --> 01:03:11.010
As you leave, the memory of the town seems
to fade from your mind in real time, but little

01:03:11.010 --> 01:03:15.549
do you know, the people of Clear Water will
never be able to leave.

01:03:15.549 --> 01:03:16.549
Ever.

01:03:16.549 --> 01:03:21.390
It’s because something horrifying will happen
in Clear Water every single year, and that

01:03:21.390 --> 01:03:26.869
thing is known to the SCP Foundation as SCP-3300.

01:03:26.869 --> 01:03:31.970
This annual anomalous event is Clear Water’s
own local curse, always occurring around mid-June.

01:03:31.970 --> 01:03:36.850
While many of the mechanics of this event
still elude the Foundation’s understanding,

01:03:36.850 --> 01:03:42.180
the outcome is well-documented: Every single
inhabitant of the town is replaced by a person

01:03:42.180 --> 01:03:44.360
who didn’t previously exist.

01:03:44.360 --> 01:03:49.310
While some elements may carry over from their
original counterparts, every person involved

01:03:49.310 --> 01:03:55.310
will simply be a whole new person, with no
memories of the change or who they once were.

01:03:55.310 --> 01:04:01.270
The process known as SCP-3300 lasts between
six and eighteen days, and once the process

01:04:01.270 --> 01:04:04.980
has begun, it’s impossible for any outsiders
to intervene.

01:04:04.980 --> 01:04:11.590
It begins with rain - a light, dreary drizzle
at first, but each day, the rain gets worse.

01:04:11.590 --> 01:04:16.230
Soon, it’s a storm, and then, a maelstrom.

01:04:16.230 --> 01:04:20.400
Flooding, hurricanes, tornadoes, all centered
around Clear Water, but cutting off neatly

01:04:20.400 --> 01:04:21.750
just beyond it.

01:04:21.750 --> 01:04:26.100
What happens in Clear Water remains in Clear
Water, and when the process has concluded

01:04:26.100 --> 01:04:30.319
and the sun shines once more, everybody has
been changed .

01:04:30.319 --> 01:04:35.109
Whenever the Foundation has tried to send
personnel or equipment into Clear Water during

01:04:35.109 --> 01:04:41.559
SCP-3300, one of two things have happened:
In the more favorable scenarios, those attempting

01:04:41.559 --> 01:04:45.490
to enter Clear Water have simply appeared
on the other side of the city limits.

01:04:45.490 --> 01:04:51.520
In the less positive instances, personnel
and equipment have been lost forever within.

01:04:51.520 --> 01:04:55.900
There is no stopping or even understanding
SCP-3300.

01:04:55.900 --> 01:05:00.430
According to Foundation records, Clear Water
has been around at least as long as the Foundation

01:05:00.430 --> 01:05:03.069
itself, perhaps even longer.

01:05:03.069 --> 01:05:07.890
Clear Water has been able to undergo its yearly
nightmare without intrusion due to a unique

01:05:07.890 --> 01:05:13.099
cognitohazardous effect, which creates a kind
of mental block around memories of the town

01:05:13.099 --> 01:05:14.460
for outsiders.

01:05:14.460 --> 01:05:19.400
You won’t forget Clear Water, per se, but
you will find it increasingly hard to focus

01:05:19.400 --> 01:05:20.400
on.

01:05:20.400 --> 01:05:23.990
Like something you can only ever see out of
the corner of your eye.

01:05:23.990 --> 01:05:26.530
There is no saving the people of Clear Water.

01:05:26.530 --> 01:05:30.720
The horror will play out again and again and
again…

01:05:30.720 --> 01:05:34.520
The Foundation has no first-hand knowledge
of what happens in Clear Water during those

01:05:34.520 --> 01:05:36.840
horrifying eighteen days.

01:05:36.840 --> 01:05:40.610
But one account they have hints at a terrifying
possibility.

01:05:40.610 --> 01:05:44.890
During an excursion into Clear Water, the
Foundation managed to collect a diary belonging

01:05:44.890 --> 01:05:47.359
to a woman named Margaret Lane.

01:05:47.359 --> 01:05:51.940
To the best of our knowledge, Margaret Lane
no longer exists, but if the contents of her

01:05:51.940 --> 01:05:58.420
diary are to be believed, then what goes on
in Clear Water during SCP-3300 is far worse

01:05:58.420 --> 01:06:00.789
than we’d ever imagined.

01:06:00.789 --> 01:06:07.280
Margaret first started her diary not long
before SCP-3300’s 1995 iteration began.

01:06:07.280 --> 01:06:11.730
She was in the middle of a tumultuous time
in her life - freshly clean from alcohol and

01:06:11.730 --> 01:06:17.819
drug addiction, forced to live with her antagonistic
mother, and having peculiar and distressing

01:06:17.819 --> 01:06:18.819
dreams.

01:06:18.819 --> 01:06:24.040
In the first dream Margaret recorded, she
was...someone else, a woman living in a small

01:06:24.040 --> 01:06:26.539
hut perhaps a century ago or more.

01:06:26.539 --> 01:06:28.020
It was plague time.

01:06:28.020 --> 01:06:33.559
She was looking down upon her daughter, bedridden,
her skin covered in painful-looking red blotches.

01:06:33.559 --> 01:06:36.000
Her husband was already dead.

01:06:36.000 --> 01:06:39.230
That’s when another man enters, a healthy
man.

01:06:39.230 --> 01:06:41.819
He tells her that he’s found their salvation.

01:06:41.819 --> 01:06:43.650
And then the dream ended.

01:06:43.650 --> 01:06:46.420
Margaret woke up to a gray, dreary day.

01:06:46.420 --> 01:06:48.380
There were clouds on the horizon.

01:06:48.380 --> 01:06:50.130
The rain was coming.

01:06:50.130 --> 01:06:54.730
It drizzled for the next few days, before
getting more intense - as one would expect

01:06:54.730 --> 01:06:57.230
from an SCP-3300 cycle.

01:06:57.230 --> 01:07:00.059
Of course, nothing seemed out of place to
Margaret.

01:07:00.059 --> 01:07:05.250
Life carried on - she continued to stay clean,
resisting the offers of her old dealer, though

01:07:05.250 --> 01:07:08.180
her relationship with her mother remained
frosty.

01:07:08.180 --> 01:07:12.700
The rain started to get worse as voices on
the radio insisted that conditions would continue

01:07:12.700 --> 01:07:15.460
to become more severe over the next few days.

01:07:15.460 --> 01:07:20.829
They tried their best to maintain normality;
Margaret invited some friends - Jared, Sam,

01:07:20.829 --> 01:07:24.890
Mike, and Isabel - to come over and play D&amp;D
at her place.

01:07:24.890 --> 01:07:27.520
That was when all hell broke loose.

01:07:27.520 --> 01:07:31.630
While the group roleplayed, there was a furious
banging at the door, like whoever was knocking

01:07:31.630 --> 01:07:33.920
was trying to bash the door down.

01:07:33.920 --> 01:07:38.810
When Margaret’s mom opened the door to investigate
the commotion, she saw that an entire family

01:07:38.810 --> 01:07:43.250
was standing there - a father, a mother, and
two young children.

01:07:43.250 --> 01:07:47.940
The father immediately began furiously asking
why all these strangers were in his house.

01:07:47.940 --> 01:07:51.990
When Margaret’s mother tried to tell him
that this wasn’t his house, he became increasingly

01:07:51.990 --> 01:07:55.010
agitated, and walked straight into the home.

01:07:55.010 --> 01:07:59.700
Margaret’s friends attempted to subdue him,
but he threw them off, displaying a supernatural

01:07:59.700 --> 01:08:00.700
strength.

01:08:00.700 --> 01:08:04.630
Margaret’s mom ran in with a golf club and
struck the mysterious man in the chest.

01:08:04.630 --> 01:08:08.329
There was a nasty splat, but he didn’t seem
to react.

01:08:08.329 --> 01:08:13.520
The golf club was just embedded in his chest,
having broken the skin and sunken in.

01:08:13.520 --> 01:08:15.610
But there was no blood.

01:08:15.610 --> 01:08:17.839
Just dripping water.

01:08:17.839 --> 01:08:21.420
The father then pulled the golf club out of
his chest, and began beating Margaret’s

01:08:21.420 --> 01:08:27.089
mother to death with it, all the while repeating
“My house” again and again, while his

01:08:27.089 --> 01:08:30.759
wife and children watched with broad, sunny
smiles in the rain.

01:08:30.759 --> 01:08:35.270
Somehow, Margaret knew that her mother was
beyond saving, and that there was no way of

01:08:35.270 --> 01:08:39.109
defeating these things in a physical confrontation.

01:08:39.109 --> 01:08:43.089
All they could do was run out to Jared’s
van with the rest of the group and high tail

01:08:43.089 --> 01:08:44.460
it to the police station.

01:08:44.460 --> 01:08:49.720
But when they arrived at the station, the
doors were barred and it appeared empty.

01:08:49.720 --> 01:08:54.370
As the torrential rain hammered down from
above, there was nothing left to do but drive

01:08:54.370 --> 01:08:58.330
out of town and try to escape whatever madness
was going on here.

01:08:58.330 --> 01:09:01.130
But that was easier said than done.

01:09:01.130 --> 01:09:05.679
They drove for what seemed like hours on end
as the rain and the howling wind persisted.

01:09:05.679 --> 01:09:10.400
Jared had been injured during the fight with
the strange family and his health deteriorated

01:09:10.400 --> 01:09:12.630
further as the drive stretched on.

01:09:12.630 --> 01:09:16.931
They should have left the town of Clear Water
a long time ago, but it seemed like they were

01:09:16.931 --> 01:09:17.931
nowhere.

01:09:17.931 --> 01:09:22.560
It wasn’t long before Jared was lying dead
in the back of the van, and now, there were

01:09:22.560 --> 01:09:24.130
only four of them left.

01:09:24.130 --> 01:09:30.600
They kept driving - afraid, grieving, hungry,
and tired - and Margaret took the opportunity

01:09:30.600 --> 01:09:31.659
to sleep.

01:09:31.659 --> 01:09:36.980
It was no time to rest, but she was so exhausted
that she had no choice.

01:09:36.980 --> 01:09:39.460
Margaret had a continuation of her earlier
dream.

01:09:39.460 --> 01:09:43.930
The different her, the dream her, was laying
the plague-ridden body of her daughter in

01:09:43.930 --> 01:09:44.930
the river.

01:09:44.930 --> 01:09:46.420
But she wasn’t the only one.

01:09:46.420 --> 01:09:50.560
All the villages of her settlement were placing
the bodies of their dead in the river, as

01:09:50.560 --> 01:09:53.609
the water washed around them and through them.

01:09:53.609 --> 01:09:58.770
The bodies became one with the water, and
then, they became the water.

01:09:58.770 --> 01:10:00.880
The water was everything.

01:10:00.880 --> 01:10:05.120
When Margaret awoke, it was to the horrible
sounds of bubbling and boiling.

01:10:05.120 --> 01:10:08.280
That’s when she saw that Jared’s body
was...dissolving.

01:10:08.280 --> 01:10:11.690
No, not dissolving, evaporating.

01:10:11.690 --> 01:10:15.969
It was bubbling and convulsing, like it was
made of water, until the entire thing burst

01:10:15.969 --> 01:10:18.710
into a cascade of hot steam.

01:10:18.710 --> 01:10:23.460
After that, Margaret and the others left the
vehicle and refused to get back inside.

01:10:23.460 --> 01:10:25.300
Nothing was making sense.

01:10:25.300 --> 01:10:27.810
It was like something out of a nightmare.

01:10:27.810 --> 01:10:30.590
As they walked, the rain hammered down upon
them.

01:10:30.590 --> 01:10:34.330
They couldn’t have been walking for more
than a mile when they crashed into something.

01:10:34.330 --> 01:10:37.700
It was a sign - “Welcome to Clear Water.”

01:10:37.700 --> 01:10:40.770
It was like the town itself had drawn them
back.

01:10:40.770 --> 01:10:45.040
Mike refused to return to the town of his
own free will, and began walking in the other

01:10:45.040 --> 01:10:46.100
direction.

01:10:46.100 --> 01:10:50.270
Moments later, he was walking back towards
them in silence, though he’d never intended

01:10:50.270 --> 01:10:51.440
to.

01:10:51.440 --> 01:10:55.449
SCP-3300 had distorted his path, and brought
him back.

01:10:55.449 --> 01:11:00.400
It was clear that Mike was shaken to the core
by the experience, but they had to press on.

01:11:00.400 --> 01:11:04.160
They would head to the grocery store for food
and then to a sporting goods store where they

01:11:04.160 --> 01:11:09.409
could hopefully grab some guns to fight the
violent, altered people who’d somehow appeared

01:11:09.409 --> 01:11:10.590
with the rain.

01:11:10.590 --> 01:11:15.000
But things didn’t go to plan - or what little
plan there even was.

01:11:15.000 --> 01:11:19.670
Mike shot himself on the first night at Dirk’s
Sporting Goods, leaving only Margaret, Sam,

01:11:19.670 --> 01:11:20.980
and Isabel alive.

01:11:20.980 --> 01:11:25.080
Perhaps one of the most terrifying details
of Mike’s death was the fact he didn’t

01:11:25.080 --> 01:11:30.679
even bleed, instead, the gaping exit wound
in the back of his head was just full of water.

01:11:30.679 --> 01:11:33.560
Water was all that seemed to be left of them.

01:11:33.560 --> 01:11:37.380
Sam, seemingly driven to the edge by the sight
of Mike’s death, grabbed a hunting knife

01:11:37.380 --> 01:11:39.220
to perform an experiment.

01:11:39.220 --> 01:11:43.880
She cut into her own skin, and was horrified
to see only water dripping out.

01:11:43.880 --> 01:11:47.400
They’d all been “changed”, and they
didn’t know why.

01:11:47.400 --> 01:11:52.010
That’s when the survivors noticed something
else: There were people standing outside in

01:11:52.010 --> 01:11:53.890
the rain, hundreds of them.

01:11:53.890 --> 01:11:58.730
Not a single one they could recognize, all
new people.

01:11:58.730 --> 01:11:59.760
Waiting.

01:11:59.760 --> 01:12:04.640
Sam said only one word, “Outside”, before
walking out of the hunting goods store and

01:12:04.640 --> 01:12:08.810
disappearing into the crowd and the rain,
never to be seen again.

01:12:08.810 --> 01:12:12.820
Margaret mused that perhaps, in the end, she
had the right idea.

01:12:12.820 --> 01:12:16.590
To be taken, killed, erased, or changed would
be inevitable.

01:12:16.590 --> 01:12:21.659
In the final entry in Margaret’s diary,
dreams blend with reality as her mind finally

01:12:21.659 --> 01:12:23.429
gives out from the terror.

01:12:23.429 --> 01:12:27.710
She realizes, in her final moments, that there
is no way out.

01:12:27.710 --> 01:12:29.340
There is no escape.

01:12:29.340 --> 01:12:31.510
There is only water.

01:12:31.510 --> 01:12:33.030
Water is eternal.

01:12:33.030 --> 01:12:35.170
The rain is eternal.

01:12:35.170 --> 01:12:37.260
All will be changed.

01:12:37.260 --> 01:12:42.080
And given the fact that no trace of Margaret
was ever found, save for her diary, all her

01:12:42.080 --> 01:12:43.850
fears turned out to be right.

01:12:43.850 --> 01:12:49.580
She was taken and replaced by SCP-3300, just
as will inevitably happen to all the current

01:12:49.580 --> 01:12:54.469
citizens of Clear Water the next time SCP-3300
rolls around.

01:12:54.469 --> 01:12:59.300
It will be as inevitable and as indifferent
to those it affects as tomorrow’s sunrise.

01:12:59.300 --> 01:13:06.409
You cannot change the rain, but believe us,
in Clear Water, Montana, the rain can change

01:13:06.409 --> 01:13:07.409
you.

01:13:07.409 --> 01:13:09.719
“There’s a monster under my bed!”

01:13:09.719 --> 01:13:14.360
Almost every parent has heard their kids make
the claim, and it’s usually nothing more

01:13:14.360 --> 01:13:19.620
than some unusual shadows, or at worst a household
pest scurrying around.

01:13:19.620 --> 01:13:24.770
Parents usually tell the child to go back
to sleep, or maybe try to dispel their fears

01:13:24.770 --> 01:13:26.730
by shining a light under the bed.

01:13:26.730 --> 01:13:32.639
It’s a childhood rite of passage, and one
that usually passes soon enough.

01:13:32.639 --> 01:13:40.320
But for one young woman in Missouri, the monster
under her bed was very real - and very dangerous.

01:13:40.320 --> 01:13:46.650
SCP-3887-A doesn’t seem like she belongs
in a containment facility.

01:13:46.650 --> 01:13:51.449
She’s a twenty-four-year-old woman who lived
a quiet life in her hometown until things

01:13:51.449 --> 01:13:52.909
went horribly wrong.

01:13:52.909 --> 01:13:57.920
She doesn’t appear to possess any special
abilities and the Foundation is able to contain

01:13:57.920 --> 01:13:59.820
her without any difficulty.

01:13:59.820 --> 01:14:04.630
But wherever she goes, death and destruction
follow.

01:14:04.630 --> 01:14:09.989
It’s not her doing, but there is something
out there that will not stand to see her hurt

01:14:09.989 --> 01:14:11.440
in any way.

01:14:11.440 --> 01:14:16.080
Her personal monster under the bed is very
protective.

01:14:16.080 --> 01:14:19.760
Something another young woman found out the
hard way.

01:14:19.760 --> 01:14:26.880
Incident 3887-A-1 occurred in 2014, when the
young woman was attending a party with her

01:14:26.880 --> 01:14:27.880
girlfriend.

01:14:27.880 --> 01:14:32.030
Her partner was berating and humiliating her
in front of the guests, which was apparently

01:14:32.030 --> 01:14:34.810
not a rare occurrence in their relationship.

01:14:34.810 --> 01:14:40.450
Suddenly, something manifested under a nearby
table and before she could react, her girlfriend

01:14:40.450 --> 01:14:43.760
was brutally mauled by the unknown creature.

01:14:43.760 --> 01:14:47.820
Her limbs were completely severed from her
body, and died at the scene.

01:14:47.820 --> 01:14:52.870
An undercover SCP agent who was implanted
within the local authorities, made their way

01:14:52.870 --> 01:14:59.590
to the scene as soon as possible and found
SCP-3887-A in a state of shock.

01:14:59.590 --> 01:15:04.880
And who can blame her, after the encounter
she just had with what would come to be known

01:15:04.880 --> 01:15:06.739
as SCP-3887-B.

01:15:06.739 --> 01:15:16.790
While 3887-A is a normal human with no unusual
abilities or characteristics, 3887-B is anything

01:15:16.790 --> 01:15:18.290
but.

01:15:18.290 --> 01:15:22.620
Foundation scientists have described it as
a humanoid entity standing over seven feet

01:15:22.620 --> 01:15:23.670
tall.

01:15:23.670 --> 01:15:29.250
Its skin is greenish-grey, and it has two
long, sharp horns on its head.

01:15:29.250 --> 01:15:35.340
Its head and neck are covered in thick black
hair, and its eyes are a striking yellow color.

01:15:35.340 --> 01:15:40.830
Its mouth is full of sharp fangs similar to
that of a shark, and its elongated arms allow

01:15:40.830 --> 01:15:43.139
it to move on all fours.

01:15:43.139 --> 01:15:48.800
It has a long, hairless tail that resembles
a rat’s, and possesses both male and female

01:15:48.800 --> 01:15:50.660
reproductive organs.

01:15:50.660 --> 01:15:56.900
No one knows where it came from, but they
do have an idea why it’s sticking around.

01:15:56.900 --> 01:16:04.760
SCP-3887-B seems to be bonded to SCP-3887-A,
and can appear in any darkened area within

01:16:04.760 --> 01:16:06.960
a five-meter radius around her.

01:16:06.960 --> 01:16:13.250
While its favorite location is under 3887-A’s
bed, which has since been brought to the facility,

01:16:13.250 --> 01:16:18.650
it appears to be able to teleport wherever
she is, just as it did during the party when

01:16:18.650 --> 01:16:21.380
it made its presence brutally clear.

01:16:21.380 --> 01:16:26.770
It has odd eating patterns, and is able to
gain nourishment from practically any object,

01:16:26.770 --> 01:16:30.430
whether it resembles what we would consider
food or not.

01:16:30.430 --> 01:16:33.100
Its favorite treats for example?

01:16:33.100 --> 01:16:35.830
SCP-3887-A’s socks.

01:16:35.830 --> 01:16:41.280
But it does have one weakness that has been
useful in containing it - it can’t stand

01:16:41.280 --> 01:16:42.280
the light.

01:16:42.280 --> 01:16:49.070
And it doesn’t just hate it, when 3887-B
is exposed to bright light, it develops blisters

01:16:49.070 --> 01:16:52.960
and wounds and flees to the nearest dark area.

01:16:52.960 --> 01:16:58.600
SCP Foundation scientists are at a loss to
explain exactly what this creature is though,

01:16:58.600 --> 01:17:05.420
and SCP-3887-B seems to be a chimera of multiple
animals with multiple types of DNA.

01:17:05.420 --> 01:17:11.420
It possesses DNA similar to humans, but also
from a type of Oryx with similar horns, as

01:17:11.420 --> 01:17:16.060
well as a rat with the same type of tail,
as well as a common cane toad.

01:17:16.060 --> 01:17:20.670
And then there’s even some DNA that doesn’t
resemble any known creature in nature.

01:17:20.670 --> 01:17:25.600
Studying it further has been trickier though,
because it seems to have the effect of disrupting

01:17:25.600 --> 01:17:31.260
any electronic recording devices near it,
causing lasting damage if it’s in proximity

01:17:31.260 --> 01:17:33.090
to them for too long.

01:17:33.090 --> 01:17:38.530
There has been one bit of good news for SCP
Scientists though, because while it has shown

01:17:38.530 --> 01:17:43.380
that it can be extremely violent, it has not
attacked Foundation officials…

01:17:43.380 --> 01:17:45.040
Not yet at least.

01:17:45.040 --> 01:17:49.550
Its good behavior may not have anything to
do with how it personally feels about Foundation

01:17:49.550 --> 01:17:58.590
staff though, and is instead all thanks to
SCP-3887-A. 3887-A has been completely cooperative

01:17:58.590 --> 01:18:01.780
since she was taken into custody by the Foundation.

01:18:01.780 --> 01:18:08.330
She doesn’t perceive them as a threat, and
so far it seems like SCP-3887-B is following

01:18:08.330 --> 01:18:09.480
her lead.

01:18:09.480 --> 01:18:13.880
It has a strong emotional connection to the
young woman, and when they’re alone they

01:18:13.880 --> 01:18:16.550
show affectionate behavior towards each other.

01:18:16.550 --> 01:18:20.780
While the creature does not seem to like the
Foundation, it doesn’t seem like it wants

01:18:20.780 --> 01:18:25.370
to become hostile - unless the Foundation
gives it a reason to.

01:18:25.370 --> 01:18:30.530
When 3887-A was interviewed following the
tragic incident, by undercover Foundation

01:18:30.530 --> 01:18:34.020
Agent Bellamy, she was panicked and terrified.

01:18:34.020 --> 01:18:38.060
She admitted that her partner often treated
her badly, and believed that the creature

01:18:38.060 --> 01:18:40.100
was trying to protect her.

01:18:40.100 --> 01:18:44.880
She admitted that she had seen the creature
before, she even had a name for it, she called

01:18:44.880 --> 01:18:46.070
her Grenda.

01:18:46.070 --> 01:18:52.840
3887-A always thought she was crazy, now there
was proof though - she was not imagining the

01:18:52.840 --> 01:18:55.489
monster under her bed.

01:18:55.489 --> 01:18:59.620
Describing Grenda as her “boogeyman”,
the young woman talked about how she had known

01:18:59.620 --> 01:19:02.070
the creature since she was a child.

01:19:02.070 --> 01:19:06.150
She grew up in an old house in the country
that was full of strange sounds that made

01:19:06.150 --> 01:19:10.870
it sound like something was in her room with
her, and sometimes she would even catch a

01:19:10.870 --> 01:19:15.700
glimpse of what she thought was a monster
under her bed watching her.

01:19:15.700 --> 01:19:20.040
She tried telling her parents but they thought
she was making the whole thing up, and even

01:19:20.040 --> 01:19:25.920
she was forced to wonder if she was hallucinating
or had somehow imagined the whole thing.

01:19:25.920 --> 01:19:31.120
But then when she was a teenager, all of her
doubts were put to bed.

01:19:31.120 --> 01:19:38.160
One night 3887-A’s parents were loudly fighting,
a sadly not rare occurrence in their household,

01:19:38.160 --> 01:19:41.570
and she locked herself in her room to get
away from them.

01:19:41.570 --> 01:19:47.550
As she hid, Grenda emerged from under her
bed for the first time - and talked with her.

01:19:47.550 --> 01:19:52.270
And she isn’t the only one that Grenda is
willing to speak with, she’s also sat down

01:19:52.270 --> 01:19:55.920
for her own interviews with Foundation researchers.

01:19:55.920 --> 01:20:00.739
Well the researcher sat down, while Grenda
remained under the bed.

01:20:00.739 --> 01:20:05.730
Foundation Researcher Dr. Tanner interviewed
Grenda, who was cordial but guarded and remained

01:20:05.730 --> 01:20:09.620
deeply protective of the girl under her protection.

01:20:09.620 --> 01:20:16.960
She expressed feeling guilty for getting 3887-A
in trouble, but Dr. Tanner assured her that

01:20:16.960 --> 01:20:22.940
3887-A was not being punished and was being
kept at the Foundation for her own safety.

01:20:22.940 --> 01:20:27.540
He offered that they could keep Grenda safe
as well, but she responded that as long as

01:20:27.540 --> 01:20:32.210
3887-A remained safe, then she would be as
well.

01:20:32.210 --> 01:20:37.540
She explained that her kind fed on the anxiety
of children, which was why they lurked under

01:20:37.540 --> 01:20:38.780
their beds.

01:20:38.780 --> 01:20:43.670
She was apparently only supposed to remain
with this girl until she was ten or so, but

01:20:43.670 --> 01:20:48.590
became attached and decided to stay with her
which was against the rules of her people

01:20:48.590 --> 01:20:51.860
and as a result she had been exiled from her
home.

01:20:51.860 --> 01:20:56.750
At this point, Grenda offered to show herself
to the researcher and began to emerge from

01:20:56.750 --> 01:20:58.100
under the bed.

01:20:58.100 --> 01:21:04.699
Unfortunately, as has become standard when
attempting to document SCP-3887-B, all of

01:21:04.699 --> 01:21:10.560
the recording equipment malfunctioned and
was unable to record Grenda’s appearance.

01:21:10.560 --> 01:21:15.770
The Foundation continued to have questions
about this pair and their strange relationship,

01:21:15.770 --> 01:21:24.480
and interviewed SCP-3887-A again, this time
by a Dr. Garden.3887-A told Dr. Garden that

01:21:24.480 --> 01:21:29.850
she had been sleeping well and had been spending
lots of time talking to the entity under her

01:21:29.850 --> 01:21:30.850
bed.

01:21:30.850 --> 01:21:37.770
That led Dr. Garden to bring up a theory about
how 3887-B had come to exist.

01:21:37.770 --> 01:21:42.420
The young woman speculated that Grenda may
have been created from her fears.

01:21:42.420 --> 01:21:47.270
One of her first memories of being scared
was when she went to an aquarium and a massive

01:21:47.270 --> 01:21:52.620
bull shark came close to the glass where it
bared its rows and rows of shark teeth, the

01:21:52.620 --> 01:21:56.100
exact same kind of teeth that Grenda possessed.

01:21:56.100 --> 01:22:01.090
In fact all of the traits Grenda exhibited,
like her rat tail, seemed to connect to childhood

01:22:01.090 --> 01:22:03.949
fears that she had experienced.

01:22:03.949 --> 01:22:09.420
3887-A always felt alone as a little girl,
and she believed that she might have manifested

01:22:09.420 --> 01:22:14.639
Grenda as a companion who was there exactly
when she needed her to be.

01:22:14.639 --> 01:22:23.310
This raised the question of whether SCP-3887-B
really was the unnatural entity, or if SCP-3887-A

01:22:23.310 --> 01:22:26.840
is the source of the entity’s existence.

01:22:26.840 --> 01:22:32.530
The next interview with SCP-3887-B would raise
even more questions.

01:22:32.530 --> 01:22:39.580
When Dr. Garden went to interview SCP-3887-B,
it was clear the entity was agitated.

01:22:39.580 --> 01:22:45.190
Grenada became hostile as soon as Dr. Garden
entered the room, saying she was hungry and

01:22:45.190 --> 01:22:47.300
didn’t want to answer questions.

01:22:47.300 --> 01:22:53.920
When Dr. Garden said that 3887-A had provided
it with socks, the entity reacted with anger.

01:22:53.920 --> 01:22:56.340
The socks were just a snack.

01:22:56.340 --> 01:22:58.969
To live it needed fear.

01:22:58.969 --> 01:23:05.620
3887-B fed off human emotions - specifically
paranoia and anxiety.

01:23:05.620 --> 01:23:11.620
SCP-3887-A used to be full of them, but now
she was unusually calm in the facility and

01:23:11.620 --> 01:23:13.830
it was having a bad effect on her companion.

01:23:13.830 --> 01:23:19.750
When Dr. Garden promised to talk to supervisors,
the creature became more agitated - and reached

01:23:19.750 --> 01:23:24.389
out from under the bed, grabbing Dr. Garden
and pulling her under the bed.

01:23:24.389 --> 01:23:31.120
No one knew what would happen to Dr. Garden
under the bed and SCP-3887-A was quickly summoned

01:23:31.120 --> 01:23:36.739
to try to calm her companion down, but when
she called for Grenda, there was no response.

01:23:36.739 --> 01:23:41.470
It was feared that Dr. Garden had been lost
to the area under the bed that no one can

01:23:41.470 --> 01:23:46.880
access, but then thirteen minutes later, the
doctor suddenly emerged from under the bed.

01:23:46.880 --> 01:23:54.070
She was bruised, soaking wet, and missing
articles including shoes, socks, and her glasses.

01:23:54.070 --> 01:23:59.190
Later Interviews with Dr. Garden would give
the best picture yet of where SCP-3887-B comes

01:23:59.190 --> 01:24:00.190
from.

01:24:00.190 --> 01:24:06.490
Dr. Garden described being pulled under the
bed, which then led somewhere else entirely.

01:24:06.490 --> 01:24:13.650
She fell for fifteen seconds, still held by
SCP-3887-B, but when she landed she was alone

01:24:13.650 --> 01:24:18.500
in a large cave made of black rock with purple
gems in the walls.

01:24:18.500 --> 01:24:25.770
The cave contained a waterfall, a lake, and
what looked like SCP-3887’s secret home.

01:24:25.770 --> 01:24:31.570
It was filled with pictures of the girl she
was bonded to, a violin, some stuffed animals

01:24:31.570 --> 01:24:36.219
- and large piles of the girl’s socks.

01:24:36.219 --> 01:24:40.469
SCP-3887-B was there in the cave with her
too, watching her.

01:24:40.469 --> 01:24:45.420
She would catch glimpses of the creature - her
white fangs and her yellow eyes.

01:24:45.420 --> 01:24:50.091
She was terrified and ran screaming, trying
to find any way out of there as the creature

01:24:50.091 --> 01:24:51.230
pursued her.

01:24:51.230 --> 01:24:55.750
She couldn’t evade her forever though, and
eventually Grenda grabbed Dr. Garden.

01:24:55.750 --> 01:25:00.770
She was lifted into the air as Grenda bared
her shark like teeth, but instead of eating

01:25:00.770 --> 01:25:06.530
her, the creature instead took off the doctor’s
socks, and thanked her before somehow sending

01:25:06.530 --> 01:25:08.830
her back up into the darkness.

01:25:08.830 --> 01:25:14.600
She then found herself back under the bed,
surrounded by worried SCP personnel.

01:25:14.600 --> 01:25:21.080
Since then, SCP-3887-B has not brought anyone
else into its home, it seems feeding on Dr.

01:25:21.080 --> 01:25:26.800
Garden’s fear was enough for the time being,
and the situation has remained stable since.

01:25:26.800 --> 01:25:31.200
The SCP Foundation has been able to develop
relatively simple containment procedures for

01:25:31.200 --> 01:25:37.610
the two entities that make up SCP-3887, as
neither is currently hostile.

01:25:37.610 --> 01:25:43.389
The two are contained within a standard humanoid
containment cell with the bed at the center.

01:25:43.389 --> 01:25:48.440
SCP-3887-A is given standard amenities, a
healthy diet including a vitamin for some

01:25:48.440 --> 01:25:52.970
minor health issues, and her own control over
the lights in the cell.

01:25:52.970 --> 01:25:57.920
She has requested and been given a gaming
system for entertainment and up-to-date entertainment

01:25:57.920 --> 01:26:04.170
media but was denied access to the internet,
a pet cat, and access to the on-site recreation

01:26:04.170 --> 01:26:09.500
areas due to the risk of SCP-3887-B getting
loose.

01:26:09.500 --> 01:26:14.650
The facility does have plans in place in case
“Grenda” decides to become hostile again

01:26:14.650 --> 01:26:15.770
though.

01:26:15.770 --> 01:26:21.410
While SCP-3887-A normally maintains control
of the lights in her cell, the Foundation

01:26:21.410 --> 01:26:25.619
has a fail-safe installed so they can turn
them up at any time.

01:26:25.619 --> 01:26:31.580
Since SCP-3887-B reacts negatively to bright
light, the lights can be used as a security

01:26:31.580 --> 01:26:36.990
system to send her retreating back under the
bed until she can be pacified through other

01:26:36.990 --> 01:26:37.990
measures.

01:26:37.990 --> 01:26:43.640
While neither of the SCP-3887 entities appears
to be seeking to escape, it is impossible

01:26:43.640 --> 01:26:51.060
to predict where and how 3887-B would act
if 3887-A was free from her cell again, and

01:26:51.060 --> 01:26:57.119
whether she would attempt to harm those she
perceives as a threat to 3887-A as she did

01:26:57.119 --> 01:26:58.360
in the past.

01:26:58.360 --> 01:27:03.630
So for now, the Foundation is focused on keeping
both of them pacified - which, in the case

01:27:03.630 --> 01:27:08.800
of 3887-B, means a healthy supply of socks.

01:27:08.800 --> 01:27:14.250
But there’s one other lingering question
the Foundation hasn’t solved.

01:27:14.250 --> 01:27:19.480
SCP-3887-B referenced being exiled from its
kin for breaking the rules and was confined

01:27:19.480 --> 01:27:20.889
to a cave.

01:27:20.889 --> 01:27:25.950
That means there might be others like “Grenda”
out there - and they may be more aggressive

01:27:25.950 --> 01:27:28.260
and less scrupulous than she is.

01:27:28.260 --> 01:27:33.179
While no other specimens have been found,
the SCP Foundation will be keeping a careful

01:27:33.179 --> 01:27:37.440
eye on any reports of monsters lurking under
children’s beds.

01:27:37.440 --> 01:27:40.820
They might just be telling the truth.

01:27:40.820 --> 01:27:45.671
Lots of people believe in the possibility
of “past lives”, the notion that the life

01:27:45.671 --> 01:27:49.600
we are currently living is not our first.

01:27:49.600 --> 01:27:54.639
Before you were the person you are now, sitting
at home and watching this video, maybe you

01:27:54.639 --> 01:28:00.530
were a Medieval king, a Renaissance painter,
or an ancient Spartan warrior.

01:28:00.530 --> 01:28:06.020
Past Life Regression is a controversial practice
that allows people to look back at their supposed

01:28:06.020 --> 01:28:10.830
past lives, looking through the eyes of someone
in another lifetime.

01:28:10.830 --> 01:28:15.820
It’s a nice idea, and there’s something
exciting about the possibility of reliving

01:28:15.820 --> 01:28:19.420
the experiences of a person from the past.

01:28:19.420 --> 01:28:25.420
And wouldn’t you know it, the SCP Foundation
just so happened to discover an artifact that

01:28:25.420 --> 01:28:29.719
allows a person to experience another person’s
memories.

01:28:29.719 --> 01:28:35.070
It is not past life regression, and you have
no control over whose life you are peeking

01:28:35.070 --> 01:28:39.760
into, but it allows you to look at the world
through their eyes.

01:28:39.760 --> 01:28:45.179
However, when you look through someone else’s
eyes, there’s always the possibility that

01:28:45.179 --> 01:28:49.080
you will see something you didn’t want to.

01:28:49.080 --> 01:28:53.530
Something troubling, frightening, even traumatic.

01:28:53.530 --> 01:28:55.119
Or worse.

01:28:55.119 --> 01:29:02.960
So you may not want to subject yourself to
SCP-1123, or, as it has been ominously nicknamed,

01:29:02.960 --> 01:29:05.100
The Atrocity Skull.

01:29:05.100 --> 01:29:10.600
SCP-1123 is an old human skull with no teeth
or lower jaw.

01:29:10.600 --> 01:29:15.780
Across the forehead region of the skull, the
Khmer word for “remember” is written in

01:29:15.780 --> 01:29:16.780
blood.

01:29:16.780 --> 01:29:21.010
Testing of the skull and blood determined
it was from the 1970s, and that both the blood

01:29:21.010 --> 01:29:24.280
and skull belonged to the same person.

01:29:24.280 --> 01:29:30.090
The Atrocity Skull was discovered by a Colonel
in the Vietnamese People’s Army in the 1980s,

01:29:30.090 --> 01:29:35.159
as part of a collection of human remains displayed
in a Cambodian museum.

01:29:35.159 --> 01:29:39.830
Struck by the bloody writing, and the peculiar
feeling that the skull gave him, the Colonel

01:29:39.830 --> 01:29:43.040
decided to send it to Hanoi for further investigation.

01:29:43.040 --> 01:29:46.739
While in transit though, the skull was intercepted…

01:29:46.739 --> 01:29:48.619
by the SCP Foundation.

01:29:48.619 --> 01:29:54.860
Foundation Agents set a trap along the road,
blowing out the tires of the Colonel’s transportation.

01:29:54.860 --> 01:29:59.780
The skull was taken and sent to a Foundation
facility, and the Colonel was given an amnestic

01:29:59.780 --> 01:30:02.750
to remove all memory of the skull’s discovery.

01:30:02.750 --> 01:30:07.090
The staff of the Cambodian museum received
a similar treatment.

01:30:07.090 --> 01:30:12.800
All written mentions of the skull were erased,
and now outside of the Foundation’s archives,

01:30:12.800 --> 01:30:17.560
there is no official record of the skull ever
having existed.

01:30:17.560 --> 01:30:22.510
The bloody writing on the skull has faded
over time and from a distance is barely visible

01:30:22.510 --> 01:30:23.510
at all.

01:30:23.510 --> 01:30:28.660
The first SCP Foundation agent to study the
skull, an unknown researcher whose name has

01:30:28.660 --> 01:30:34.290
since been scrubbed from the Foundation archives,
had a series of unusual experiences while

01:30:34.290 --> 01:30:36.090
observing the skull.

01:30:36.090 --> 01:30:40.000
He reported that the script was invisible
from five meters away.

01:30:40.000 --> 01:30:45.520
As he approached it, he noted that the writing
became clearer with each meter he got closer

01:30:45.520 --> 01:30:49.480
until at one meter away, the writing looked
fresh.

01:30:49.480 --> 01:30:53.800
Unable to stop himself, he reached out to
touch it, and found that his fingers came

01:30:53.800 --> 01:30:56.360
away slick and red.

01:30:56.360 --> 01:31:03.200
Somehow, the bloody writing was still wet,
as if it had been drawn only moments before.

01:31:03.200 --> 01:31:08.310
As soon as he touched the text, he began to
experience anomalous sensory phenomena.

01:31:08.310 --> 01:31:13.300
The room filled with the smell of smoke, he
could hear the sound of heavy breathing, and

01:31:13.300 --> 01:31:15.130
the pounding of a heartbeat.

01:31:15.130 --> 01:31:20.480
There were thundering footsteps behind him,
and he turned to look, but found nothing there.

01:31:20.480 --> 01:31:25.320
He jerked his hand back away from the skull,
recoiling at the sensation of ants crawling

01:31:25.320 --> 01:31:27.160
over the back of his hand.

01:31:27.160 --> 01:31:32.989
His eyes began to sting, as if filled with
ash, and he stumbled backward, only to fall

01:31:32.989 --> 01:31:38.300
to the ground from a sudden stabbing sensation,
like a shard of glass piercing his shoe and

01:31:38.300 --> 01:31:39.720
the sole of his foot.

01:31:39.720 --> 01:31:44.020
The researcher was removed from the room and
examined by a physician, who found that none

01:31:44.020 --> 01:31:47.619
of these sensations had accompanying physical
symptoms.

01:31:47.619 --> 01:31:50.940
They were purely psychosomatic, so it seemed.

01:31:50.940 --> 01:31:54.670
There was nothing in his eyes, no wound on
his foot.

01:31:54.670 --> 01:32:00.180
Contact with the skull had caused him to experience
these physical stimuli, but it was all in

01:32:00.180 --> 01:32:01.180
his head.

01:32:01.180 --> 01:32:08.040
And this was far from the full extent of SCP-1123’s
impact on those who interacted with it.

01:32:08.040 --> 01:32:13.480
After several weeks untouched, the skull was
examined by yet another Foundation researcher.

01:32:13.480 --> 01:32:17.710
When she touched the surface of the skull
to lift it and take a closer look, she fell

01:32:17.710 --> 01:32:23.750
into a dissociative fugue state - a kind of
distressing altered state of consciousness.

01:32:23.750 --> 01:32:29.050
She became confused, disoriented, and wouldn’t
respond to her name.

01:32:29.050 --> 01:32:33.909
The skull was removed from her grasp as soon
as she became unresponsive, but this did nothing

01:32:33.909 --> 01:32:35.880
to return her to normal.

01:32:35.880 --> 01:32:40.280
The accompanying researchers simply had to
observe her and wait for her to wake up.

01:32:40.280 --> 01:32:45.540
Six hours later, when she finally did, she
recounted what she experienced after touching

01:32:45.540 --> 01:32:46.800
the skull.

01:32:46.800 --> 01:32:50.510
She claimed that she had seen the life of
another person in the time between touching

01:32:50.510 --> 01:32:53.260
the skull and returning to consciousness.

01:32:53.260 --> 01:32:58.590
She could recount details of this other person’s
life, describing places she had never been,

01:32:58.590 --> 01:33:03.420
events she had never witnessed, and even speaking
a language she had previously demonstrated

01:33:03.420 --> 01:33:05.020
no command of.

01:33:05.020 --> 01:33:09.730
The other researchers determined that the
person described actually had existed, though

01:33:09.730 --> 01:33:15.110
they had since passed away, and that all the
little details were too specific to be a simple

01:33:15.110 --> 01:33:16.239
coincidence.

01:33:16.239 --> 01:33:22.199
After this encounter with SCP-1123, several
other researchers experienced similarly traumatic

01:33:22.199 --> 01:33:23.610
fugue states.

01:33:23.610 --> 01:33:28.010
The Foundation was able to identify several
shared characteristics among those who touched

01:33:28.010 --> 01:33:31.790
the skull and experienced the life of another
person.

01:33:31.790 --> 01:33:36.160
All of the people whose memories were seen
by test subjects died before the subject was

01:33:36.160 --> 01:33:42.820
born, were a victim of violence or imprisonment,
died in a tragic or violent way by murder,

01:33:42.820 --> 01:33:49.020
starvation, or infection, and died as a result
of being targeted by a political movement.

01:33:49.020 --> 01:33:54.360
These patterns led to the coining of the SCP’s
nickname, The Atrocity Skull.

01:33:54.360 --> 01:33:59.880
It is a skull that forces those who touch
it to relive past atrocities.

01:33:59.880 --> 01:34:04.530
In order to further understand the nature
of the skull’s effects on test subjects

01:34:04.530 --> 01:34:09.550
and the nature of the lives it imprints on
them, a series of experiments were performed

01:34:09.550 --> 01:34:11.380
by the Foundation.

01:34:11.380 --> 01:34:16.720
Various people of differing cultural backgrounds
were exposed to the skull, in an attempt to

01:34:16.720 --> 01:34:21.760
determine what correlation, if any, there
is between someone exposed to the skull and

01:34:21.760 --> 01:34:25.480
the type of person whose memories they experience.

01:34:25.480 --> 01:34:31.110
In the first experiment, a man of Irish and
French ancestry was told to touch the skull.

01:34:31.110 --> 01:34:36.770
He immediately collapsed, and began to scream
in Armenian and resist any and all assistance

01:34:36.770 --> 01:34:38.639
from Foundation officers.

01:34:38.639 --> 01:34:43.070
When he returned to full consciousness, he
explained that he had taken on the memories

01:34:43.070 --> 01:34:49.489
of an Armenian farmer who was burned alive
by the Ottoman army in 1915 during the Armenian

01:34:49.489 --> 01:34:50.760
Genocide.

01:34:50.760 --> 01:34:55.469
During a different experiment, a man with
Haitian ancestry touched the skull.

01:34:55.469 --> 01:35:00.969
Just before touching it, he complained of
a chemical smell and a powerful itching sensation.

01:35:00.969 --> 01:35:04.170
After he touched it, he began to violently
cough.

01:35:04.170 --> 01:35:09.280
His fugue state lasted for 60 minutes, and
was characterized by confusion and a sudden

01:35:09.280 --> 01:35:11.650
ability to speak Kurdish.

01:35:11.650 --> 01:35:16.250
After waking up from the fugue state, the
man was able to describe the imprinted personality

01:35:16.250 --> 01:35:21.040
of an 85 year victim of a mustard gas attack
in Iraq in 1989.

01:35:21.040 --> 01:35:27.880
A third experiment involved a woman with Chinese
ancestry, who became unresponsive for over

01:35:27.880 --> 01:35:30.590
two hours after touching the skull.

01:35:30.590 --> 01:35:35.380
She was clearly distressed and began to loudly
weep as the time progressed.

01:35:35.380 --> 01:35:39.310
Once the two hours were up, she was able to
give an interview where she described her

01:35:39.310 --> 01:35:41.790
experience while in the fugue state.

01:35:41.790 --> 01:35:48.150
She experienced the life of a young Ukrainian
girl who died in 1932 as a result of violence

01:35:48.150 --> 01:35:50.780
at the hands of a Soviet brigade.

01:35:50.780 --> 01:35:54.850
Several other experiments were also conducted,
producing similar results.

01:35:54.850 --> 01:35:59.710
Each time, the subject would experience a
fugue state lasting from around an hour to

01:35:59.710 --> 01:36:02.320
upwards of six hours.

01:36:02.320 --> 01:36:06.199
The experiments allowed the Foundation to
determine some statistical patterns in the

01:36:06.199 --> 01:36:10.150
personalities and memories experienced by
test subjects.

01:36:10.150 --> 01:36:14.820
The more victims that can be attributed to
a historical event, the more likely it is

01:36:14.820 --> 01:36:19.770
that a test subject will experience the memories
of someone killed in that event.

01:36:19.770 --> 01:36:25.030
There is no apparent correlation between the
nationality of the test subject and the nationality

01:36:25.030 --> 01:36:28.380
of the person whose memories they will live
through.

01:36:28.380 --> 01:36:32.340
While there are no negative physical effects
on test subjects who have come into contact

01:36:32.340 --> 01:36:37.940
with the skull, there is a notable psychological
impact which can be attributed to the traumatic

01:36:37.940 --> 01:36:42.980
nature of the memories that they were exposed
to during the course of the experiment.

01:36:42.980 --> 01:36:47.600
Subjects have demonstrated bouts of grief
and depression, as well as struggles with

01:36:47.600 --> 01:36:48.860
survivor’s guilt.

01:36:48.860 --> 01:36:53.830
Though they themselves did not survive the
events that they witnessed, they feel as though

01:36:53.830 --> 01:36:54.830
they did.

01:36:54.830 --> 01:36:59.970
In an attempt to alleviate these psychological
effects, the Foundation administered several

01:36:59.970 --> 01:37:02.510
types of amnestics to test subjects.

01:37:02.510 --> 01:37:08.160
However, these were not effective and in many
cases, they were actively harmful.

01:37:08.160 --> 01:37:13.639
The SCP Foundation uses a variety of amnestic
compounds as a part of its work, but none

01:37:13.639 --> 01:37:18.720
of them were effective in treating test subjects
who had been exposed to SCP 1123.

01:37:18.720 --> 01:37:24.860
Class B Amnestics, or Regressive Retrograde,
remove the most recently formed memories from

01:37:24.860 --> 01:37:26.400
a person’s mind.

01:37:26.400 --> 01:37:32.200
When these were administered to SCP 1123 test
subjects, their own memories began to fade

01:37:32.200 --> 01:37:37.360
away, while the memories of their imprinted
personality remained intact.

01:37:37.360 --> 01:37:42.199
If the dosage was increased, only the memories
of the atrocity would remain.

01:37:42.199 --> 01:37:47.300
Other amnestics with similar functions yielded
similar, and equally troubling results.

01:37:47.300 --> 01:37:52.080
The wrong memories would disappear, and the
subject’s original personality would begin

01:37:52.080 --> 01:37:56.570
to give way to that of the person the skull
had imprinted on them.

01:37:56.570 --> 01:38:01.300
And so another type of amnestic was applied
in an attempt to solve this issue.

01:38:01.300 --> 01:38:06.719
Class E amnestics, or Ennui, do not remove
memories from the subject’s mind, but rather

01:38:06.719 --> 01:38:09.969
lessen the subject’s emotional response
to them.

01:38:09.969 --> 01:38:14.761
They are intended to weaken neural pathways
and remove the emotional component from a

01:38:14.761 --> 01:38:20.570
given memory, reducing the subject’s stress
or trauma response to the information of said

01:38:20.570 --> 01:38:21.570
memory.

01:38:21.570 --> 01:38:25.849
All of the science behind this class of amnestic
suggests that it would be beneficial to the

01:38:25.849 --> 01:38:32.020
test subjects involved in this research, but
for some reason they were still ineffective.

01:38:32.020 --> 01:38:36.771
The application of Class E amnestics to test
subjects following exposure to the Atrocity

01:38:36.771 --> 01:38:43.030
Skull only worsened the subject’s trauma
response, contributing to panic attacks, flashbacks,

01:38:43.030 --> 01:38:46.560
and other symptoms of severe Post-Traumatic
Stress Disorder.

01:38:46.560 --> 01:38:53.770
Eventually, the use of amnestics to benefit
these test subjects was abandoned entirely.

01:38:53.770 --> 01:38:57.349
Experimentation with the skull was placed
on hold until a beneficial treatment program

01:38:57.349 --> 01:39:00.320
for the test subjects could be established.

01:39:00.320 --> 01:39:06.380
Currently, to preserve the condition of the
skull and the writing on its surface, SCP-1123

01:39:06.380 --> 01:39:11.690
is kept contained in a hermetically sealed
container in an argon gas atmosphere.

01:39:11.690 --> 01:39:17.310
When it is removed from containment for experimentation
and testing, it is kept in light at no more

01:39:17.310 --> 01:39:23.889
than 50 lux, with the temperature inside the
container kept between 20 and 24 degrees Celsius,

01:39:23.889 --> 01:39:26.159
and 55% humidity.

01:39:26.159 --> 01:39:31.889
No one is permitted to handle the skull under
any circumstances except for controlled experimentation.

01:39:31.889 --> 01:39:38.500
There is a saying that says those who do not
learn from history are doomed to repeat it.

01:39:38.500 --> 01:39:44.550
As distressing as the experience of touching
SCP-1123 may be, perhaps there is a use for

01:39:44.550 --> 01:39:45.550
it.

01:39:45.550 --> 01:39:50.340
Confronting historical atrocities directly,
and looking through the eyes of their victims,

01:39:50.340 --> 01:39:55.290
is a stark reminder of all the evil that humanity
is capable of.

01:39:55.290 --> 01:40:00.150
Certainly the history reflected by the Atrocity
Skull, imprinted directly into the minds of

01:40:00.150 --> 01:40:04.040
all who touch it, will not be soon forgotten.

01:40:04.040 --> 01:40:08.980
Those who have touched it, those who speak
to them, and all who learn about the impact

01:40:08.980 --> 01:40:13.179
of the Atrocity Skull, should take care to
remember history.

01:40:13.179 --> 01:40:14.500
To learn from it.

01:40:14.500 --> 01:40:18.700
To make sure that these evils are never repeated
again.

01:40:18.700 --> 01:40:22.960
Perhaps, we will even reach a point where
we do not have to look through the eyes of

01:40:22.960 --> 01:40:25.790
the victims of institutionalized evil.

01:40:25.790 --> 01:40:28.699
We will simply have moved beyond it.

01:40:28.699 --> 01:40:32.969
Then, and only then, will it be time for the
skull to be destroyed.

01:40:32.969 --> 01:40:38.690
Until then, it remains preserved in the halls
of the SCP Foundation as a reminder that,

01:40:38.690 --> 01:40:45.770
amidst all of the horrors contained in those
walls, sometimes the greatest monster is us.

01:40:45.770 --> 01:40:49.580
For a moment, we want you to cast your mind
back to your childhood.

01:40:49.580 --> 01:40:54.010
A time when you weren’t as busy or burdened
with the pressures of life that come as you

01:40:54.010 --> 01:40:55.110
grow up.

01:40:55.110 --> 01:41:00.080
When you were carefree and had your whole
life ahead of you, nothing but potential and

01:41:00.080 --> 01:41:01.380
opportunity.

01:41:01.380 --> 01:41:06.679
A simpler time, when the highest award you
could achieve wasn’t a grade or a promotion,

01:41:06.679 --> 01:41:11.400
but something as simple as your mom or dad
pinning a drawing you did to the door of the

01:41:11.400 --> 01:41:12.400
refrigerator.

01:41:12.400 --> 01:41:14.330
Oh, to be a kid again, right?

01:41:14.330 --> 01:41:18.500
Then again, maybe returning to younger days
is better left as a fantasy.

01:41:18.500 --> 01:41:24.020
It’s hard to imagine that something so pure,
so simple and wholesome as a drawing on the

01:41:24.020 --> 01:41:28.150
fridge could ever be something dark, horrific
even.

01:41:28.150 --> 01:41:34.110
But then, you learn about SCP-683, and all
of a sudden returning to your childhood becomes

01:41:34.110 --> 01:41:37.400
something you hope never happens.

01:41:37.400 --> 01:41:44.489
SCP-683 is an anomaly with various parts to
it, so we’ll start with SCP-683-1.

01:41:44.489 --> 01:41:49.900
At first glance, it looks to be just an ordinary
refrigerator; to be more precise, it’s actually

01:41:49.900 --> 01:41:55.550
a 1953 Crosley Shelvador, for any of you fridge
experts out there who are curious about the

01:41:55.550 --> 01:41:59.530
exact make and model of SCP-683-1.

01:41:59.530 --> 01:42:04.040
For everyone else, picture the refrigerator
that Indiana Jones hid inside to miraculously

01:42:04.040 --> 01:42:07.580
survive a nuclear blast in Kingdom of the
Crystal Skull.

01:42:07.580 --> 01:42:13.159
I don’t know about you guys, but I’m feeling
nervous already.

01:42:13.159 --> 01:42:17.460
Like we said, at first glance you’d struggle
to spot anything out of the ordinary about

01:42:17.460 --> 01:42:23.000
this particular fridge, apart from maybe some
slight wear and tear on the outside.

01:42:23.000 --> 01:42:27.830
Inside though, it’s perfectly clean, kept
in perfect working condition for keeping food

01:42:27.830 --> 01:42:28.830
cool.

01:42:28.830 --> 01:42:32.770
But that’s the first weird thing about SCP-683-1.

01:42:32.770 --> 01:42:37.690
You see, despite the Foundation conducting
tests to deliberately make it messier, the

01:42:37.690 --> 01:42:43.090
fridge seems to have an inbuilt function that
you wouldn’t find in one from Home Depot.

01:42:43.090 --> 01:42:44.560
It can self-clean.

01:42:44.560 --> 01:42:49.370
Yes, that doesn’t sound all that impressive
- unless you’re a fridge owner yourself

01:42:49.370 --> 01:42:52.270
and know what a nightmare they can be to keep
clean.

01:42:52.270 --> 01:42:58.330
While it’s definitely weird, it’s not
the last of SCP-683-1’s anomalous properties.

01:42:58.330 --> 01:43:02.679
The next is the fact that the power cord of
this refrigerator ends with a plug that doesn’t

01:43:02.679 --> 01:43:05.560
match any known type of wall outlet.

01:43:05.560 --> 01:43:09.909
Seems even stranger, after all, who would
design a fridge that can’t even be plugged

01:43:09.909 --> 01:43:10.909
in, right?

01:43:10.909 --> 01:43:16.790
In fact, the SCP Foundation had to design
their very own completely one of a kind adapter

01:43:16.790 --> 01:43:22.360
to connect SCP-683-1 to an ordinary gas-powered
home generator.

01:43:22.360 --> 01:43:28.849
Once plugged in though, SCP-683-1 functions
exactly like you would expect any other refrigerator

01:43:28.849 --> 01:43:31.080
to… sort of.

01:43:31.080 --> 01:43:37.840
It’s about time we move on to SCP-683’s
second component, designated as SCP-683-2.

01:43:37.840 --> 01:43:43.540
Again, much like the fridge it is somehow
affixed to, at first look this part looks

01:43:43.540 --> 01:43:44.820
completely ordinary.

01:43:44.820 --> 01:43:49.880
It’s a drawing, created using felt pens
and pencils, presumably by a child between

01:43:49.880 --> 01:43:52.400
the ages of five and seven years old.

01:43:52.400 --> 01:43:56.489
There’s evidence of some moderate water
damage to the paper, but once again nothing

01:43:56.489 --> 01:43:58.730
all that strange to look at.

01:43:58.730 --> 01:44:03.040
Even the subject of this child’s drawing
is pretty mundane, just some scribbles of

01:44:03.040 --> 01:44:08.920
a pleasant mountainous landscape, a house,
a well, a dog, a figure wearing a chef’s

01:44:08.920 --> 01:44:13.460
toque and, of course, an anthropomorphic sun
with a smiley face.

01:44:13.460 --> 01:44:18.510
Now sure, that might not sound all that impressive,
but we would advise not to say anything like

01:44:18.510 --> 01:44:19.949
that out loud.

01:44:19.949 --> 01:44:24.639
Criticizing the drawing is a comment you might
wish you hadn’t made, just like when you

01:44:24.639 --> 01:44:29.910
fill our comment sections with dated Among
Us memes.

01:44:29.910 --> 01:44:34.860
Any person that makes any kind of negative
or disparaging remark about the SCP-683-2

01:44:34.860 --> 01:44:41.760
drawing, or tries to remove the paper from
the fridge door of SCP-683-1 will suffer a

01:44:41.760 --> 01:44:44.570
grim, horrific fate.

01:44:44.570 --> 01:44:49.369
The next time they try to eat anything, this
person will suffer immense, irreparable damage

01:44:49.369 --> 01:44:54.300
to their internal organs, along with their
skin and muscle tissue.

01:44:54.300 --> 01:45:00.130
This is intensely painful, causing the subject
agonizing pain as their organs and skin are

01:45:00.130 --> 01:45:01.489
melted down.

01:45:01.489 --> 01:45:06.100
The amount the person loses is equal to the
mass of food they’ve eaten; with each bite,

01:45:06.100 --> 01:45:08.570
they will lose more and more of their body.

01:45:08.570 --> 01:45:14.369
The painful process will not stop until they
have ingested 0.42 kilograms of food.

01:45:14.369 --> 01:45:18.660
Making this even worse, the process doesn’t
seem to target any organs that would kill

01:45:18.660 --> 01:45:20.320
the subject immediately.

01:45:20.320 --> 01:45:25.880
They’re made to suffer in excruciating pain,
punished with torture for daring to try and

01:45:25.880 --> 01:45:28.469
remove the drawing from the fridge.

01:45:28.469 --> 01:45:33.650
Any and all subjects will die within twenty-six
days of taking that final bite and thus losing

01:45:33.650 --> 01:45:35.770
the last piece of themselves.

01:45:35.770 --> 01:45:38.929
But, where do the body parts of these people
go?

01:45:38.929 --> 01:45:42.420
Surely, they don’t disappear, you must be
thinking.

01:45:42.420 --> 01:45:43.980
And you’d be right.

01:45:43.980 --> 01:45:50.820
In instances like this, the mystery third
component of SCP-683 is revealed.

01:45:50.820 --> 01:45:59.969
Referred to as SCP-683-3, a brown paper lunch
bag will manifest inside the SCP-683-1 fridge,

01:45:59.969 --> 01:46:04.310
containing a grim and grizzly assortment of
meals.

01:46:04.310 --> 01:46:10.599
On every occasion, the bag contains a sandwich,
with a pretty disgusting filling: the flesh

01:46:10.599 --> 01:46:16.080
and viscera of the last person who dared to
criticize the drawing on the refrigerator.

01:46:16.080 --> 01:46:20.760
There is also a plastic ziploc bag, in which
you’ll find the other half of the stolen

01:46:20.760 --> 01:46:26.429
organs and flesh of this unlucky person, along
with three chocolate chip cookies.

01:46:26.429 --> 01:46:31.580
Surprisingly, these are actually completely
normal cookies with no traces of DNA or other

01:46:31.580 --> 01:46:33.679
abnormalities to them.

01:46:33.679 --> 01:46:38.650
Every time, there is also one final item that
forms the contents of SCP-683-3, and that’s

01:46:38.650 --> 01:46:44.690
a note which reads “Be a good boy today”.

01:46:44.690 --> 01:46:49.350
This note bears the same handwriting as appears
on the outer surface of the paper bag, upon

01:46:49.350 --> 01:46:51.900
which a single name is written: Eric.

01:46:51.900 --> 01:46:57.060
Now, for those of you in the know about the
various anomalies of the SCP Foundation, that

01:46:57.060 --> 01:47:01.219
particular, unassuming name might sound very
familiar.

01:47:01.219 --> 01:47:07.480
It was the same name mentioned by another
anomaly, known as SCP-066.

01:47:07.480 --> 01:47:13.070
A brief bit of context for you, SCP-066 was
a living ball of yarn that displayed friendly

01:47:13.070 --> 01:47:15.280
behavior towards Foundation staff.

01:47:15.280 --> 01:47:20.340
However, during an experiment, a thread was
cut from SCP-066’s body.

01:47:20.340 --> 01:47:25.159
This caused the yarn to transform into a ball
of meat, with a pair of functional eyes protruding

01:47:25.159 --> 01:47:26.370
from it.

01:47:26.370 --> 01:47:31.610
SCP-066 became hostile, constantly asking
for an ‘Eric’ whenever someone gets too

01:47:31.610 --> 01:47:32.750
close to it.

01:47:32.750 --> 01:47:38.710
The same name, Eric, was also found carved
into the back of SCP-168, another anomaly

01:47:38.710 --> 01:47:41.810
encountered by the SCP Foundation.

01:47:41.810 --> 01:47:47.060
SCP-168 was an anomalous calculator, which
actually possessed some level of sentience

01:47:47.060 --> 01:47:49.409
and had the ability to communicate.

01:47:49.409 --> 01:47:51.170
So, who is Eric?

01:47:51.170 --> 01:47:57.110
Well, theories range far and wide, but there’s
no real definitive answer as to exactly who,

01:47:57.110 --> 01:47:59.429
or what Eric might be.

01:47:59.429 --> 01:48:04.291
Some claim he’s a reality-bending entity,
others posit he’s an SCP that the Foundation

01:48:04.291 --> 01:48:06.060
just doesn’t know about yet.

01:48:06.060 --> 01:48:11.780
Regardless, he’s connected to some intriguing
entities; a sentient calculator, a formerly

01:48:11.780 --> 01:48:17.220
friendly ball of yarn, and a fridge with a
child’s drawing on it that can steal people’s

01:48:17.220 --> 01:48:21.040
organs and put them in a lunch bag especially
for him.

01:48:21.040 --> 01:48:26.449
It would seem that Eric is a child, maybe
a schoolboy, possibly even the one responsible

01:48:26.449 --> 01:48:29.500
for the drawing on SCP-683.

01:48:29.500 --> 01:48:32.920
This child could even potentially be anomalous
in nature.

01:48:32.920 --> 01:48:38.000
Of course, this is all just rampant speculation
on our part, so it’s probably best to take

01:48:38.000 --> 01:48:39.870
all of that with a grain of salt.

01:48:39.870 --> 01:48:45.840
As we’ve said before, it’s just a theory
- an SCP Explained theory.

01:48:45.840 --> 01:48:51.920
Eric might just remain one of the Foundation’s
many unanswered mysteries for years to come.

01:48:51.920 --> 01:48:58.170
But if that answer doesn’t satisfy you,
then why don’t we go back to SCP-683.

01:48:58.170 --> 01:49:02.630
Maybe something in the fridge’s origin will
give us a further clue to the mystery of who

01:49:02.630 --> 01:49:03.790
Eric is.

01:49:03.790 --> 01:49:08.780
The fridge was first discovered by the SCP
Foundation in the storage unit of a Washington

01:49:08.780 --> 01:49:11.690
home, owned by a woman named Yolanda.

01:49:11.690 --> 01:49:17.170
As coincidence would have it, Yolanda was
a collector of vintage home furnishings, including

01:49:17.170 --> 01:49:21.170
refrigerators, which would probably explain
why she didn’t think to throw out such an

01:49:21.170 --> 01:49:24.530
old model of fridge from the 1950s.

01:49:24.530 --> 01:49:29.920
According to her, she found SCP-683 simply
left on a nearby street corner, with nobody

01:49:29.920 --> 01:49:34.030
around that could have left it there, or anyone
that could have possibly been transporting

01:49:34.030 --> 01:49:35.790
it to the local dump.

01:49:35.790 --> 01:49:40.420
To give her a hand moving the fridge, Yolanda
enlisted the help of her nephew, who agreed

01:49:40.420 --> 01:49:45.500
to step in and assist her in getting SCP-683
back to her house.

01:49:45.500 --> 01:49:50.420
Unfortunately, though, the nephew passed away
only two weeks later, apparently due to medical

01:49:50.420 --> 01:49:55.119
complications that came as the result of a
hernia according to his death certificate.

01:49:55.119 --> 01:49:59.119
Could Yolanda’s nephew have been the mysterious
and elusive Eric?

01:49:59.119 --> 01:50:03.000
Could something have happened to him after
his death that allowed him to become some

01:50:03.000 --> 01:50:04.140
kind of anomaly?

01:50:04.140 --> 01:50:10.670
Who’s to say, we can only guess and hope
that one day we might get a full answer.

01:50:10.670 --> 01:50:16.050
As to why Yolanda never suffered the effects
of SCP-683, she never actually tried to take

01:50:16.050 --> 01:50:19.820
the SCP-683-2 drawing down from the fridge.

01:50:19.820 --> 01:50:24.050
When asked why, she simply replied “It’s
a nice little picture, isn't it?

01:50:24.050 --> 01:50:25.860
Why take it down?”

01:50:25.860 --> 01:50:30.650
Maybe, just maybe, it might have even reminded
her of her nephew.

01:50:30.650 --> 01:50:35.230
It would have been a futile and foolish idea
for Yolanda to have even tried to remove the

01:50:35.230 --> 01:50:41.030
drawing at any rate, as any who try will suffer
that painful and horrifying process of losing

01:50:41.030 --> 01:50:45.250
their organs and having them appear in Eric’s
paper lunch bag.

01:50:45.250 --> 01:50:50.310
Even fire can’t remove the drawing from
the fridge, at least not permanently, suggesting

01:50:50.310 --> 01:50:54.949
that even the paper it is drawn on has its
own anomalous properties.

01:50:54.949 --> 01:51:01.829
On three separate occasions, the SCP Foundation
has attempted to test this, setting SCP-683-2

01:51:01.829 --> 01:51:04.460
on fire with nothing more than a match.

01:51:04.460 --> 01:51:09.900
Every time, the drawing was incinerated, burned
to ashes until there was nothing left.

01:51:09.900 --> 01:51:16.460
But, within sixty-eight hours, SCP-683-2 had
returned to its permanent fixture on the fridge

01:51:16.460 --> 01:51:19.869
door, as if nothing had happened.

01:51:19.869 --> 01:51:23.360
Interestingly though, the D Class members
of personnel that were instructed to burn

01:51:23.360 --> 01:51:28.969
the drawing didn’t suffer the usual anomalous
effects of SCP-683.

01:51:28.969 --> 01:51:34.640
A similar thing happens if multiple people
attempt to remove SCP-683-2 or say anything

01:51:34.640 --> 01:51:36.500
negative towards the drawing.

01:51:36.500 --> 01:51:41.500
In cases like this, only the very first person
who made a disparaging remark, or tried to

01:51:41.500 --> 01:51:46.790
rip the drawing from the fridge will be the
one to suffer a long, painful torture by organ

01:51:46.790 --> 01:51:49.510
removal, followed swiftly by death.

01:51:49.510 --> 01:51:53.860
Now, if you cast your mind back to earlier
in the video, we told you that someone who

01:51:53.860 --> 01:52:00.600
tries removing or disparages SCP-683-2 will
only suffer an anomalous lack of organs when

01:52:00.600 --> 01:52:02.040
they next eat something.

01:52:02.040 --> 01:52:07.780
So, you must be thinking that the way to avoid
that is to simply not eat, to fast, and not

01:52:07.780 --> 01:52:09.800
ingest a single meal.

01:52:09.800 --> 01:52:14.219
And yes, you’d be right, that does stave
off the anomalous effects of the fridge and

01:52:14.219 --> 01:52:19.920
the drawing, but also means you’re heading
towards an even slower, painful death from

01:52:19.920 --> 01:52:21.540
starvation.

01:52:21.540 --> 01:52:25.679
To date, two different Foundation test subjects
have died this way by refusing to eat after

01:52:25.679 --> 01:52:27.600
interacting with SCP-683.

01:52:27.600 --> 01:52:33.210
True, the SCP Foundation is most likely sitting
on a whole cavalcade of different anomalies

01:52:33.210 --> 01:52:38.510
that can keep a person alive without the need
for food, but you know what they’re like,

01:52:38.510 --> 01:52:39.510
right?

01:52:39.510 --> 01:52:44.099
The Foundation’s hardly likely to share
the keys to surviving without having to eat.

01:52:44.099 --> 01:52:47.389
And there you have it, folks, that’s SCP-683.

01:52:47.389 --> 01:52:51.429
Don’t worry, it’s highly unlikely that
you’ll ever encounter it.

01:52:51.429 --> 01:52:56.980
The Foundation keeps it under lock and key,
in a cell fitted with a steel door and reinforced

01:52:56.980 --> 01:52:58.220
hinges.

01:52:58.220 --> 01:53:03.369
SCP-683 remains covered in a large cloth to
prevent any members of personnel from looking

01:53:03.369 --> 01:53:07.989
at it when the fridge isn’t being used for
research or experiments.

01:53:07.989 --> 01:53:13.489
But you have to wonder, what if it’s not
the only fridge with these anomalous properties?

01:53:13.489 --> 01:53:18.989
After all, it’s rare for a manufacturer
to make just a single refrigerator of a certain

01:53:18.989 --> 01:53:19.989
model.

01:53:19.989 --> 01:53:23.800
Maybe you’d better be wary next time you
visit someone with an older model of fridge

01:53:23.800 --> 01:53:30.650
in their kitchen, and just to be safe, if
there’s a drawing pinned to the front door,

01:53:30.650 --> 01:53:32.120
leave it where it is.

01:53:32.120 --> 01:53:35.980
Sometimes, dealing with anomalies that could
destroy the world with a flick of their wrist

01:53:35.980 --> 01:53:37.530
can get a little old.

01:53:37.530 --> 01:53:41.940
Sure, it definitely wouldn’t be a good thing
if the Devourer of Worlds...Well, devoured

01:53:41.940 --> 01:53:47.990
the world, or if SCP-001 - When Day Breaks
- turned us all into weird, melty zombies.

01:53:47.990 --> 01:53:52.360
But it’s almost impossible to conceive the
sheer scale of destruction that an XK-Class

01:53:52.360 --> 01:53:54.929
End of the World Scenario would cause.

01:53:54.929 --> 01:53:58.719
You’d be almost numb to it, if you even
survived.

01:53:58.719 --> 01:54:04.840
In the words of SCP-2430 creator Josef Stalin,
“The death of one man is a tragedy.

01:54:04.840 --> 01:54:07.300
The death of millions is a statistic.”

01:54:07.300 --> 01:54:11.570
Okay, he didn’t actually say that, but it’s
an appropriate quote either way.

01:54:11.570 --> 01:54:15.400
Today, we’re talking about a much smaller,
pettier kind of evil.

01:54:15.400 --> 01:54:20.750
Sure, this anomaly can kill people - and has,
many, many times, in fact - but where it really

01:54:20.750 --> 01:54:26.210
gets its kicks, is in making you feel like
crap on a more emotional level.

01:54:26.210 --> 01:54:32.920
It’s SCP-056: Ironically known by the nickname,
“A Beautiful Person”, because on the inside,

01:54:32.920 --> 01:54:36.489
this self-obsessed monster is anything but
beautiful.

01:54:36.489 --> 01:54:40.180
This crafty creature spent what potentially
could have been hundreds of years around humans

01:54:40.180 --> 01:54:45.710
before the SCP Foundation eventually located
and apprehended it, meaning you may have even

01:54:45.710 --> 01:54:49.570
run into it at some point or another before
it was rightfully imprisoned.

01:54:49.570 --> 01:54:52.140
How do you know if you had a brush with SCP-056?

01:54:52.140 --> 01:54:57.370
Well, it’s difficult to know for sure, but
perhaps the biggest indicator is that it probably

01:54:57.370 --> 01:54:59.400
annoyed the living hell out of you.

01:54:59.400 --> 01:55:05.480
You see, SCP-056 is a sentient shapeshifter
with a subtle mind-warping ability, whose

01:55:05.480 --> 01:55:09.810
entire reason for existence is using those
abilities to make everyone around them feel

01:55:09.810 --> 01:55:11.670
incredibly inadequate.

01:55:11.670 --> 01:55:17.370
They don’t have any kind of consistent or
“true” form, only a consistent ethos - And

01:55:17.370 --> 01:55:22.239
that ethos is “Anything you can do, I can
do better.”

01:55:22.239 --> 01:55:25.190
And we mean this in its most literal sense.

01:55:25.190 --> 01:55:30.680
Whenever SCP-056 is left with a person, an
animal, or even an object, the second all

01:55:30.680 --> 01:55:35.360
eyes are taken off of it, it’ll become a
slightly better version of whatever it’s

01:55:35.360 --> 01:55:36.360
encountering.

01:55:36.360 --> 01:55:41.320
If the thing in question is capable of thinking
or feeling, it will not feel good about this

01:55:41.320 --> 01:55:42.320
development.

01:55:42.320 --> 01:55:46.389
Just like we said, it’s probably not going
to bring the world to its knees, but it sure

01:55:46.389 --> 01:55:50.079
would suck to know SCP-056.

01:55:50.079 --> 01:55:55.060
Its lack of a consistent form makes SCP-056
a little difficult to think about visually

01:55:55.060 --> 01:56:00.230
- Which was also the reason it was so hard
to catch - but for the sake of consistency,

01:56:00.230 --> 01:56:05.210
we’ll present it here with one of its favorite
forms: A woman who’s a real dead ringer

01:56:05.210 --> 01:56:15.070
for “perfection” - famous actress Scarlett
Johanssen, of Black Widow fame.

01:56:15.070 --> 01:56:19.900
So what is it really like to experience SCP-056’s
anomalous effects first-hand?

01:56:19.900 --> 01:56:24.740
Well, we’ll take you through a little crash-course
in anomalous insecurity and frustration.

01:56:24.740 --> 01:56:29.400
Let’s say that this creature, in human form,
is one of your co-workers.

01:56:29.400 --> 01:56:33.719
When the Foundation discovered it, it was
working in the fashion industry, but who knows

01:56:33.719 --> 01:56:35.780
what job it could have held before then?

01:56:35.780 --> 01:56:40.079
If it worked in your office, it was probably
that one irritating coworker who always wore

01:56:40.079 --> 01:56:45.090
nicer clothes than you, had a brighter, whiter
smile, and much better hair.

01:56:45.090 --> 01:56:49.639
While you were thanklessly toiling away on
the reports for the latest financial quarter,

01:56:49.639 --> 01:56:54.910
056 was schmoozing with your boss on golf
lunches, scoring perfect games and promotions

01:56:54.910 --> 01:56:57.420
one “hole in one” at a time.

01:56:57.420 --> 01:57:00.450
Of course, they tell you about it at the water
cooler.

01:57:00.450 --> 01:57:04.260
Like everyone who’s feeling inadequate,
maybe you buy yourself a new car.

01:57:04.260 --> 01:57:08.320
A vintage Cadillac convertible that makes
you look more like a gangster than an office

01:57:08.320 --> 01:57:09.320
drone.

01:57:09.320 --> 01:57:10.320
Awesome!

01:57:10.320 --> 01:57:12.550
That’ll make all those feelings that you’re
not good enough go away.

01:57:12.550 --> 01:57:17.639
You even buy yourself a stylish pair of sunglasses,
and start cruising around town with the top

01:57:17.639 --> 01:57:21.099
down, hoping that everyone sees how cool you
are now.

01:57:21.099 --> 01:57:25.739
But when you’re stopped at a stop light,
you see something approaching in the lane

01:57:25.739 --> 01:57:26.900
next to you.

01:57:26.900 --> 01:57:31.119
It’s the latest Rolls Royce, in jet black.

01:57:31.119 --> 01:57:37.400
And who would be behind the wheel but SCP-056,
in Armani shades that are much nicer than

01:57:37.400 --> 01:57:38.400
yours.

01:57:38.400 --> 01:57:43.010
It grins and nods to you in the mirrors, and
you can feel your soul shriveling up inside

01:57:43.010 --> 01:57:46.840
you, only to be replaced by rage and resentment.

01:57:46.840 --> 01:57:51.050
Maybe later that month, you and all your co-workers
are at a bar, enjoying drinks.

01:57:51.050 --> 01:57:56.550
Of course, SCP-056 is the best dressed one
there, and is telling all the most interesting

01:57:56.550 --> 01:57:57.550
stories.

01:57:57.550 --> 01:58:02.489
Your jokes don’t get any laughs, but 056
is bringing down the house with every word.

01:58:02.489 --> 01:58:05.489
Feeling ignored, you decide to get everyone
a round on you.

01:58:05.489 --> 01:58:11.370
056 is a designated driver in its new Rolls
Royce, so you just decide to get them a Pepsi

01:58:11.370 --> 01:58:12.370
instead.

01:58:12.370 --> 01:58:16.159
However, by the time you return to their stool,
they’re nowhere to be seen.

01:58:16.159 --> 01:58:21.889
A tall glass of Coca Cola with ice cubes is
sitting on the bar next to their seat.

01:58:21.889 --> 01:58:26.050
Perhaps one day you finally snap and decide
you can’t take it anymore.

01:58:26.050 --> 01:58:31.440
You’ll meet SCP-056 after work and put this
showboating jerk in its place at long last.

01:58:31.440 --> 01:58:35.409
You sneak up on it in an alley with a knife
in your palm and swing for it, but your blade

01:58:35.409 --> 01:58:37.510
never makes contact.

01:58:37.510 --> 01:58:42.349
SCP-056 unleashes some high-level Jiu-Jitsu
move on you, easily knocks the knife from

01:58:42.349 --> 01:58:44.650
your hands, and beats the living hell out
of you.

01:58:44.650 --> 01:58:48.820
When you’re later convicted of attempted
murder, all you can do is scream “They made

01:58:48.820 --> 01:58:50.239
me do it!”

01:58:50.239 --> 01:58:53.450
Again and again in your prison cell.

01:58:53.450 --> 01:58:55.969
Envy can do crazy things to a person.

01:58:55.969 --> 01:58:57.550
But there’s more!

01:58:57.550 --> 01:59:03.460
Really, if you lose your mind from an encounter
with SCP-056, you still haven’t done too

01:59:03.460 --> 01:59:04.460
badly.

01:59:04.460 --> 01:59:10.110
While its methods of attack are more commonly
psychological, as we alluded to earlier, SCP-056

01:59:10.110 --> 01:59:14.930
is definitely not above committing some pretty
horrifying acts of violence.

01:59:14.930 --> 01:59:19.610
SCP-056 was discovered in its clothing design
job after causing an unusually high number

01:59:19.610 --> 01:59:23.929
of murders, suicides, and mental breakdowns
among its coworkers.

01:59:23.929 --> 01:59:28.520
However, things took an even more unpleasant
turn when the Foundation sent personnel to

01:59:28.520 --> 01:59:30.079
detain it.

01:59:30.079 --> 01:59:35.400
SCP-056 reacted poorly to this show of potential
force, and turned into something even more

01:59:35.400 --> 01:59:39.250
dangerous than the Foundation planned for
in getting it under control.

01:59:39.250 --> 01:59:43.969
We don’t know exactly what it transformed
into due to SCP Foundation redactions, but

01:59:43.969 --> 01:59:49.480
our guesses for what it transformed into would
either be a giant monster, a Rambo-esque unstoppable

01:59:49.480 --> 01:59:53.510
super-soldier, or something like one of those
huge killer robots from Robocop.

01:59:53.510 --> 01:59:58.659
Pick your favorite down there in the comments,
but whatever the case, it caused the unfortunate

01:59:58.659 --> 02:00:02.440
deaths of seventeen agents and ten civilians.

02:00:02.440 --> 02:00:06.440
The incident was blamed on an employee at
the company going postal and deciding to kill

02:00:06.440 --> 02:00:11.199
a bunch of innocents, which...Technically
wasn’t untrue?

02:00:11.199 --> 02:00:16.489
Not long after, Foundation operatives were
able to tranquilize SCP-056.

02:00:16.489 --> 02:00:20.800
Perhaps you think this nasty little monster
decided to mellow out a little bit after being

02:00:20.800 --> 02:00:24.699
contained, but if you did think that, I’m
afraid you’d be dead wrong.

02:00:24.699 --> 02:00:29.960
It just decided to start terrorizing Foundation
staff with its infuriating anomalous abilities

02:00:29.960 --> 02:00:30.960
instead.

02:00:30.960 --> 02:00:33.170
Wait until you see this!

02:00:33.170 --> 02:00:38.679
Compared to a lot of entities locked up at
the SCP Foundation, SCP-056 really lives in

02:00:38.679 --> 02:00:40.120
the lap of luxury.

02:00:40.120 --> 02:00:44.969
It has a well-furnished room, easy access
to members of staff, and is given permission

02:00:44.969 --> 02:00:50.710
to interact with any object it desires - As
long as those objects aren’t anomalous.

02:00:50.710 --> 02:00:54.989
Why is this Euclid-Class anomaly with over
seventeen dead Foundation staff members to

02:00:54.989 --> 02:00:56.820
its name given so much leeway?

02:00:56.820 --> 02:01:02.460
Well, to answer that, remember the ethos:
“Anything you can do, I can do better.”

02:01:02.460 --> 02:01:07.100
And this holds true, whether we’re talking
physical appearance or one’s capacity to

02:01:07.100 --> 02:01:09.429
commit tremendous acts of violence.

02:01:09.429 --> 02:01:14.621
The Foundation is forced to cater to most
of SCP-056’s whims, or it’ll become a

02:01:14.621 --> 02:01:19.079
hell of a lot more dangerous in response to
any kind of external resistance.

02:01:19.079 --> 02:01:20.079
See?

02:01:20.079 --> 02:01:23.469
We told you it’d suck to have to know this
thing, and nobody knows that better than the

02:01:23.469 --> 02:01:28.930
employees of the SCP Foundation who are forced
to interact with it on a daily basis for containment

02:01:28.930 --> 02:01:30.190
and testing.

02:01:30.190 --> 02:01:33.840
First, let’s take a look at some of the
forms it’s occupied since it began its time

02:01:33.840 --> 02:01:35.260
at the SCP Foundation.

02:01:35.260 --> 02:01:41.490
When a researcher brought in their beloved
pooch, SCP-056 decided to flex on it by becoming

02:01:41.490 --> 02:01:44.000
a beautiful, well-groomed labrador retriever.

02:01:44.000 --> 02:01:49.020
When younger female staff passed it, it decided
to once again take on its Scarlett Johanssen

02:01:49.020 --> 02:01:50.020
form.

02:01:50.020 --> 02:01:54.119
When speaking to a group of other researchers
about intelligence, it became a female researcher

02:01:54.119 --> 02:01:59.120
with an IQ score thirty points higher than
the top-scoring human researcher on site.

02:01:59.120 --> 02:02:03.500
When it took a trip to the containment site’s
gym, where the guards and mobile task forces

02:02:03.500 --> 02:02:08.619
exercise and train, it decided to take its
flexes to a more literal level.

02:02:08.619 --> 02:02:13.219
It transformed into a ripped, hunky bodybuilder,
who strutted into the middle of the gym and

02:02:13.219 --> 02:02:16.679
bench-pressed 250 kilos, no problem.

02:02:16.679 --> 02:02:20.829
This was thirty kilos more than the strongest
human guard working at the site.

02:02:20.829 --> 02:02:26.040
Its commitment to being the best is so great
that when left alone in its containment chamber,

02:02:26.040 --> 02:02:30.220
it will sometimes literally transform into
a nicer couch than the one the Foundation

02:02:30.220 --> 02:02:31.220
provided for it.

02:02:31.220 --> 02:02:33.440
Doesn’t it just make your blood boil?

02:02:33.440 --> 02:02:35.780
But wait, there’s more!

02:02:35.780 --> 02:02:39.820
Just in case this wasn’t absurd enough,
the Foundation felt like testing the limits

02:02:39.820 --> 02:02:41.290
of its anomalous abilities.

02:02:41.290 --> 02:02:47.570
In particular, they were extremely eager to
see if 056 had a secret default form.

02:02:47.570 --> 02:02:51.929
They left it alone with a single security
camera in order to observe what it transformed

02:02:51.929 --> 02:02:54.060
into when not being observed.

02:02:54.060 --> 02:02:55.739
And can you guess what happened?

02:02:55.739 --> 02:03:00.560
It turned into an even higher-quality security
camera, and stared back.

02:03:00.560 --> 02:03:05.461
While the transformations can only take place
while 056 isn’t being observed, it’s very

02:03:05.461 --> 02:03:09.989
astute at creating periods where it can’t
be seen or interacted with.

02:03:09.989 --> 02:03:14.460
Vision or camera feeds have been known to
briefly go foggy in order to facilitate a

02:03:14.460 --> 02:03:15.460
transformation.

02:03:15.460 --> 02:03:20.460
It’s fitting that 056, being the ultimate
diva, will only ever let people look at it

02:03:20.460 --> 02:03:22.150
on its own terms.

02:03:22.150 --> 02:03:26.970
It also seems to get off on causing shame
- and the degree to which that statement is

02:03:26.970 --> 02:03:31.400
metaphorical is, well, open to interpretation.

02:03:31.400 --> 02:03:35.460
Staff members made insecure by its antics
feel compelled to enter its cell and verbally

02:03:35.460 --> 02:03:40.820
berate it, at which point 056 will shame them
even harder, and send them out with their

02:03:40.820 --> 02:03:42.570
tail between their legs.

02:03:42.570 --> 02:03:47.020
It’s like every toxic friend rolled into
one nasty package.

02:03:47.020 --> 02:03:52.960
Curious as to what else SCP-056 was capable
of, the Foundation conducted a few other tests

02:03:52.960 --> 02:03:56.220
between SCP-056 and their personnel.

02:03:56.220 --> 02:04:01.010
Here, they discovered that 056 seemed incredibly
responsive to intent.

02:04:01.010 --> 02:04:06.560
When a D-Class was sent in with a knife and
the intent to kill, 056 transformed into a

02:04:06.560 --> 02:04:09.830
lean, athletic man, before disarming and killing
the D-Class.

02:04:09.830 --> 02:04:14.099
A somewhat attractive D-Class female was sent
in with a bottle of wine.

02:04:14.099 --> 02:04:18.579
056 became a beautiful woman and accepted
the wine, before taking a sip, and spitting

02:04:18.579 --> 02:04:21.140
it back into the D-Class’ face.

02:04:21.140 --> 02:04:25.400
A mixed-gender pair of D-Classes were sent
in next with no real intent.

02:04:25.400 --> 02:04:30.059
056 became an attractive woman in a well-tailored
business suit, who looked over the pair before

02:04:30.059 --> 02:04:31.849
kicking them both out.

02:04:31.849 --> 02:04:34.480
Ten male D-Classes were sent in after that.

02:04:34.480 --> 02:04:39.250
056 turned into a beautiful woman in a low-cut
dress, and simply waited until the ten men

02:04:39.250 --> 02:04:44.449
were driven mad with desire and began physically
fighting one another for her affection.

02:04:44.449 --> 02:04:48.639
She watched them doing this for seven minutes
before laughing and leaving the simp squadron

02:04:48.639 --> 02:04:50.260
to duke it out alone.

02:04:50.260 --> 02:04:54.460
In another test, a female staff member with
Level 4 clearance, who was also judged to

02:04:54.460 --> 02:04:59.469
be the most attractive woman on site - which
seems like an HR issue that the Ethics Committee

02:04:59.469 --> 02:05:03.790
should probably look into - was sent into
056’s testing chamber.

02:05:03.790 --> 02:05:10.320
056 became, quote, “An extremely aesthetically
pleasing woman, who displayed a large lexicon

02:05:10.320 --> 02:05:12.739
and understanding of management skills.”

02:05:12.739 --> 02:05:13.739
Unquote.

02:05:13.739 --> 02:05:17.920
The two spoke for around 90 minutes until
the Level 4 staff member stormed out in a

02:05:17.920 --> 02:05:18.920
rage.

02:05:18.920 --> 02:05:24.079
Recently, 056 has requested access to the
internet, saying that the Foundation has been

02:05:24.079 --> 02:05:28.280
unable to provide it with enough sycophants,
and that via the internet, the whole world

02:05:28.280 --> 02:05:30.730
will be able to see its face.

02:05:30.730 --> 02:05:36.780
If ever 056 got onto YouTube and transformed
into a more successful SCP Channel, I just

02:05:36.780 --> 02:05:39.040
don’t think we’d be able to take it!

02:05:39.040 --> 02:05:41.889
Thankfully, this request was denied.

02:05:41.889 --> 02:05:45.820
Legends about the end of the world often come
with the sounds of thundering hooves, and

02:05:45.820 --> 02:05:47.590
the approach of Four Horsemen.

02:05:47.590 --> 02:05:48.590
War.

02:05:48.590 --> 02:05:49.590
Famine.

02:05:49.590 --> 02:05:50.590
Pestilence.

02:05:50.590 --> 02:05:51.590
Death.

02:05:51.590 --> 02:05:55.290
They will descend on the world and usher in
the end of days.

02:05:55.290 --> 02:06:01.020
It’s a terrifying idea, these horsemen bringing
darkness and decay wherever they go, as the

02:06:01.020 --> 02:06:03.120
world collapses all around them.

02:06:03.120 --> 02:06:07.190
We all hope that we’ll never see the day
that the Four Horsemen come.

02:06:07.190 --> 02:06:11.860
Unfortunately, some unlucky people out there
have already encountered their own version

02:06:11.860 --> 02:06:18.369
of the Horsemen of the Apocalypse, shadowy
riders with inhuman strength that follow disaster,

02:06:18.369 --> 02:06:21.010
destruction, and untold suffering.

02:06:21.010 --> 02:06:26.170
The SCP Foundation came across a series of
journal entries written by Dave Harkand, an

02:06:26.170 --> 02:06:31.909
infantryman in the British Expeditionary Force
during World War I. That first World War was

02:06:31.909 --> 02:06:38.340
a nightmare for all who fought in it, a sea
of bloodshed and gunfire, young men crouched

02:06:38.340 --> 02:06:43.140
terrified in foxholes and wondering when death
would finally come for them.

02:06:43.140 --> 02:06:49.150
The horrors of war are notable, but not exactly
the sort of thing the SCP Foundation preoccupies

02:06:49.150 --> 02:06:50.510
itself with.

02:06:50.510 --> 02:06:56.690
So what was so captivating, so specifically
terrible, about Dave Harkand’s journals?

02:06:56.690 --> 02:07:01.440
They described his experiences over the course
of The Battle of the Somme, and an anomaly

02:07:01.440 --> 02:07:06.070
he encountered there that was unlike anything
he had ever seen.

02:07:06.070 --> 02:07:11.650
No military training, no combat experience,
could have prepared him for what was waiting,

02:07:11.650 --> 02:07:13.690
hiding in the fog of war.

02:07:13.690 --> 02:07:18.760
His first journal entry began on a lighthearted
note, or as lighthearted as one can be in

02:07:18.760 --> 02:07:20.590
the face of combat.

02:07:20.590 --> 02:07:24.640
“June 27th, 1916
Finally arrived at the front!

02:07:24.640 --> 02:07:28.571
I picked up this little journal while I was
in Paris, figured I might as well keep record

02:07:28.571 --> 02:07:30.460
of my heroics on the battlefield.

02:07:30.460 --> 02:07:33.520
Quite chuffed to finally be in action, though
it seems I'm the only one.

02:07:33.520 --> 02:07:37.550
Most of these blokes have been fighting for
a couple months now, and they look downright

02:07:37.550 --> 02:07:38.550
dreadful.

02:07:38.550 --> 02:07:42.099
Mud all over the uniform, and their faces
are so pale, look like they haven't eaten

02:07:42.099 --> 02:07:43.530
or slept for months.”

02:07:43.530 --> 02:07:48.829
A few days later, he began to hear stirrings
amongst his fellow soldiers, and strange sounds

02:07:48.829 --> 02:07:50.540
that rocked their barracks.

02:07:50.540 --> 02:07:54.190
He described the first unsettling incident:
“July 2nd, 1916

02:07:54.190 --> 02:07:57.230
Woke in the early hours of the morning.

02:07:57.230 --> 02:08:01.580
Ground was shaking, damn near shook me out
into the muck on the dugout floor.

02:08:01.580 --> 02:08:05.130
Poor blokes in the bunks on the other side
looked liked they had seen a ghoul.

02:08:05.130 --> 02:08:08.710
Pair of Northern Irish lads from Kitchener’s
Armies if I remember right.

02:08:08.710 --> 02:08:12.639
Kept muttering about a Nuckatee?...Were both
gripping a gold crucifix.

02:08:12.639 --> 02:08:16.440
Was about to lay my head back down and get
a wink of shuteye when I ended up scrambling

02:08:16.440 --> 02:08:17.440
into the mud.

02:08:17.440 --> 02:08:19.270
Loudest damn thing I'd ever heard.

02:08:19.270 --> 02:08:23.760
Thought it was the Hun Artillery bout to mark
us with a whizz-bang, only problem was, never

02:08:23.760 --> 02:08:24.940
did get the bang.

02:08:24.940 --> 02:08:27.770
This morning asked our brass hat about the
Artillery barrage.

02:08:27.770 --> 02:08:31.690
Gave me a funny look, and asked what the bloody
hell I was talking about.”

02:08:31.690 --> 02:08:35.300
The next day, Dave went searching for the
source of the loud sound.

02:08:35.300 --> 02:08:40.400
He didn’t find any evidence of artillery,
but instead found something he had never seen

02:08:40.400 --> 02:08:41.400
before.

02:08:41.400 --> 02:08:44.360
It was a crater, shaped like a giant horse’s
hoof.

02:08:44.360 --> 02:08:49.090
He brushed it off as just another oddity of
the battlefield, a bit strange but nothing

02:08:49.090 --> 02:08:50.690
to be concerned about.

02:08:50.690 --> 02:08:53.320
There were more important things at hand,
anyway.

02:08:53.320 --> 02:08:58.880
The next day, he finally saw combat first-hand,
and things only got more bizarre and frightening.

02:08:58.880 --> 02:09:03.560
“July 3rd, 1916
Huns made a push today, first time they've

02:09:03.560 --> 02:09:04.780
moved in our region.

02:09:04.780 --> 02:09:06.699
First time I'd ever seen combat.

02:09:06.699 --> 02:09:08.680
It's not romantic and adventurous.

02:09:08.680 --> 02:09:10.840
It's terrifying, and deadly.

02:09:10.840 --> 02:09:14.329
My hands can't stop shaking, already messed
up the chit once.

02:09:14.329 --> 02:09:18.869
The Huns had our outfit up against a wall,
damn near overran us, didn't help that it

02:09:18.869 --> 02:09:22.340
rained the night before making our fox hole
filled to the brim with muck.

02:09:22.340 --> 02:09:26.170
One of the Fritz came right at me…just…I
put one right between his eyes.

02:09:26.170 --> 02:09:30.400
Fell right at the edge of the trench, and
had to look him in the eyes, poor lad couldn't

02:09:30.400 --> 02:09:32.389
have been more than 17 or 18.

02:09:32.389 --> 02:09:34.810
Martin, one of those Irish lads, is gone.

02:09:34.810 --> 02:09:38.830
Was unlike anything I'd ever seen, one moment
he's standing shooting at the Huns, all of

02:09:38.830 --> 02:09:40.520
the sudden, the mud starts boiling.

02:09:40.520 --> 02:09:45.380
Fore anyone can react, Mud just flies everywhere,
everyone else is suddenly knocked down off

02:09:45.380 --> 02:09:46.380
their feet.

02:09:46.380 --> 02:09:48.310
I look up, and he’s just gone.

02:09:48.310 --> 02:09:49.920
Wasn't even body parts left.

02:09:49.920 --> 02:09:54.340
Haven't told anyone…but I'd swear that there
was bones coming up from underneath him right

02:09:54.340 --> 02:09:55.840
before the mud went flying.

02:09:55.840 --> 02:10:00.320
His mate, Brendan, was digging in the mud
for hours, looking for the crucifix.”

02:10:00.320 --> 02:10:03.869
Martin’s body was never found, no matter
how they searched.

02:10:03.869 --> 02:10:07.909
A little over a week later, things got even
worse.

02:10:07.909 --> 02:10:12.969
“July 14th &amp; 15th, 1916
Huns tried to push this morning in the rain.

02:10:12.969 --> 02:10:17.360
I was in the machine gun nest with Brendan,
the other Irish chap in my unit.

02:10:17.360 --> 02:10:21.650
They kept coming and coming, and getting stuck
in the mud, and I just kept shooting.

02:10:21.650 --> 02:10:22.650
Sun is rising.

02:10:22.650 --> 02:10:26.270
I'm on watch till 8, at least that's what
the Brasshat said.

02:10:26.270 --> 02:10:29.330
I've started losing track of how much times
been passing.

02:10:29.330 --> 02:10:31.190
There's something out there.

02:10:31.190 --> 02:10:34.070
Something lurking out in the mud and dead
Huns.

02:10:34.070 --> 02:10:37.639
Nearly dozed off last night, listening to
the moans of the blighty wounded stuck out

02:10:37.639 --> 02:10:38.910
in No-man's land.

02:10:38.910 --> 02:10:40.690
Poor souls got left behind.

02:10:40.690 --> 02:10:44.270
Saw something out of the edge of my vision,
something big.

02:10:44.270 --> 02:10:49.380
Couldn't quite make it out, it was much darker
than usual, overcast sky was obscuring the

02:10:49.380 --> 02:10:50.380
full moon.

02:10:50.380 --> 02:10:55.059
Heard a couple of screams, but whatever it
was, was gone before my flare hit the sky.”

02:10:55.059 --> 02:10:59.449
This would not be Dave’s last sighting of
the large, dark figure.

02:10:59.449 --> 02:11:03.699
This mysterious shadow would appear again,
several days later.

02:11:03.699 --> 02:11:05.520
And there would be more of them.

02:11:05.520 --> 02:11:10.119
“July 30th, 1916
I've been seeing them at the edge of my vision,

02:11:10.119 --> 02:11:11.500
ever since that first night.

02:11:11.500 --> 02:11:15.719
They're huge, but they move so damn fast that
they're gone before I can get a clear look.

02:11:15.719 --> 02:11:18.520
Or at least, that's how it was mucking out
until today.

02:11:18.520 --> 02:11:22.219
Thick fog and mist rolled in this morning,
blanketed everything.

02:11:22.219 --> 02:11:24.850
We figured the Huns might use it to launch
another push.

02:11:24.850 --> 02:11:27.020
Bastards have been pushing non-stop since
the 20th.

02:11:27.020 --> 02:11:31.480
Saw it, through the fog, looked like a shadow,
hiding in the mist.

02:11:31.480 --> 02:11:37.130
Some sort of Horse like creature, with a something
dragging along the ground, and a giant lump

02:11:37.130 --> 02:11:39.809
where the rider would sit…cept the lump
started moving.

02:11:39.809 --> 02:11:43.260
Could have sworn it was a person, or something
that looked like a person.

02:11:43.260 --> 02:11:47.760
Sat up, and the things dragging along the
ground reached out in front of it and picked

02:11:47.760 --> 02:11:52.250
up something, thought it was a couple dead
Jerry's…until they started squirming.

02:11:52.250 --> 02:11:54.000
I'll never forget the noise it made.

02:11:54.000 --> 02:11:56.650
Louder than a banshee, shrill and twisted.

02:11:56.650 --> 02:11:58.550
It looked right at me.

02:11:58.550 --> 02:12:01.210
Two pairs of red glowing orbs.”

02:12:01.210 --> 02:12:06.320
Two weeks after meeting eyes with this chilling
apparition, Dave wrote a short note in his

02:12:06.320 --> 02:12:07.559
journal:
“August 5th

02:12:07.559 --> 02:12:08.750
Brendan calls them Nuckelavees.

02:12:08.750 --> 02:12:10.969
Won't tell me much more than that.

02:12:10.969 --> 02:12:14.429
Beginning to understand why all these blokes
looked so terrified when I first arrived.”

02:12:14.429 --> 02:12:18.530
It wasn’t until another week had passed
that Dave would truly begin to understand

02:12:18.530 --> 02:12:21.340
just what kind of monster he was up against.

02:12:21.340 --> 02:12:25.550
Not the enemy soldiers, but something far
more horrible.

02:12:25.550 --> 02:12:26.550
Something inhuman.

02:12:26.550 --> 02:12:28.510
“August 13th
Bloody hell.

02:12:28.510 --> 02:12:29.690
They're nightmares.

02:12:29.690 --> 02:12:34.809
Been on watch two nights in a row, one just…appeared
right there, right in front of me.

02:12:34.809 --> 02:12:37.440
20 feet, had to be at least 20 feet away.

02:12:37.440 --> 02:12:38.489
Towered into the sky.

02:12:38.489 --> 02:12:42.900
Got my flare to go off in time to see it pick
up a couple wounded Jerry's in the mud.

02:12:42.900 --> 02:12:44.610
They don't have bloody skin.

02:12:44.610 --> 02:12:46.420
There's just muscle, and fat.

02:12:46.420 --> 02:12:50.040
The thing on its back…wasn't human, no way
could it be human.

02:12:50.040 --> 02:12:54.230
Had no skin either, no legs, just merged straight
into the horse at the stomach.

02:12:54.230 --> 02:12:59.070
I took a couple shots at it with my rifle…did
absolutely nothing, like I was shooting it

02:12:59.070 --> 02:13:00.400
with a sling shot.

02:13:00.400 --> 02:13:03.869
It stopped soon as my flare reached its highest
point, and turned.

02:13:03.869 --> 02:13:08.360
Looked straight down at me, both the horse
and the…thing on its back.

02:13:08.360 --> 02:13:09.360
It smiled.”

02:13:09.360 --> 02:13:13.661
He tried to talk to his superiors, tried to
warn of the horrors he was seeing and the

02:13:13.661 --> 02:13:17.010
danger he felt they posed, but they wouldn’t
listen.

02:13:17.010 --> 02:13:19.500
Night after night, the creatures came back.

02:13:19.500 --> 02:13:23.989
“August 17th 1916
Been assigned night watch the past four nights

02:13:23.989 --> 02:13:24.989
straight.

02:13:24.989 --> 02:13:26.230
Tried to tell the brass hat about the nuckelavees.

02:13:26.230 --> 02:13:27.480
Didn't believe me.

02:13:27.480 --> 02:13:30.760
Said it was the shell shock playing with my
head.

02:13:30.760 --> 02:13:32.349
Had to put a sock in it, and keep on.

02:13:32.349 --> 02:13:34.050
It keeps coming back.

02:13:34.050 --> 02:13:35.179
Every night.

02:13:35.179 --> 02:13:37.180
Same spot, 20 feet in front of me.

02:13:37.180 --> 02:13:40.210
Picks up wounded Jerry's, turns and looks…and
then it's gone.

02:13:40.210 --> 02:13:42.369
It's playing with me, I'm sure of it.

02:13:42.369 --> 02:13:43.860
Last night there was another one too.

02:13:43.860 --> 02:13:47.130
Four of those things on its back, did the
same damn thing.”

02:13:47.130 --> 02:13:51.199
A few days later, Dave spotted something that
made his blood run cold.

02:13:51.199 --> 02:13:52.260
“7:00 A.M.

02:13:52.260 --> 02:13:56.110
August 20th 1916
Jerry's made a big push yesterday.

02:13:56.110 --> 02:13:58.630
Rained two days ago, all day, so the muck
was deep.

02:13:58.630 --> 02:14:01.309
We were on the machinegun again in the pillbox.

02:14:01.309 --> 02:14:05.619
So many of them in no-man's land last night,
couldn't tell the dead from the living.

02:14:05.619 --> 02:14:06.809
Haven't slept in six days.

02:14:06.809 --> 02:14:08.179
There were five tonight.

02:14:08.179 --> 02:14:12.219
Three of them had more than one of those…things
on their back.

02:14:12.219 --> 02:14:14.140
The one that keeps coming back…dropped something.

02:14:14.140 --> 02:14:17.349
Saw it shine in the flare light.

02:14:17.349 --> 02:14:18.349
10:00 A.M.

02:14:18.349 --> 02:14:21.770
August 20th 1916
Went out into the mud where it appears every

02:14:21.770 --> 02:14:22.770
night.

02:14:22.770 --> 02:14:24.429
Found Martin's crucifix and tin hat.”

02:14:24.429 --> 02:14:27.670
Whatever this thing was, it had taken Martin.

02:14:27.670 --> 02:14:30.000
It seemed to want Dave to know that, too.

02:14:30.000 --> 02:14:33.590
It left behind Martin’s lost things for
him to find.

02:14:33.590 --> 02:14:34.929
As if it was gloating.

02:14:34.929 --> 02:14:37.369
As if it already knew that it had won.

02:14:37.369 --> 02:14:42.059
“August 20th 1916
They're getting bold, saw one out in broad

02:14:42.059 --> 02:14:43.059
daylight.

02:14:43.059 --> 02:14:44.480
Pretty sure it was the same one.

02:14:44.480 --> 02:14:47.530
Buried itself in the mud, just lying there…waiting.

02:14:47.530 --> 02:14:49.449
We're going over the top at three.

02:14:49.449 --> 02:14:53.650
There are more out there now…all doing the
same thing…god help us.”

02:14:53.650 --> 02:14:58.880
Dave Harkand was declared Missing in Action
on August 20, 1916, following an attempted

02:14:58.880 --> 02:15:01.710
counterattack against the German forces.

02:15:01.710 --> 02:15:06.030
Another soldier from his unit, Brendan O’Malley,
was also reported Missing in Action on the

02:15:06.030 --> 02:15:07.030
same day.

02:15:07.030 --> 02:15:10.780
Though Dave’s body was never recovered,
his journal was found 20 feet away from the

02:15:10.780 --> 02:15:13.389
edge of the German trenches two months later.

02:15:13.389 --> 02:15:17.610
Poor Dave Harkand had no idea what he, and
the rest of his fellow soldiers, encountered

02:15:17.610 --> 02:15:18.610
out there.

02:15:18.610 --> 02:15:24.739
He didn’t live to learn more, but he came
face to face with SCP-3456.

02:15:24.739 --> 02:15:32.260
SCP-3456 is not one being, but rather a group
of quadrupeds that vaguely resemble horses.

02:15:32.260 --> 02:15:36.010
From a distance, their silhouette looks like
that of a horse with a human riding on its

02:15:36.010 --> 02:15:37.010
back.

02:15:37.010 --> 02:15:41.619
However, once the observer gets closer, they
will notice some disturbing differences.

02:15:41.619 --> 02:15:45.020
These creatures do not look like any ordinary
horse.

02:15:45.020 --> 02:15:50.170
They are smooth and hairless, with translucent
skin and three-toed hooves.

02:15:50.170 --> 02:15:53.409
Anyone unfortunate enough to get close to
one of these creatures will be able to see

02:15:53.409 --> 02:15:57.159
through their skin to the blood vessels and
muscle underneath.

02:15:57.159 --> 02:16:01.170
They will also notice that there is no rider
perched atop the creature’s back at all.

02:16:01.170 --> 02:16:07.389
The humanoid shape is a part of the creature’s
body, an extension of them, fused to its back.

02:16:07.389 --> 02:16:12.059
The humanoid figure consists of a pair of
long arms, which drag along the ground as

02:16:12.059 --> 02:16:14.130
the creature moves, and a head.

02:16:14.130 --> 02:16:19.530
The arms end in sharpened bones rather than
fingers, and the head has mostly human features,

02:16:19.530 --> 02:16:22.940
with the exception of a hole where the nose
should be.

02:16:22.940 --> 02:16:27.790
The creatures vary greatly in size, with the
largest on record measuring at a height of

02:16:27.790 --> 02:16:29.280
30 meters and a width of 15.

02:16:29.280 --> 02:16:34.620
They appear to be invulnerable, at least when
it comes to any traditional human weaponry

02:16:34.620 --> 02:16:37.290
they have currently been exposed to.

02:16:37.290 --> 02:16:43.700
Gunfire, explosives, swords and arrows, and
even nuclear blasts seem to have no effect.

02:16:43.700 --> 02:16:48.170
If you happen to get a look at one of these
bulletproof abominations in person, then I

02:16:48.170 --> 02:16:49.229
am so sorry.

02:16:49.229 --> 02:16:51.730
You are as good as gone.

02:16:51.730 --> 02:16:56.620
Because once you’ve seen one of these creatures,
they have also seen you, and they will not

02:16:56.620 --> 02:16:58.870
stop until they have taken you.

02:16:58.870 --> 02:17:04.359
They will track you, stalk you, hide buried
in mud and nestled in bushes.

02:17:04.359 --> 02:17:08.300
They will wait for the opportune moment, and
they will reach out with their unnaturally

02:17:08.300 --> 02:17:14.520
long arms, smiling with no lips as their blood
red eyes burn like hellfire, and you will

02:17:14.520 --> 02:17:16.330
disappear forever.

02:17:16.330 --> 02:17:20.410
They will travel far beyond the site where
they first appeared, until they have finally

02:17:20.410 --> 02:17:22.059
captured their prey.

02:17:22.059 --> 02:17:25.690
This isn’t an SCP-096 situation, either.

02:17:25.690 --> 02:17:28.110
They aren’t punishing you for seeing their
face.

02:17:28.110 --> 02:17:32.691
They want to be seen, and will go out of their
way to show themselves to people until they

02:17:32.691 --> 02:17:35.130
have captured as many as they want.

02:17:35.130 --> 02:17:40.760
No one knows what becomes of SCP-3456’s
victims, but they are never seen again.

02:17:40.760 --> 02:17:45.870
Though items once belonging to the missing
people may resurface, their bodies are never

02:17:45.870 --> 02:17:46.870
found.

02:17:46.870 --> 02:17:53.040
There is only one way to escape from SCP-3456,
and that is to find and cross a body of fresh

02:17:53.040 --> 02:17:54.040
water.

02:17:54.040 --> 02:17:59.540
For reasons unknown, the entities are unable
or unwilling to cross rivers, streams, and

02:17:59.540 --> 02:18:00.540
lakes.

02:18:00.540 --> 02:18:04.559
The Foundation first discovered this during
an operation in Iraq, in which several agents

02:18:04.559 --> 02:18:07.920
encountered a group of SCP-3456 manifestations.

02:18:07.920 --> 02:18:12.849
They fled from the monsters, and quickly retreated
across the Tigris river.

02:18:12.849 --> 02:18:16.689
Once they had reached the other side, they
saw that the creatures had not followed them

02:18:16.689 --> 02:18:18.030
onto the bridge.

02:18:18.030 --> 02:18:23.460
Instead, they remained at the riverbank on
the other side, watching, and waiting.

02:18:23.460 --> 02:18:28.570
This was quickly noted, and added to potential
containment procedures, though the exact reason

02:18:28.570 --> 02:18:33.220
for SCP-3456’s dislike of fresh water is
currently unknown.

02:18:33.220 --> 02:18:37.960
In Dave Harkland’s journals, his fellow
soldier described the creatures as “Nuckelavees,”

02:18:37.960 --> 02:18:40.530
but would not elaborate beyond that.

02:18:40.530 --> 02:18:42.370
So what is a Nuckelavee?

02:18:42.370 --> 02:18:46.810
The word refers to a creature from the waters
of Orkney, a group of islands on the northern

02:18:46.810 --> 02:18:48.500
coast of Scotland.

02:18:48.500 --> 02:18:53.210
Their name is thought to come from an Orcadian
word meaning “Devil of the Sea,” and they

02:18:53.210 --> 02:18:55.960
truly are like something out of hell.

02:18:55.960 --> 02:19:00.380
These creatures are native to the ocean, and
supposedly take on another form when in their

02:19:00.380 --> 02:19:04.570
natural habitat, but no one knows what they
truly look like.

02:19:04.570 --> 02:19:09.410
On land, the creature is a hybrid of man and
horse, with a large snout like that of a pig,

02:19:09.410 --> 02:19:13.620
and a single red eye that burns like the embers
of a fire.

02:19:13.620 --> 02:19:19.720
It has no hair or skin, just raw, tissue and
bone dripping black blood.

02:19:19.720 --> 02:19:24.250
Everything about the creature is malicious
and deadly, intended to bring harm and calamity

02:19:24.250 --> 02:19:25.620
to humans.

02:19:25.620 --> 02:19:30.990
Even its breath is toxic, thought to cause
disease, plague, and the death of crops.

02:19:30.990 --> 02:19:35.660
As they are native to the ocean, they detest
fresh water, and will not cross it even in

02:19:35.660 --> 02:19:37.280
pursuit of their prey.

02:19:37.280 --> 02:19:39.880
They will also not appear when it is raining.

02:19:39.880 --> 02:19:43.540
In the legends of the Nuckelavee, they do
have a natural enemy.

02:19:43.540 --> 02:19:48.300
A creature from Orcadian folklore known as
the Mither of the Sea is said to have the

02:19:48.300 --> 02:19:51.970
power to keep the monsters from coming ashore
during the Summer months.

02:19:51.970 --> 02:19:57.350
The Mither, or Mother, is a benevolent force
of nature, giving warmth to the oceans and

02:19:57.350 --> 02:20:00.740
life to the beings of the water and the land.

02:20:00.740 --> 02:20:05.870
Though SCP-3456 has appeared during the Summer
months, it has never been spotted in the Orkney

02:20:05.870 --> 02:20:08.430
region during this time of year.

02:20:08.430 --> 02:20:13.570
Perhaps this is a coincidence, but some Foundation
researchers have proposed a research expedition

02:20:13.570 --> 02:20:17.270
to the area in order to look for the kindly
ocean spirit.

02:20:17.270 --> 02:20:20.479
So far, this proposal has been denied.

02:20:20.479 --> 02:20:25.800
SCP-3456 is classified as Keter, and there
is currently no way to effectively contain

02:20:25.800 --> 02:20:26.800
it.

02:20:26.800 --> 02:20:30.950
All previous attempts to contain or to neutralize
the horsemen have failed, though the Foundation

02:20:30.950 --> 02:20:33.570
is always looking for new methods to attempt.

02:20:33.570 --> 02:20:37.970
Currently, any personnel who see the horsemen
will be given Class G amnestics at a treatment

02:20:37.970 --> 02:20:42.960
center located within one kilometer of a freshwater
stream, river, or lake.

02:20:42.960 --> 02:20:47.460
All references to the horsemen have been scrubbed
from historical records, and any sightings

02:20:47.460 --> 02:20:52.130
are to be blamed on PTSD, shock, and trauma-induced
hysteria.

02:20:52.130 --> 02:20:58.649
Areas that are likely to attract SCP-3456,
such as war zones and areas impacted by natural

02:20:58.649 --> 02:21:01.790
disasters, are to be heavily monitored by
the Foundation.

02:21:01.790 --> 02:21:06.780
In the event of a disaster, Foundation personnel
will be sent to help with evacuation in order

02:21:06.780 --> 02:21:11.729
to get all civilians away from SCP-3456 as
quickly as possible.

02:21:11.729 --> 02:21:14.890
So what is SCP-3456?

02:21:14.890 --> 02:21:18.900
Is it the dreaded Nuckelavee from folktales
and whispered fireside warnings?

02:21:18.900 --> 02:21:24.260
There are some notable differences between
the stories and what the Foundation encountered.

02:21:24.260 --> 02:21:29.109
SCP-3456 does not seem to have come from the
ocean, nor is it limited to only appearing

02:21:29.109 --> 02:21:30.540
around Orkney.

02:21:30.540 --> 02:21:36.080
These beasts seem to manifest from thin air,
and disappear the same way when their nasty

02:21:36.080 --> 02:21:37.180
work is done.

02:21:37.180 --> 02:21:41.390
But, folklore and passing down stories often
distorts things.

02:21:41.390 --> 02:21:45.110
Details change, and others are added or left
out.

02:21:45.110 --> 02:21:49.109
In the original stories, the Nuckelavee was
thought to be the cause of famines, plagues,

02:21:49.109 --> 02:21:50.360
and disasters.

02:21:50.360 --> 02:21:56.300
Perhaps it was simply drawn to these events,
lured there by the scent of pure human misery.

02:21:56.300 --> 02:22:02.450
Perhaps the Nuckelavee is not just similar
to SCP-3456, but the two are one and the same.

02:22:02.450 --> 02:22:06.000
Or perhaps they are something entirely different.

02:22:06.000 --> 02:22:10.140
Whatever the case may be, there is nothing
we can do to stop them.

02:22:10.140 --> 02:22:16.580
War, famine, pestilence, and death are everywhere,
they are inevitable and unfortunate parts

02:22:16.580 --> 02:22:18.000
of life on earth.

02:22:18.000 --> 02:22:24.360
So, it seems, are these deadly riders, these
monsters that are neither horse nor man, but

02:22:24.360 --> 02:22:26.590
still somehow both.

02:22:26.590 --> 02:22:32.660
Every time we wage war, every time disaster
strikes, they will come to watch, to pick

02:22:32.660 --> 02:22:35.180
through the rubble, and to smile.

02:22:35.180 --> 02:22:39.140
Maybe, we don’t need to dread the coming
of the Horsemen of the Apocalypse.

02:22:39.140 --> 02:22:41.830
They are already here.

02:22:41.830 --> 02:22:47.311
There are many things in this world that we
do not, and perhaps cannot, understand.

02:22:47.311 --> 02:22:52.450
The SCP Foundation dedicates itself to researching
and containing these things, but even they

02:22:52.450 --> 02:22:57.080
occasionally encounter something that defies
any kind of true understanding.

02:22:57.080 --> 02:23:02.560
The unknown is terrifying to the average person,
but for an organization that specializes in

02:23:02.560 --> 02:23:09.080
knowing the unknowable, a mystery that refuses
to be understood can be downright nightmarish.

02:23:09.080 --> 02:23:13.930
A Foundation expedition team lost contact
with their command while on a mission in the

02:23:13.930 --> 02:23:15.910
Northern Ural mountains of Russia.

02:23:15.910 --> 02:23:21.130
After six hours of silence, radio contact
was reestablished, though video feed continued

02:23:21.130 --> 02:23:22.340
to be disabled.

02:23:22.340 --> 02:23:27.560
A lone agent, Dr. Felsenstein, called out
desperately over the radio waves, begging

02:23:27.560 --> 02:23:31.010
for someone, anyone, to answer him.

02:23:31.010 --> 02:23:34.560
Command responded, requesting a status update
on the rest of his crew.

02:23:34.560 --> 02:23:38.590
At first, they were met only with the wet,
hollow sound of Felsenstein weeping.

02:23:38.590 --> 02:23:47.670
Finally, he explained that they were all dead,
and he was the only man left standing.

02:23:47.670 --> 02:23:48.930
“Something got him,” he said, of fellow
agent Myers.

02:23:48.930 --> 02:23:50.750
“It was long…slippery.

02:23:50.750 --> 02:23:54.410
I saw a grown man pulled into a tiny hole.”

02:23:54.410 --> 02:23:59.170
He began to hyperventilate, his descriptions
becoming less and less coherent.

02:23:59.170 --> 02:24:03.200
Command offered to send reinforcements to
collect the survivor, but he begged them not

02:24:03.200 --> 02:24:04.200
to.

02:24:04.200 --> 02:24:09.529
He was beyond saving at this point, describing
himself as “nothing but a walking corpse.”

02:24:09.529 --> 02:24:14.040
After slipping into a crevice, Felsenstein
had broken his ankle and torn a hole in his

02:24:14.040 --> 02:24:15.149
hazmat suit.

02:24:15.149 --> 02:24:19.800
Command honored his insistence that no reinforcements
be sent in, but encouraged him to try and

02:24:19.800 --> 02:24:23.820
pull himself back to the surface and retrieve
additional data.

02:24:23.820 --> 02:24:28.510
Even if he was doomed, he could still provide
valuable information on the threat he encountered.

02:24:28.510 --> 02:24:32.820
When Felsenstein attempted to free himself
from the crevice, he slipped deeper into the

02:24:32.820 --> 02:24:34.290
crack in the ground.

02:24:34.290 --> 02:24:38.200
Pushing through his fear of being crushed
to death, he tried again.

02:24:38.200 --> 02:24:41.900
Fighting against the burning of the toxic
air in his lungs and the straining of his

02:24:41.900 --> 02:24:44.490
muscles, he finally pulled himself to freedom.

02:24:44.490 --> 02:24:46.920
Then, he took in his surroundings.

02:24:46.920 --> 02:24:50.960
He was at the edge of a chasm, so deep he
could not see the bottom.

02:24:50.960 --> 02:24:54.930
He posited that he was somewhere underneath
or inside of a mountain.

02:24:54.930 --> 02:25:00.700
There was a putrid smell in the air, burning
his eyes, his skin, everything.

02:25:00.700 --> 02:25:04.610
Command told him to remain calm, still hoping
for the possibility of a rescue.

02:25:04.610 --> 02:25:09.130
Meanwhile, on their end, hostile forces were
closing in and forcing them to evacuate.

02:25:09.130 --> 02:25:13.319
They asked Felsenstein to continue describing
his surroundings, so that his account might

02:25:13.319 --> 02:25:15.180
be recorded for the archives.

02:25:15.180 --> 02:25:19.399
They would attempt to come back with reinforcements
when it was safe for them to do so.

02:25:19.399 --> 02:25:24.940
As Felsenstein made it deeper into the chasm,
he was engulfed in a thick yellow fog.

02:25:24.940 --> 02:25:29.891
Through the haze, he could make out thousands
of eggs, and piles of meat being devoured

02:25:29.891 --> 02:25:35.601
by small creatures with the bodies of grubs
and the faces of human infants.

02:25:35.601 --> 02:25:40.399
The creatures did not respond to his presence,
either unaware of him or too consumed with

02:25:40.399 --> 02:25:42.170
their feeding to care.

02:25:42.170 --> 02:25:47.029
As he passed the creatures, he spotted a massive
black temple with architecture like nothing

02:25:47.029 --> 02:25:52.920
he had seen before, all polished and sharp
with angles that hurt his eyes to look at.

02:25:52.920 --> 02:25:57.979
As he stopped to take a better look, he realized
he was still moving somehow, without moving

02:25:57.979 --> 02:25:59.180
his feet.

02:25:59.180 --> 02:26:03.600
He was being dragged by something, tendrils
wrapped around his legs and pulling him along

02:26:03.600 --> 02:26:07.620
against his will, leaving a trail of his blood
behind.

02:26:07.620 --> 02:26:11.729
As he was dragged, dozens of what seemed like
humans watched him.

02:26:11.729 --> 02:26:15.700
The final words recorded on the audio transcript
were the most troubling of all.

02:26:15.700 --> 02:26:19.620
Felsenstein saw what he described as an “angel”
with a thousand wings.

02:26:19.620 --> 02:26:25.060
The angel pulled him into her embrace, clutching
him to her breast…and the connection was

02:26:25.060 --> 02:26:26.060
lost.

02:26:26.060 --> 02:26:28.229
Dr. Felsenstein was never seen again.

02:26:28.229 --> 02:26:30.529
His colleagues’ bodies were never recovered.

02:26:30.529 --> 02:26:38.319
The entire team of men was lost forever, inside
the incomprehensible hellhole known as SCP-2133.

02:26:38.319 --> 02:26:44.600
SCP-2133 is an unnamed village in the Northern
Ural mountains in Eastern Europe, with an

02:26:44.600 --> 02:26:47.279
estimated population of around fifty people.

02:26:47.279 --> 02:26:51.660
The village is considered dangerous to enter
without proper hazmat gear, due to the presence

02:26:51.660 --> 02:26:57.010
of a wide variety of microbial pathogens within
its limits, including those which cause leprosy,

02:26:57.010 --> 02:27:03.490
pneumonic, septicemic, and bubonic plagues,
typhoid fever, influenza, cholera, and smallpox.

02:27:03.490 --> 02:27:06.609
A veritable hypochondriac’s worst nightmare.

02:27:06.609 --> 02:27:11.649
In spite of this cocktail of diseases in which
they live, the residents of 2133 seem to be

02:27:11.649 --> 02:27:14.229
resistant to the negative effects of infection.

02:27:14.229 --> 02:27:19.270
Of course, they experience physical symptoms,
to the point of visible disfigurement or disability,

02:27:19.270 --> 02:27:23.710
but they do not die at a rate consistent with
the sheer volume of deadly pathogens present

02:27:23.710 --> 02:27:24.840
in their town.

02:27:24.840 --> 02:27:27.880
The people of SCP-2133 do not leave it.

02:27:27.880 --> 02:27:32.500
The Foundation cannot fully determine whether
they cannot leave, or simply choose not to,

02:27:32.500 --> 02:27:36.859
but whatever the case may be they stay within
the limits of their village.

02:27:36.859 --> 02:27:41.979
Their relative resistance to disease, small
population, and refusal to leave the boundaries

02:27:41.979 --> 02:27:46.859
of their village are all unusual, but that
is far from the most unusual thing about the

02:27:46.859 --> 02:27:49.779
population of SCP-2133.

02:27:49.779 --> 02:27:54.420
The people of the village age and die, yes,
but they do not stay dead.

02:27:54.420 --> 02:27:59.439
They engage in what can only be described
as some kind of reincarnation.

02:27:59.439 --> 02:28:03.850
When a resident of the village dies, they
are placed in the field, where they quickly

02:28:03.850 --> 02:28:04.850
decay.

02:28:04.850 --> 02:28:08.960
On the night of the first new moon, a newborn
infant is pulled from the soil where the decaying

02:28:08.960 --> 02:28:10.550
body once lay.

02:28:10.550 --> 02:28:15.380
The reborn version of each person looks like
their previous self, and carries all of the

02:28:15.380 --> 02:28:17.569
memories they had in their previous life.

02:28:17.569 --> 02:28:22.240
The Foundation performed extensive soil tests
on the field where this curious rebirth takes

02:28:22.240 --> 02:28:26.590
place, and found that the soil there contains
high levels of embryonic fluid.

02:28:26.590 --> 02:28:31.410
Beyond the presence of this fluid in the earth,
it is unknown how exactly this reincarnation

02:28:31.410 --> 02:28:33.040
process works.

02:28:33.040 --> 02:28:40.050
The residents of the village, known as SCP-2133-1,
speak an old Russian dialect and occasionally

02:28:40.050 --> 02:28:44.229
agree to be interviewed by Foundation staff
fluent in this dialect.

02:28:44.229 --> 02:28:48.359
Though they will sit for interviews and chat
with Foundation personnel, they are secretive

02:28:48.359 --> 02:28:52.730
about their lives, their history, and the
culture of their little village.

02:28:52.730 --> 02:28:57.479
The first resident to be successfully interviewed
was an elderly man named Aristarkh, who was

02:28:57.479 --> 02:29:01.670
missing his left arm and had necrosis on most
of his visible skin.

02:29:01.670 --> 02:29:06.540
The interview was conducted by Dr. Judith
Low, one of the head researchers on the case.

02:29:06.540 --> 02:29:11.160
She asked the man how far back he was able
to remember, and he recounted a time of “Tsars

02:29:11.160 --> 02:29:12.160
and Khans.”

02:29:12.160 --> 02:29:17.510
When Dr. Low pressed the man about the rebirth
that his people practice, he responded that

02:29:17.510 --> 02:29:20.140
it was “The Church of the Red Harvest.

02:29:20.140 --> 02:29:21.970
We serve until the end.

02:29:21.970 --> 02:29:25.080
That is the terms of our agreement.”

02:29:25.080 --> 02:29:29.430
Dr. Low asked him why he, and the rest of
his people, would continue to live their lives

02:29:29.430 --> 02:29:32.590
this way when it causes them such obvious
suffering.

02:29:32.590 --> 02:29:35.140
He explained, simply: “There is no choice.

02:29:35.140 --> 02:29:36.760
The land calls.

02:29:36.760 --> 02:29:37.920
We answer.”

02:29:37.920 --> 02:29:42.979
She continued to push the issue, inquiring
about how this all began so many years ago.

02:29:42.979 --> 02:29:46.740
He explained that a priestess came to the
village many lifetimes ago.

02:29:46.740 --> 02:29:50.140
She offered the people paradise, in exchange
for their servitude.

02:29:50.140 --> 02:29:53.960
However, as the years passed, the people became
more and more exhausted.

02:29:53.960 --> 02:29:57.050
They feared that they had failed somehow,
and were being punished.

02:29:57.050 --> 02:30:02.040
Aristarkh became visibly upset at this point
in the interview, but continued to insist:

02:30:02.040 --> 02:30:04.980
“The Church of the Red Harvest is truth.

02:30:04.980 --> 02:30:06.790
There is no other.”

02:30:06.790 --> 02:30:11.391
The second interview was conducted again by
Dr. Judith Low, who spoke with Anya, a young

02:30:11.391 --> 02:30:14.660
girl who appeared to be between the ages of
six and eight.

02:30:14.660 --> 02:30:19.270
Low greeted the girl, and attempted to ask
her first question, but Anya simply said:

02:30:19.270 --> 02:30:21.029
“You don’t belong here.

02:30:21.029 --> 02:30:22.029
Leave.”

02:30:22.029 --> 02:30:26.080
Low brushed this off, and offered the girl
medical assistance, but was rebuffed again:

02:30:26.080 --> 02:30:28.170
“You are not of the covenant.

02:30:28.170 --> 02:30:29.710
You will never understand.”

02:30:29.710 --> 02:30:34.710
Dr. Low asked Anya to elaborate on the nature
of this covenant, and her explanation was

02:30:34.710 --> 02:30:37.660
similar to that of the previous interviewee.

02:30:37.660 --> 02:30:42.440
There was an agreement made, a long time ago,
and now the people of the village would serve

02:30:42.440 --> 02:30:44.300
until the end of time.

02:30:44.300 --> 02:30:49.380
Again, she insisted that the Foundation should
leave, and did not belong in the town.

02:30:49.380 --> 02:30:54.420
Finally, irritated with the questions, Anya
had only this to say about the church: “The

02:30:54.420 --> 02:30:56.600
church was here long before the village.

02:30:56.600 --> 02:30:58.890
A church of stone beneath the earth.

02:30:58.890 --> 02:30:59.890
It is sacred.

02:30:59.890 --> 02:31:04.970
A church of wood was built atop it, for the
heresy of the cross - before we embraced the

02:31:04.970 --> 02:31:06.090
true faith.

02:31:06.090 --> 02:31:08.450
The Karcist Alka will enlighten you.

02:31:08.450 --> 02:31:12.939
You are only alive because she has chosen
to let you live.”

02:31:12.939 --> 02:31:17.050
Hearing the word Karcist probably gives you
some indication as to what’s really going

02:31:17.050 --> 02:31:21.399
on here - If the disease, corruption, and
mutation of the flesh didn’t give you enough

02:31:21.399 --> 02:31:22.640
of a clue.

02:31:22.640 --> 02:31:25.550
This horror is Sarkic through and through.

02:31:25.550 --> 02:31:31.120
Dr. Low’s final question was a seemingly
easy one: does the village have a name?

02:31:31.120 --> 02:31:36.670
As soon as the words left Dr. Low’s lips,
Anya began to vomit up a thick black substance,

02:31:36.670 --> 02:31:39.060
ending the interview.

02:31:39.060 --> 02:31:44.740
Instances of SCP-2133-1 are largely apathetic
toward Foundation agents, unless they get

02:31:44.740 --> 02:31:46.070
in the way of their routine.

02:31:46.070 --> 02:31:50.920
The agents are allowed to go inside of any
buildings in the village, with one notable

02:31:50.920 --> 02:31:53.850
exception: the Church of the Red Harvest.

02:31:53.850 --> 02:31:58.110
Any attempts to learn more about the church
or enter its walls are met with refusal to

02:31:58.110 --> 02:32:01.399
explain, or, in some cases, outright hostility.

02:32:01.399 --> 02:32:05.370
Though the villagers are largely peaceful
toward the Foundation, they are not the only

02:32:05.370 --> 02:32:08.550
entity living in SCP-2133.

02:32:08.550 --> 02:32:13.880
Throughout the village, there are instances
of something known as SCP-2133-2.

02:32:13.880 --> 02:32:19.300
These organic structures, which have the appearance
of dark red tentacles, display overt hostility

02:32:19.300 --> 02:32:23.170
toward outsiders and will attack any that
get too close.

02:32:23.170 --> 02:32:27.180
They are especially aggressive to any outsiders
that attempt to enter the church.

02:32:27.180 --> 02:32:31.899
Tissue samples were taken from the tentacles
for observation, and they were found, horrifyingly

02:32:31.899 --> 02:32:36.240
enough, to genetically resemble tissue samples
from humans.

02:32:36.240 --> 02:32:39.910
After the interview with Anya, the Foundation
research team determined that entering the

02:32:39.910 --> 02:32:42.520
church was of the utmost importance.

02:32:42.520 --> 02:32:46.720
Mobile Task Force Beta-7 was dispatched for
this mission, and, after the residents of

02:32:46.720 --> 02:32:50.689
the town were restrained, a team of twelve
operatives was sent in.

02:32:50.689 --> 02:32:55.490
They were armed with radios, video recorders,
hazmat suits, and air tanks.

02:32:55.490 --> 02:33:00.380
As they attempted to enter the church, the
tentacles attacked, but were subdued with

02:33:00.380 --> 02:33:01.380
flamethrowers.

02:33:01.380 --> 02:33:06.000
Apparently, like most living things, they
are not immune to fire.

02:33:06.000 --> 02:33:10.220
Inside the church, the research team found
small idols crafted from bone and leather,

02:33:10.220 --> 02:33:14.359
and a few others made from tumors, hanging
from iron hooks on the ceiling.

02:33:14.359 --> 02:33:18.640
At the building’s center was an entrance
to a system of caves and caverns beneath the

02:33:18.640 --> 02:33:22.140
village, stretching beyond its borders into
the mountains.

02:33:22.140 --> 02:33:28.840
Several previously unseen organisms, designated
only as SCP-2133-3, were discovered inside.

02:33:28.840 --> 02:33:32.530
One was terminated, and taken back to the
Foundation for an autopsy.

02:33:32.530 --> 02:33:36.820
The creature was humanoid in nature, with
swollen organs and flesh, and an overgrowth

02:33:36.820 --> 02:33:38.920
of bone and fatty tissue.

02:33:38.920 --> 02:33:42.580
After the autopsy, the team of operatives
refreshed their air tanks and headed back

02:33:42.580 --> 02:33:45.410
into the village to continue their research.

02:33:45.410 --> 02:33:49.900
About fifty minutes into their expedition,
all contact was lost out of nowhere.

02:33:49.900 --> 02:33:55.000
Six hours later, Dr. Felsenstein would make
his infamous radio contact, and the nightmare

02:33:55.000 --> 02:33:57.020
would unfold from there.

02:33:57.020 --> 02:34:00.340
Currently, SCP-2133 is easily contained.

02:34:00.340 --> 02:34:05.360
A security perimeter is maintained at a ten-kilometer
radius around the town, preventing any civilians

02:34:05.360 --> 02:34:07.439
from making their way inside.

02:34:07.439 --> 02:34:12.390
There are guards positioned along the perimeter,
under the guise of a Russian military base.

02:34:12.390 --> 02:34:18.021
In spite of the horrifying nature of SCP-2133,
the villagers do not seem to pose an immediate

02:34:18.021 --> 02:34:19.351
threat to anyone.

02:34:19.351 --> 02:34:24.501
They simply want to be left alone, to till
the fields and attend their church, in an

02:34:24.501 --> 02:34:28.990
endless cycle of winters and summers as they
wait for the end to come.

02:34:28.990 --> 02:34:35.450
As they hope that finally, their agreement
will be honored, and they will find peace.

02:34:35.450 --> 02:34:38.150
The ocean is a terrifying place.

02:34:38.150 --> 02:34:40.530
We’ve all heard the statistics.

02:34:40.530 --> 02:34:43.260
More than 80 percent of the ocean remains
unexplored.

02:34:43.260 --> 02:34:49.060
That’s most of the water covering the globe,
completely unmapped and unobserved by science.

02:34:49.060 --> 02:34:54.080
It’s a scary thought to dwell on, realizing
there’s more water than land on earth, and

02:34:54.080 --> 02:34:59.050
the sheer expanse of that water is so large
that we’ve been unable to fully explore

02:34:59.050 --> 02:35:00.450
all of it.

02:35:00.450 --> 02:35:05.200
Just think, there are places in the ocean
that have never been seen by a human.

02:35:05.200 --> 02:35:06.779
Who knows what’s down there?

02:35:06.779 --> 02:35:11.950
If there were ever a personification of the
fear of the unknown, the ocean could definitely

02:35:11.950 --> 02:35:12.950
be it.

02:35:12.950 --> 02:35:18.540
Ancient shipwrecks sunk to the ocean floor,
unknown sea creatures hiding away from humanity,

02:35:18.540 --> 02:35:23.729
and the general isolation of the suffocating
dark blue the ocean swallows its victims with,

02:35:23.729 --> 02:35:27.970
all of these are images that come to mind
when thinking about the vast and mysterious

02:35:27.970 --> 02:35:29.950
depths of the sea.

02:35:29.950 --> 02:35:34.150
And no one is more familiar with nautical
mysteries than the SCP Foundation.

02:35:34.150 --> 02:35:40.810
Today we’ll be taking a look at SCP-5007,
the Bass Strait, a wave of oceanic anomalies

02:35:40.810 --> 02:35:46.030
fit to make any seasoned sailor shiver in
fear.

02:35:46.030 --> 02:35:50.060
is an area of ocean dividing Tasmania and
the Australian mainland.

02:35:50.060 --> 02:35:54.140
It’s also the location of an unusually high
amount of disappearances.

02:35:54.140 --> 02:35:59.240
Sailors disappearing from their ships, fishermen
leaving in the night and never coming back,

02:35:59.240 --> 02:36:02.850
even civilians disappearing from the shores
that connect to the Strait.

02:36:02.850 --> 02:36:08.310
The Foundation was aware of these disappearances
since 1858, but were only able to craft theories

02:36:08.310 --> 02:36:10.229
about what was causing them.

02:36:10.229 --> 02:36:12.570
Was it an anomalous group of interest?

02:36:12.570 --> 02:36:15.640
Hostile aerial entities patrolling the skies
above the Strait?

02:36:15.640 --> 02:36:19.229
Phenomena associated with unidentified flying
objects?

02:36:19.229 --> 02:36:23.810
What about subterranean anomalies,weather
patterns, or time dilation?

02:36:23.810 --> 02:36:28.010
For nearly a century, the Foundation was unable
to determine the cause of the high number

02:36:28.010 --> 02:36:34.061
of disappearances in the Bass Strait, and
then, the phenomena suddenly revealed itself.

02:36:34.061 --> 02:36:40.840
In 1980, on a beach connected to the strait,
Agent Taberner, an operative of the SCP Foundation,

02:36:40.840 --> 02:36:44.480
was vacationing with his wife, Mary, and his
three young children.

02:36:44.480 --> 02:36:49.260
The Taberner family was simply enjoying their
day, when they saw what looked like balloons

02:36:49.260 --> 02:36:50.430
in the sky.

02:36:50.430 --> 02:36:54.189
They were approaching quickly, and naturally,
the family moved closer.

02:36:54.189 --> 02:36:59.279
What happened next was a whirlwind, and those
balloons the family was so interested in lifted

02:36:59.279 --> 02:37:03.250
them up from the ground, and carried them
away.

02:37:03.250 --> 02:37:07.770
Agent Taberner tried to fight back, but there
was nothing he could do, except report to

02:37:07.770 --> 02:37:09.521
the Foundation what had occurred.

02:37:09.521 --> 02:37:12.720
And the organization responded in full force.

02:37:12.720 --> 02:37:16.700
The Foundation’s research discovered that
reports of UFOs and lights in the sky had

02:37:16.700 --> 02:37:21.450
coincided with many disappearances in the
Strait, and that this was a pattern.

02:37:21.450 --> 02:37:25.350
The search for the four lost Taberner family
members had become a large-scale investigation

02:37:25.350 --> 02:37:31.319
into unexplained disappearances along the
Bass Strait, and within 3 weeks, it was determined

02:37:31.319 --> 02:37:36.939
that these patterns were consistent across
the entirety of the Strait’s coastal regions.

02:37:36.939 --> 02:37:42.229
Some witnesses were interviewed, but the vast
majority of these abduction cases had no witnesses

02:37:42.229 --> 02:37:43.229
whatsoever.

02:37:43.229 --> 02:37:47.770
Of the minimal reports filed, the Foundation
was told that there were lights in the sky,

02:37:47.770 --> 02:37:52.279
and the appearance of unidentified flying
objects described as having the appearance

02:37:52.279 --> 02:37:53.569
of balloons.

02:37:53.569 --> 02:37:57.920
One such witness interviewed was a man by
the name of Alan Stewart, a witness who was

02:37:57.920 --> 02:38:03.100
present during the disappearance of former
Australian Prime Minister Harold Holt, whose

02:38:03.100 --> 02:38:07.609
disappearance the Foundation believed may
have had a connection to the Bass Strait anomalies.

02:38:07.609 --> 02:38:11.750
During the interview, Stewart claimed that
Holt and his family, while voyaging on their

02:38:11.750 --> 02:38:14.870
yacht, decided to leave the boat and go for
a swim.

02:38:14.870 --> 02:38:19.130
Holt turned to Stewart and asked him if he
could see the balloons around the cliff.

02:38:19.130 --> 02:38:24.060
Stewart had no idea what Holt was talking
about, but Holt was insistent on seeing them.

02:38:24.060 --> 02:38:28.400
He swam deeper out into the ocean, saying
that they weren’t normal balloons, and that

02:38:28.400 --> 02:38:30.529
there was someone inside of them.

02:38:30.529 --> 02:38:34.780
Stewart and Holt’s family called out for
him to come to shore, but he wouldn’t listen.

02:38:34.780 --> 02:38:37.189
Stewart tried to rationalize what he saw next.

02:38:37.189 --> 02:38:39.609
Maybe it was the current sweeping Holt away.

02:38:39.609 --> 02:38:42.040
But he couldn’t lie to the Foundation interviewer.

02:38:42.040 --> 02:38:46.890
Stewart saw Holt go further and further out
into the water, and suddenly, the Prime Minister

02:38:46.890 --> 02:38:47.890
turned around.

02:38:47.890 --> 02:38:50.090
He began swimming in the opposite direction.

02:38:50.090 --> 02:38:52.090
And he was screaming.

02:38:52.090 --> 02:38:56.740
Suddenly, Holt was lifted from the sea and
pulled into the air by something emerging

02:38:56.740 --> 02:38:58.080
from the clouds.

02:38:58.080 --> 02:39:02.120
The Foundation thanked Stewart for the interview,
and continued their investigation.

02:39:02.120 --> 02:39:07.580
Two years later, in 1982, emergency services
received a large number of calls pertaining

02:39:07.580 --> 02:39:11.470
to UFO sightings off the coast of Norman Bay,
Victoria.

02:39:11.470 --> 02:39:16.190
The Foundation was quick to respond, alerting
task forces and local sites to prepare for

02:39:16.190 --> 02:39:17.840
an investigation.

02:39:17.840 --> 02:39:21.950
Upon arriving at the scene, they confirmed
the existence of multiple entities that would

02:39:21.950 --> 02:39:24.450
later be documented as SCP-5007.

02:39:24.450 --> 02:39:30.560
They evacuated civilians from the area and
successfully managed to capture the creature,

02:39:30.560 --> 02:39:33.540
which was later transported to Site-40 for
containment.

02:39:33.540 --> 02:39:35.830
It was a sight to behold.

02:39:35.830 --> 02:39:43.030
The entity, now designated SCP-5007-S1, was
a cluster of human bodies fused between a

02:39:43.030 --> 02:39:46.380
grouping of black tentacles of varying length.

02:39:46.380 --> 02:39:49.890
Each tentacle was fused to the skin it touched
directly.

02:39:49.890 --> 02:39:55.680
The stomachs of the corpses were grossly swollen
and distorted to massive sizes to hold large

02:39:55.680 --> 02:40:01.210
quantities of gasses inside, the buoyancy
of which the entity used to achieve a passive

02:40:01.210 --> 02:40:02.210
flight.

02:40:02.210 --> 02:40:06.910
Across the entity’s surface were clusters
of eyes and bioluminescent, glowing organs.

02:40:06.910 --> 02:40:10.710
Many of the humanoid components of the corpses
appeared to have been removed and misplaced

02:40:10.710 --> 02:40:13.279
across various parts of the entity’s body.

02:40:13.279 --> 02:40:18.880
What’s more, is that the Foundation discovered
that the human portions of SCP-5007 appeared

02:40:18.880 --> 02:40:22.310
somewhat cognizant and aware of their situation.

02:40:22.310 --> 02:40:27.271
Their vocalizations were incoherent and barely
understandable, consisting of gasping and

02:40:27.271 --> 02:40:31.670
whimpering, but the corpses were observed
to implore other individuals to approach them

02:40:31.670 --> 02:40:33.520
when encountered.

02:40:33.520 --> 02:40:38.570
SCP-5007’s behavior during abduction scenarios
was documented during the initial containment

02:40:38.570 --> 02:40:43.700
event, and due to the Foundation’s painstaking
research, a pattern was established between

02:40:43.700 --> 02:40:46.390
all SCP-5007 encounters.

02:40:46.390 --> 02:40:52.070
First, the victim would be alone, or otherwise
vulnerable in a coastal location.

02:40:52.070 --> 02:40:57.870
SCP-5007 haven’t shown a preference for
weather, be they clear or hostile skies, but

02:40:57.870 --> 02:41:02.980
they have localized all of their activity
to the Bass Strait, in small coastal towns,

02:41:02.980 --> 02:41:05.190
beaches, or boats.

02:41:05.190 --> 02:41:09.990
SCP-5007 will then move towards the shore,
stalking the victim before lowering its tentacles

02:41:09.990 --> 02:41:14.640
and appendages to grab the individual, snatching
them into the sky.

02:41:14.640 --> 02:41:19.540
An SCP-5007 instance can even abduct multiple
people at once.

02:41:19.540 --> 02:41:23.740
One event observed had eight men from the
decks of a commercial fishing boat taken into

02:41:23.740 --> 02:41:26.760
the sky in under 15 seconds.

02:41:26.760 --> 02:41:32.201
Once captured, SCP-5007 instances will dart
across the water at a high speed, and take

02:41:32.201 --> 02:41:35.109
their victims to an unknown location.

02:41:35.109 --> 02:41:40.620
Discovering where SCP-5007 took their victims
became a top priority for the Foundation.

02:41:40.620 --> 02:41:45.750
After extensive witness interviews and compiling
a database of likely victims, they determined

02:41:45.750 --> 02:41:51.600
there must be at least 16 instances of SCP-5007
unaccounted for.

02:41:51.600 --> 02:41:55.850
Personnel kept a close watch on the coastlines
and waters of the Bass Strait, and equipped

02:41:55.850 --> 02:42:01.321
various marine task forces with research vessels
capable of tracking any instances if they

02:42:01.321 --> 02:42:02.660
encountered them.

02:42:02.660 --> 02:42:08.439
In 1985, the Foundation’s research efforts
paid off, and several survey teams operating

02:42:08.439 --> 02:42:14.670
in the area reported a sighting of an extremely
large SCP-5007 instance heading towards a

02:42:14.670 --> 02:42:15.979
coastal town.

02:42:15.979 --> 02:42:19.010
A Mobile Task force was sent to track the
entity.

02:42:19.010 --> 02:42:23.430
The team observed the entity from afar as
it stalked a private fishing boat.

02:42:23.430 --> 02:42:27.460
Even from the distance, Foundation personnel
recognized the likenesses of several missing

02:42:27.460 --> 02:42:31.830
persons as faces on the corpses of SCP-5007.

02:42:31.830 --> 02:42:35.950
The Task force captain had to remind his team
to keep it together, claiming that they were

02:42:35.950 --> 02:42:38.930
not people, but just parts of the specimen.

02:42:38.930 --> 02:42:41.240
But everyone secretly knew the truth.

02:42:41.240 --> 02:42:45.350
The fishing vessel was a private one, occupied
by a small family.

02:42:45.350 --> 02:42:49.149
The entity slowly approached, and quickly
pulled a woman into the air.

02:42:49.149 --> 02:42:53.650
The family panicked and quickly tried to reach
cover for safety, running into the ship’s

02:42:53.650 --> 02:42:54.650
cabin.

02:42:54.650 --> 02:42:59.390
The entity ran its tentacles along the boat
until it pulled the door open, snatching another

02:42:59.390 --> 02:43:00.560
two victims.

02:43:00.560 --> 02:43:04.850
The task force was unable to help them, as
their mission was to track the instance to

02:43:04.850 --> 02:43:06.200
its origin point.

02:43:06.200 --> 02:43:09.029
It was a horror to watch.

02:43:09.029 --> 02:43:13.479
The task force implanted a tracking beacon
onto the entity, and quietly followed it out

02:43:13.479 --> 02:43:15.420
to sea over the next four hours.

02:43:15.420 --> 02:43:23.330
They then discovered a large, gray reef, with
several shipwrecks dotted across it.13 SCP-5007

02:43:23.330 --> 02:43:28.101
instances floated over the area, some holding
onto the land-reef with their tentacles.

02:43:28.101 --> 02:43:32.170
The entity dropped the abductees from the
fishing boat, who were coerced by the entities

02:43:32.170 --> 02:43:36.870
into diving into a massive pool of water located
in the center of the reef.

02:43:36.870 --> 02:43:41.649
One by one, each abductee was pulled below
the surface by something lurking inside the

02:43:41.649 --> 02:43:42.649
pool.

02:43:42.649 --> 02:43:46.110
All while the SCP-5007 instances watched.

02:43:46.110 --> 02:43:50.250
Disgusted, the task force reported what they
observed to the main site, and the reef would

02:43:50.250 --> 02:43:54.240
be designated as SCP-5007-A.

02:43:54.240 --> 02:43:58.240
The Foundation’s analysis of the reef led
to the discovery that the rock covering it

02:43:58.240 --> 02:44:03.550
seeped iron oxide from an unknown source,
and the rocks achieved growth at an anomalously

02:44:03.550 --> 02:44:07.200
fast rate, often as little as 40 minutes.

02:44:07.200 --> 02:44:10.990
All of the wrecked ships and aircraft that
washed across the shore of the reef were covered

02:44:10.990 --> 02:44:12.570
with the dark stone.

02:44:12.570 --> 02:44:18.319
The reef was teeming with anomalous marine
life, including SCP-5007, a red algae that

02:44:18.319 --> 02:44:24.040
fed upon the freshly grown rock, marine worms
capable of levitation, spiders that lived

02:44:24.040 --> 02:44:29.560
in silk retreats underneath the waterline,
small fish, and giant organisms resembling

02:44:29.560 --> 02:44:35.550
large clumps of kelp, which the Foundation
had previously documented as SCP-4159 in a

02:44:35.550 --> 02:44:37.370
separate investigation.

02:44:37.370 --> 02:44:42.620
SCP-5007 often rested their tentacles on the
outcroppings of the reef while inactive.

02:44:42.620 --> 02:44:47.560
But what caught the Foundation’s attention
the most was the giant pit located at the

02:44:47.560 --> 02:44:48.649
reef’s center.

02:44:48.649 --> 02:44:53.860
Unmanned exploration drones found that it
had a depth of at least 4000 meters and water

02:44:53.860 --> 02:44:59.439
samples taken from the pit revealed large
quantities of human DNA, prehistoric bacteria,

02:44:59.439 --> 02:45:03.779
and unknown compounds that possessed significant
life-preserving qualities.

02:45:03.779 --> 02:45:08.490
When a being was submerged in the compound,
they were able to survive heavy injuries,

02:45:08.490 --> 02:45:12.109
even when fully surrounded by the liquid and
unable to breathe.

02:45:12.109 --> 02:45:16.029
The Foundation’s exploration of one of the
shipwrecks led them to a journal.

02:45:16.029 --> 02:45:21.370
Most of it was illegible due to water damage,
but one passage survived, located in the back

02:45:21.370 --> 02:45:22.370
of the book.

02:45:22.370 --> 02:45:26.630
It detailed the experience of an unknown crew
member of a ship caught in a storm.

02:45:26.630 --> 02:45:27.630
It reads:

02:45:27.630 --> 02:45:31.529
“Moresby spied land ahead, and the boys
say there are giant balloons hanging over

02:45:31.529 --> 02:45:32.529
the island.

02:45:32.529 --> 02:45:37.061
We are all afeared, but there is naught we
can do but beach ourselves and hope for rescue.

02:45:37.061 --> 02:45:42.050
Should I be killed in the crash, I want my
mates to give this journal to my Mary might

02:45:42.050 --> 02:45:44.870
know I spent my last thinking only of her.”

02:45:44.870 --> 02:45:49.471
The interior of the ship contained human remains
inside, but there were less skeletons than

02:45:49.471 --> 02:45:52.450
the Foundation would expect for a ship of
its size.

02:45:52.450 --> 02:45:55.569
The location of the rest of the bodies was
unknown.

02:45:55.569 --> 02:45:59.850
Another event related to SCP-5007 the Foundation
documented involved

02:45:59.850 --> 02:46:05.420
Frederick Valentich, a pilot engaged in a
training flight over the Bass Strait in 1978.

02:46:05.420 --> 02:46:09.479
Valentich’s disappearance was marked by
his latest communication with air traffic

02:46:09.479 --> 02:46:14.510
control, when he mistook an SCP-5007 instance
for an unidentified aircraft.

02:46:14.510 --> 02:46:15.910
It seems like it's stationary.

02:46:15.910 --> 02:46:20.520
What I'm doing right now is orbiting and the
thing is just orbiting on top of me.

02:46:20.520 --> 02:46:26.050
Also it's got a green light and sort of metallic,
like it's all shiny on the outside.

02:46:26.050 --> 02:46:30.560
Shortly after this, Valentich’s transmission
was interrupted by what was described as metallic,

02:46:30.560 --> 02:46:36.420
scraping sounds, believed to be the SCP-5007
instance attacking the aircraft and jamming

02:46:36.420 --> 02:46:38.620
its propellers with its mass.

02:46:38.620 --> 02:46:42.680
After crashing into the reef, it was believed
that Valentich and his aircraft were pulled

02:46:42.680 --> 02:46:46.899
beneath the surface of the pit, just as the
abductees had been prior.

02:46:46.899 --> 02:46:51.090
The Foundation decided to construct a provisional
secure research facility on the reef.

02:46:51.090 --> 02:46:58.090
They named it Site-40-R, and documented all
returns and departures of SCP-5007.

02:46:58.090 --> 02:47:03.820
They also set up a series of containment procedures
that resulted in SCP-5007 returning with victims

02:47:03.820 --> 02:47:08.340
83% less often then before the site’s construction.

02:47:08.340 --> 02:47:09.950
But this was short lived.

02:47:09.950 --> 02:47:16.359
In 2008, the site logged over thirty six instances
returning to the reef, with only two not having

02:47:16.359 --> 02:47:18.000
any fresh abductees.

02:47:18.000 --> 02:47:23.649
These instances' origins were unknown, and
it was as if they appeared out of thin air.

02:47:23.649 --> 02:47:27.850
No other monitoring post had documented their
appearance, or even spotted them before they

02:47:27.850 --> 02:47:29.420
arrived at the reef.

02:47:29.420 --> 02:47:35.130
It was years later, in 2017, that the Foundation
eventually was able to successfully explore

02:47:35.130 --> 02:47:38.660
what was deep inside the pit at the center
of the reef.

02:47:38.660 --> 02:47:43.340
They already knew there was a large entity
lurking beneath, as evidenced by what happened

02:47:43.340 --> 02:47:48.840
to the victims of SCP-5007 that were deposited
inside the pool.

02:47:48.840 --> 02:47:52.720
All previous attempts to explore the pool
were met with failure, as the water pressure

02:47:52.720 --> 02:47:56.750
of the pit’s depths caused all craft to
collapse due to hull damage.

02:47:56.750 --> 02:48:02.800
This time, however, they managed to construct
a high-tech submarine, labeled the SCPS Nautilus,

02:48:02.800 --> 02:48:07.540
which was capable of diving a maximum of 13,500
meters underwater.

02:48:07.540 --> 02:48:11.830
They decided that a D-Class personnel would
be trained to man the submersible and carry

02:48:11.830 --> 02:48:13.529
out the exploration.

02:48:13.529 --> 02:48:14.880
The mission was simple.

02:48:14.880 --> 02:48:19.310
The Nautilus was to dive to the bottom of
the pit and to describe the depth readings.

02:48:19.310 --> 02:48:21.800
Cameras and a microphone were equipped to
the vessel.

02:48:21.800 --> 02:48:25.190
Due to the depth, remote viewing of this footage
was impossible.

02:48:25.190 --> 02:48:29.689
Instead, the Foundation had to physically
recollect the vessel in order to view the

02:48:29.689 --> 02:48:30.689
footage.

02:48:30.689 --> 02:48:35.000
Upon recovery, some of the footage suffered
data corruption, but what was there shook

02:48:35.000 --> 02:48:37.220
those who viewed it to their core.

02:48:37.220 --> 02:48:41.210
The footage showed the D-Class’s experience
going deeper inside the pit.

02:48:41.210 --> 02:48:43.410
At first, it seemed ordinary.

02:48:43.410 --> 02:48:47.729
The trench had a number of rocky outcroppings,
dotted with black-yellow vines growing along

02:48:47.729 --> 02:48:49.050
the walls.

02:48:49.050 --> 02:48:53.350
Also present were the various marine lifeforms,
such as the spiders or the fish.

02:48:53.350 --> 02:48:58.920
Going deeper, the sub observed an SCP-5007
instance clinging to an outcropping.

02:48:58.920 --> 02:49:03.040
Several tendrils emerging from the pits depths
were wrapped around the instance and holding

02:49:03.040 --> 02:49:06.340
onto the entity, as if it were feeding from
it.

02:49:06.340 --> 02:49:13.729
Another 16 SCP-5007 instances were seen resting
along the walls, each clinging to the outcropping.

02:49:13.729 --> 02:49:19.029
As the sub went deeper, the D-Class remarked
that there were dozens of plane and shipwrecks,

02:49:19.029 --> 02:49:23.780
but also well over a hundred SCP-5007 entities.

02:49:23.780 --> 02:49:26.311
Most of them were held there by the black
tendrils.

02:49:26.311 --> 02:49:31.350
The D-Class, as the sub went even deeper,
began noticing human remains.

02:49:31.350 --> 02:49:33.069
No short amount of them, either.

02:49:33.069 --> 02:49:37.840
Deep into the pit, there was a large mass
of human remains, covering the entirety of

02:49:37.840 --> 02:49:38.850
the pit.

02:49:38.850 --> 02:49:44.350
Bodies crushed and drained of blood, but still
possessing intact eyes.

02:49:44.350 --> 02:49:49.620
Each individual was still alive, kept preserved
by the life-sustaining compounds found within

02:49:49.620 --> 02:49:50.620
the water.

02:49:50.620 --> 02:49:54.900
The bodies stared at the sub and moved, attempting
to grab onto the vehicle.

02:49:54.900 --> 02:49:59.121
The D-Class swore they were trying to say
something, mouthing words to the camera of

02:49:59.121 --> 02:50:00.121
the sub.

02:50:00.121 --> 02:50:05.080
As the sub passed through the mass of bodies,
it emerged into a completely dark, black clearing

02:50:05.080 --> 02:50:06.569
at the bottom of the pit.

02:50:06.569 --> 02:50:08.710
For a second, the D-Class thought he was safe.

02:50:08.710 --> 02:50:14.560
But then, a large black tentacle rapidly emerged
from below and grabbed onto the Nautilus,

02:50:14.560 --> 02:50:17.370
dragging it even further into the depths.

02:50:17.370 --> 02:50:21.280
The D-Class screamed and panicked, but there
was nothing he could do.

02:50:21.280 --> 02:50:25.800
The tentacle possessed large clusters of eyes,
mouths, and human heads seemingly grafted

02:50:25.800 --> 02:50:27.030
onto its mass.

02:50:27.030 --> 02:50:30.350
And then there was another tentacle, and then
another.

02:50:30.350 --> 02:50:33.130
The Nautilus was pulled to the bottom of the
pool.

02:50:33.130 --> 02:50:37.260
The D-Class’s screams were still heard,
even as the picture cut out.

02:50:37.260 --> 02:50:41.700
Sometimes, graphic, body-alerting images of
the tentacle's features were visible on the

02:50:41.700 --> 02:50:44.989
screen, but most of the footage was indecipherable.

02:50:44.989 --> 02:50:49.750
After minutes of distorted, corrupted footage,
the Nautilus was seen again, rapidly ascending

02:50:49.750 --> 02:50:50.750
to the surface.

02:50:50.750 --> 02:50:55.150
Somehow, it had managed to escape the entity
at the bottom of the pit.

02:50:55.150 --> 02:50:59.380
Upon recovery of the craft, it was found that
the Nautilus was covered in a thick, organic

02:50:59.380 --> 02:51:04.540
coating similar to a black slime mold, but
with dozens of eyes growing from it.

02:51:04.540 --> 02:51:10.090
The D-Class inside showed severe psychological
damage and attempted to harm Foundation personnel.

02:51:10.090 --> 02:51:14.450
They were terminated shortly after, due to
being a danger to those around them.

02:51:14.450 --> 02:51:19.420
Following review of the footage, the Nautilus
was to be dismantled and incinerated, alongside

02:51:19.420 --> 02:51:20.970
the remains of the D-Class.

02:51:20.970 --> 02:51:25.490
A reinforced containment seal was fitted over
the pit, with the intention of keeping whatever

02:51:25.490 --> 02:51:27.770
was down there isolated from the surface.

02:51:27.770 --> 02:51:30.590
But this was short lived.

02:51:30.590 --> 02:51:35.939
After the containment seal was fitted, Site-40
underwent a massive communications blackout.

02:51:35.939 --> 02:51:40.490
Every device on the site received an email
containing a single image of a large eye,

02:51:40.490 --> 02:51:42.310
taken from a security camera.

02:51:42.310 --> 02:51:45.780
The text beneath it simply read “FOUND YOU”.

02:51:45.780 --> 02:51:50.850
Some personnel who viewed the email underwent
anomalous changes, growing new physical features,

02:51:50.850 --> 02:51:54.410
such as eyes and other various growths, across
their body.

02:51:54.410 --> 02:51:59.870
The entirety of Site-40-R went offline, and
the Foundation could not establish contact.

02:51:59.870 --> 02:52:05.970
In an emergency effort to do so, Mobile Task
Force Gamma-6, Deep Feeders, was sent to investigate.

02:52:05.970 --> 02:52:10.569
The task force’s assault on Site-40-R was
a daring effort, as the majority of the site

02:52:10.569 --> 02:52:15.030
was completely overtaken by tentacles, growths,
and anomalous alterations.

02:52:15.030 --> 02:52:20.640
While numerous altered personnel were lost
during the mission, it was ultimately a success.

02:52:20.640 --> 02:52:24.439
Some altered personnel were able to be saved
through extensive surgery to remove their

02:52:24.439 --> 02:52:25.950
anomalous growths.

02:52:25.950 --> 02:52:30.290
And after everything was said and done, the
site was repaired and reconstructed without

02:52:30.290 --> 02:52:31.490
incident.

02:52:31.490 --> 02:52:35.090
Following the site’s repair, there has been
little activity from the entity within the

02:52:35.090 --> 02:52:39.920
pit, but the Foundation continues to keep
an eye on the creature and the ecosystem of

02:52:39.920 --> 02:52:44.460
the anomalous marine life that live on the
Bass Strait, never knowing what their next

02:52:44.460 --> 02:52:49.689
move might be, and always keeping in mind
the risk that comes with dealing with these

02:52:49.689 --> 02:52:52.050
poorly-understood entities.

02:52:52.050 --> 02:52:55.540
A lot of us have fond memories of Halloween.

02:52:55.540 --> 02:52:59.580
Dressing up in spooky costumes, wandering
around the neighborhood with friends while

02:52:59.580 --> 02:53:04.320
trick or treating, getting home with literal
buckets full of candy, and then eating so

02:53:04.320 --> 02:53:07.380
many sugary treats that you feel sick.

02:53:07.380 --> 02:53:13.239
Halloween is a beloved holiday, especially
throughout many parts of the United States.

02:53:13.239 --> 02:53:17.290
And if you were lucky enough to grow up in
a town that really went all out when the last

02:53:17.290 --> 02:53:22.600
night of October rolled around, then you may
even have had a local Halloween themed fairground

02:53:22.600 --> 02:53:25.680
to visit on the creepiest night of the year.

02:53:25.680 --> 02:53:30.109
Scary rides, mazes, and jack o’ lanterns
as far as the eye can see.

02:53:30.109 --> 02:53:35.480
But, with all that said, if you lived in a
certain town in the Midwest, then maybe the

02:53:35.480 --> 02:53:40.710
county fair is a little more frightening than
the spirit of the Halloween season usually

02:53:40.710 --> 02:53:42.120
encourages.

02:53:42.120 --> 02:53:51.590
Settle in for a story of scares, a tale of
terror and a fable of frights, this is SCP-097,

02:53:51.590 --> 02:53:54.880
also known as Old Fairgrounds.

02:53:54.880 --> 02:54:00.120
Cordoned off by the SCP Foundation using huge
concrete walls is ten acres of rural land

02:54:00.120 --> 02:54:04.330
in an undisclosed area of the Midwestern United
States.

02:54:04.330 --> 02:54:09.630
The place itself is completely abandoned,
left silent and alone as everything contained

02:54:09.630 --> 02:54:13.320
within those walls slowly falls into disrepair.

02:54:13.320 --> 02:54:19.420
This is all that remains of the local County
Fair, held in the year 1969.

02:54:19.420 --> 02:54:21.030
And right in the middle of it all?

02:54:21.030 --> 02:54:25.101
A pickup truck, crushed and wrecked beyond
all use.

02:54:25.101 --> 02:54:31.030
But this truck didn’t crash, oh no this
was no tragic roadside accident.

02:54:31.030 --> 02:54:34.310
The thing that crushed it happened to be a
gigantic pumpkin.

02:54:34.310 --> 02:54:39.030
Now, we aren’t just talking about a local
vegetable growing competition winner here.

02:54:39.030 --> 02:54:43.979
When we say this is a big pumpkin, we are
talking huge.

02:54:43.979 --> 02:54:49.280
The colossal squash has been recorded to measure
well over seven meters in height, with a diameter

02:54:49.280 --> 02:54:52.739
just over eight meters at the widest point.

02:54:52.739 --> 02:55:00.700
According to estimates, this pumpkin, known
as SCP-097-1, weighs an enormous 15,000 kilograms,

02:55:00.700 --> 02:55:02.109
or 33,070 pounds.

02:55:02.109 --> 02:55:08.390
To give you a frame of reference, that’s
about four times the average weight of a hippopotamus.

02:55:08.390 --> 02:55:13.410
The pumpkin even manages to keep a perfectly
spherical shape, staying plump and round rather

02:55:13.410 --> 02:55:18.260
than spreading out under its own weight, as
you might expect a plant of such size would.

02:55:18.260 --> 02:55:21.840
Okay, a pickup truck crushed by a giant pumpkin?

02:55:21.840 --> 02:55:24.880
You might be wondering, surely that can’t
be all there is?

02:55:24.880 --> 02:55:29.710
Well, don’t you worry, we’re just getting
started with this creep show.

02:55:29.710 --> 02:55:35.830
The rest of the surrounding area of SCP-097
is abundant in overgrown pumpkins, none that

02:55:35.830 --> 02:55:42.960
quite reach the enviable size of SCP-097-1,
but plenty of all different subspecies and

02:55:42.960 --> 02:55:43.960
types.

02:55:43.960 --> 02:55:49.990
On average, these smaller pumpkins weigh around
250 kilograms, or 550 pounds.

02:55:49.990 --> 02:55:55.300
Along with various other crops that have grown
within the area of SCP-097, the pumpkins seem

02:55:55.300 --> 02:55:59.680
to have formed some kind of maze, no pun intended.

02:55:59.680 --> 02:56:04.370
Get it, maize like corn?

02:56:04.370 --> 02:56:06.320
These jokes are wasted on you.

02:56:06.320 --> 02:56:10.980
Spooky mazes are no strange inclusion at rural
Halloween fairs like this one.

02:56:10.980 --> 02:56:15.170
Getting lost in the middle of the night, surrounded
by rows of corn taller than a human being

02:56:15.170 --> 02:56:17.080
is all part of the fun.

02:56:17.080 --> 02:56:20.750
Makes a person feel like they’re right in
the middle of a classic eighties slasher movie,

02:56:20.750 --> 02:56:24.640
where the killer could be creeping up behind
them any second.

02:56:24.640 --> 02:56:29.279
The naturally formed labyrinth found within
SCP-097 has spread all throughout what is

02:56:29.279 --> 02:56:34.750
left of the 1969 county fairgrounds, with
the “walls” of crops reaching over one

02:56:34.750 --> 02:56:38.480
and a half meters tall, depending on the year.

02:56:38.480 --> 02:56:40.210
So, is that all?

02:56:40.210 --> 02:56:43.240
A maze of crops with one giant pumpkin at
its center?

02:56:43.240 --> 02:56:47.710
Oh, that’s far from all there is to SCP-097.

02:56:47.710 --> 02:56:52.149
During the time between April and November
of every year, a number of bizarre and anomalous

02:56:52.149 --> 02:56:57.649
phenomena take place within this abandoned
county fairground, ranging from strange happenings

02:56:57.649 --> 02:57:02.069
that defy explanation, to things that are
downright dangerous.

02:57:02.069 --> 02:57:07.700
Since they first came into contact with SCP-097,
the Foundation have lost eight agents to the

02:57:07.700 --> 02:57:13.050
phenomena that occur within that area, with
a another seventeen being severely maimed.

02:57:13.050 --> 02:57:18.520
While the exact time of these events seems
to vary, the SCP Foundation keeps an extensive

02:57:18.520 --> 02:57:21.540
record of phenomena that occur within SCP-097.

02:57:21.540 --> 02:57:27.069
Now sometimes, these will be as harmless and
annoying as the sound of drums playing throughout

02:57:27.069 --> 02:57:30.550
the day, for almost twenty four hours without
stopping.

02:57:30.550 --> 02:57:34.779
Then, there’s the sightings of entities
moving through the maze only to disappear

02:57:34.779 --> 02:57:37.649
after a few short seconds.

02:57:37.649 --> 02:57:41.440
Security footage the Foundation’s agents
have gathered of these entities depict them

02:57:41.440 --> 02:57:47.109
as what can only be described as “bed sheet
ghosts”, the kind you might see and immediately

02:57:47.109 --> 02:57:51.109
think of as a last minute low budget Halloween
costume.

02:57:51.109 --> 02:57:58.040
On one particular occasion, singing was heard
in the maze, coming from an unidentified source.

02:57:58.040 --> 02:58:02.720
When analyzed, recordings made by the Foundation
revealed there were up to thirty children’s

02:58:02.720 --> 02:58:08.200
voices, all singing in unintelligible gibberish
for three consecutive hours.

02:58:08.200 --> 02:58:13.109
Another incident involved a member of personnel
on site, Agent McRoy, who cut a pumpkin vine

02:58:13.109 --> 02:58:14.700
using a machete.

02:58:14.700 --> 02:58:16.560
Horrifyingly, the severed vine bled.

02:58:16.560 --> 02:58:22.620
By that we mean, actual human blood came pouring
out of the plant.

02:58:22.620 --> 02:58:29.210
Another agent, on a separate occasion, was
also found dead within the SCP-097 maze.

02:58:29.210 --> 02:58:34.100
Agent Long had disappeared on the way to the
restroom, only to be discovered lifeless and

02:58:34.100 --> 02:58:36.750
bloodied, resting against a pumpkin.

02:58:36.750 --> 02:58:42.819
During one weekly examination of SCP-097,
one Agent Cole broke open a pumpkin completely

02:58:42.819 --> 02:58:44.140
by accident.

02:58:44.140 --> 02:58:48.790
As the pumpkin split apart, however, to the
agent’s horror, a child’s skeleton was

02:58:48.790 --> 02:58:51.200
revealed to be inside.

02:58:51.200 --> 02:58:56.830
A human child’s skeleton, a little girl
crouched in the fetal position, believed to

02:58:56.830 --> 02:58:59.899
only have been about five years of age.

02:58:59.899 --> 02:59:05.500
Another incident saw O’Toole, a research
assistant working on site at SCP-097 experiencing

02:59:05.500 --> 02:59:07.080
symptoms of nausea.

02:59:07.080 --> 02:59:13.200
O’Toole also appeared to be vomiting pumpkin
seeds, despite not having eaten any recently.

02:59:13.200 --> 02:59:17.670
Within a day, O’Toole was dead, seeming
to have died overnight in his sleep.

02:59:17.670 --> 02:59:22.170
An autopsy conducted by Foundation experts
revealed that O’Toole’s chest cavity,

02:59:22.170 --> 02:59:27.390
the space beneath his ribs, was somehow filled
with the same pumpkin seeds.

02:59:27.390 --> 02:59:31.460
All of these happenings are strange to say
the least, but perhaps most concerning of

02:59:31.460 --> 02:59:38.080
all is the effect that the abandoned fairground
of SCP-097 seems to have on children.

02:59:38.080 --> 02:59:43.220
Any under or up to the age of ten years old
can fall victim to an unpredictable signal

02:59:43.220 --> 02:59:51.149
that seems to emanate from SCP-097, with a
maximum range that is, as of yet, undetermined.

02:59:51.149 --> 02:59:55.279
Usually beginning in early April, children
that are affected by this signal become afflicted

02:59:55.279 --> 03:00:00.109
with somnambulism, or sleep walking as it
is more commonly known.

03:00:00.109 --> 03:00:04.989
On clear nights, these children will wander
around their own homes, often only stopping

03:00:04.989 --> 03:00:07.420
in front of closed doorways.

03:00:07.420 --> 03:00:13.029
This behavior usually doesn’t happen often,
at least at first, only occurring once a week.

03:00:13.029 --> 03:00:18.000
However, sleep walking gradually becomes more
frequent, and by around the middle of August,

03:00:18.000 --> 03:00:20.021
it will be a nightly occurrence.

03:00:20.021 --> 03:00:24.280
If children with this affliction are ever
woken up while sleepwalking, they will scream

03:00:24.280 --> 03:00:27.450
for several seconds, before appearing confused.

03:00:27.450 --> 03:00:31.490
This seems to be the only known way to break
the influence of SCP-097.

03:00:31.490 --> 03:00:37.450
However, if left undisturbed, a child will
spend their sleep walking episodes familiarizing

03:00:37.450 --> 03:00:40.279
themselves with the doorways of their house.

03:00:40.279 --> 03:00:45.500
They will stop at every entrance, exit, garage
door, gate, even the neighbors’ front doors

03:00:45.500 --> 03:00:47.600
once they find a way outside.

03:00:47.600 --> 03:00:52.410
From September, the sleepwalking children
will stay outside, upright but asleep until

03:00:52.410 --> 03:00:54.060
the sun comes up.

03:00:54.060 --> 03:00:57.990
Many are often found laying on the grass in
their gardens, and commonly recall having

03:00:57.990 --> 03:01:01.149
dreams about autumn-season activities.

03:01:01.149 --> 03:01:05.830
Between September first and November first,
any affected child not awoken during their

03:01:05.830 --> 03:01:11.030
sleepwalking will begin to migrate towards
SCP-097’s location.

03:01:11.030 --> 03:01:16.080
All while still unconscious, they will traverse
country roads, cutting across large empty

03:01:16.080 --> 03:01:21.710
fields, as they gradually make their way towards
the abandoned remains of the county fairground.

03:01:21.710 --> 03:01:26.100
Once there, they will even be able to blindly
navigate a path through the maze that surrounds

03:01:26.100 --> 03:01:30.990
most of SCP-097, until they find the center.

03:01:30.990 --> 03:01:33.770
What happens when they make it to the center
of the maze?

03:01:33.770 --> 03:01:39.720
Any sleepwalking children who are able to
make it that far will seek out SCP-097-1,

03:01:39.720 --> 03:01:44.700
the gigantic pumpkin crushing the truck in
the middle of the SCP-097 area.

03:01:44.700 --> 03:01:49.800
The children will then sit down around the
almost 23 foot tall pumpkin, and begin to

03:01:49.800 --> 03:01:50.800
sing.

03:01:50.800 --> 03:01:55.189
Even though the SCP Foundation have managed
to make recordings of this, much of the singing

03:01:55.189 --> 03:02:00.029
seems to be gibberish, or at least not sung
in any known language.

03:02:00.029 --> 03:02:04.899
However, music will also begin playing from
an unknown source, seeming to include a number

03:02:04.899 --> 03:02:09.560
of basic instruments, most commonly simple
drums and pipes.

03:02:09.560 --> 03:02:13.430
After the sleepwalking children have spent
a number of minutes singing like this, that

03:02:13.430 --> 03:02:18.850
is when things take a turn for the far, far
worse, like a Charlie Brown Halloween special

03:02:18.850 --> 03:02:22.120
straight out of your most horrific nightmares.

03:02:22.120 --> 03:02:27.970
From the tangled mess of plants that make
up the maze within SCP-097, things will start

03:02:27.970 --> 03:02:29.460
to emerge.

03:02:29.460 --> 03:02:33.790
These entities will crawl out of the surrounding
flora, or will come bursting out from within

03:02:33.790 --> 03:02:36.399
the larger of the nearby pumpkins.

03:02:36.399 --> 03:02:41.080
They appear to be childlike in both their
appearance and mannerisms, some even wearing

03:02:41.080 --> 03:02:43.710
pajamas or similar clothing.

03:02:43.710 --> 03:02:44.710
Why?

03:02:44.710 --> 03:02:48.229
Simple, because these are the children that
sleep walked before.

03:02:48.229 --> 03:02:53.569
They are all previous victims, the ones stolen
from their families and brought into this

03:02:53.569 --> 03:02:54.569
maze.

03:02:54.569 --> 03:02:58.439
Still wearing the clothes that they were last
seen in; they are all the children known to

03:02:58.439 --> 03:03:01.630
be lost to SCP-097.

03:03:01.630 --> 03:03:04.220
What happens next is truly chilling.

03:03:04.220 --> 03:03:08.120
The latest child that has been affected by
the draw of the pumpkin-filled fairground

03:03:08.120 --> 03:03:11.681
will be quickly surrounded by all their fellow
victims.

03:03:11.681 --> 03:03:17.800
The other children, if they are in fact still
human children, will encircle the newest child,

03:03:17.800 --> 03:03:20.790
singing and dancing around them in a circle.

03:03:20.790 --> 03:03:27.840
As they do this, a dim light begins to glow
from somewhere within SCP-097-1, the biggest

03:03:27.840 --> 03:03:30.729
pumpkin in the center of SCP-097.

03:03:30.729 --> 03:03:36.200
Finally, at this point in the process, the
newly affected child will wake up.

03:03:36.200 --> 03:03:40.359
Normally, they experience a great deal of
terror and confusion.

03:03:40.359 --> 03:03:44.760
After all, they have been unconscious throughout
this entire ordeal, sleepwalking far away

03:03:44.760 --> 03:03:49.320
from the safety of their own home to a maze
in the middle of nowhere.

03:03:49.320 --> 03:03:54.620
Terror is a powerful thing, enough to make
even the bravest person let out a scream.

03:03:54.620 --> 03:04:00.239
But the moment the now awakened child lets
out any sound, that is when they are doomed.

03:04:00.239 --> 03:04:05.570
Should they scream, cry or make any form of
vocal noise, then the others will swarm them.

03:04:05.570 --> 03:04:11.120
The other children, the ones previously lured
into SCP-097 while sleep walking, will attack

03:04:11.120 --> 03:04:13.000
the terrified newcomer.

03:04:13.000 --> 03:04:18.029
Each time is different, sometimes they will
claw at the new child, other times they might

03:04:18.029 --> 03:04:19.340
bite or kick.

03:04:19.340 --> 03:04:23.490
The methods are always different, but most
often this swarm of the pumpkin’s previous

03:04:23.490 --> 03:04:28.580
victims will strangle or dismember the latest
visitor to the abandoned fairground.

03:04:28.580 --> 03:04:32.450
At this point, there is no saving the latest
victim.

03:04:32.450 --> 03:04:37.750
Any attempt to interfere will only fail, either
the children will all become intangible, or

03:04:37.750 --> 03:04:43.620
another violent phenomenon will occur within
SCP-097, stopping any onlooker from saving

03:04:43.620 --> 03:04:45.230
the child’s life.

03:04:45.230 --> 03:04:49.800
When the deed is finally done, and the latest
victim has been killed by the other children,

03:04:49.800 --> 03:04:53.960
the gigantic pumpkin at the heart of SCP-097
will open.

03:04:53.960 --> 03:04:58.689
Its side will split like a pair of great,
devouring jaws, and the children will throw

03:04:58.689 --> 03:05:03.399
the body of the newest child into SCP-097-1.

03:05:03.399 --> 03:05:07.960
Once the body has been disposed of, these
entities, once children that sleep walked

03:05:07.960 --> 03:05:12.921
away from their families, will follow, crawling
into the pumpkin before it closes and the

03:05:12.921 --> 03:05:15.210
music finally stops.

03:05:15.210 --> 03:05:19.239
The exact number of children between the ages
of three and ten years of age who have been

03:05:19.239 --> 03:05:23.820
lost to SCP-097 is currently kept secret by
the Foundation.

03:05:23.820 --> 03:05:28.540
And perhaps, for all of our sanities, that
is for the best.

03:05:28.540 --> 03:05:32.350
Like we said, a lot of us have fond memories
